window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS=(window.GALLERY_CHAPTERS||[]).concat([{"title":"Chapter 35","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (2)","In the Gallery, the term armband usually referred to either the Moderator or an Assistant Moderator.","They were administrators granted the authority to manage the Gallery.","That made it sound as though they were expected to work hard at managing it, but that wasn’t actually true.","It was perfectly acceptable for the Moderator to manage the Gallery carelessly.","Everyone had their own circumstances, after all.","In such cases, the Moderator could appoint an assistant manager—an Assistant Moderator—and share some of their authority.","***","Title: What’s Good About Being an Assistant Moderator?","Genuinely asking.","You can delete Gallery posts and ban users.","And?","That’s it lol.","Then why would anyone become one?","Exactly. That’s why nobody does.","If you manage the Gallery like shit, you can get fired too lol.","Isn’t that also true for the Moderator?","The Moderator is fine as long as they occasionally log in. Assistant Moderators don’t even get that privilege lol.","That’s basically how serfdom started lol.","Fuck, talking about group projects reminds me of the academy. Being a commoner was miserable.","These days, nobles are practically forced to become group leaders. Apparently, nobles are supposed to set an example lol.","Society has finally improved.","The problem was that the rewards were pitiful compared to the authority granted.","It was practically unpaid volunteer work.","That was why users tried their hardest to avoid being appointed as an Assistant Moderator.","Even when they disliked the Moderator, a single question—","Do you want to turn blue?","—was enough to silence them.","***","Title: This Moderator Really Doesn’t Appoint Any Assistants","Isn’t managing everything alone exhausting?","Yeah, that’s why everyone keeps telling them to appoint an Assistant Moderator—as long as it isn’t them lol.","Infinite selfishness at its finest lol.","Would you want to be an Assistant Moderator?","I’d do it if they paid me lol.","Basically, Assistant Moderator equals group-project leader. Understand now?","An Assistant Moderator was a necessary position that nobody wanted for themselves but desperately wanted someone else to take.","The authority to delete Gallery posts and ban users?","Even that wasn’t much.","No reward came with doing the job well.","***","Title: This Reminds Me of the Old Days","Remember when the Moderator and Assistant Moderator met up in real life to fight and both died?","Oh, I remember that lol. It was fucking hilarious.","The surprising part was that one of them was a noble lol.","Why did they fight?","I think the Assistant Moderator demanded the Moderator’s armband. Said they did all the work while the Moderator did nothing.","Fair reason.","So the Moderator said they’d hand it over if the Assistant Moderator won the fight lol.","And then they both died lol.","***","Title: What Authority Does the Moderator Have?","Everything an Assistant Moderator has, but better. They can also make trades whenever they want. I think they can have private one-on-one conversations too.","Can’t they track users’ locations as well?","Yeah. Someone once threatened to attack the Emperor, and the Moderator revealed their location so they could be executed. I think the Moderator even received a reward.","That’s a dangerously powerful ability.","That’s why one Moderator stalked some noble lady, had his eyes gouged out, and got thrown in prison lol.","It really was dangerous lol.","The Moderator’s authority, on the other hand, was extremely powerful.","They weren’t restricted by the rule preventing another trade for twenty-four hours after completing one, and they could interfere with various systems.","As a result, the atmosphere and direction of the Gallery largely depended on whoever held the Moderator position at the time.","The current Moderator, Don’t Abandon the Hero , was somewhat scatterbrained but principled and generally righteous.","To put it less kindly, he was stubborn and old-fashioned.","Fortunately, he possessed at least a little flexibility.","For some reason, however, he would occasionally disappear for long periods, causing the Gallery to descend into chaos.","An Assistant Moderator was needed precisely for situations like that, yet he had never appointed one.","***","Title: Why Won’t the Moderator Give Anyone an Armband?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I can handle all the difficult work myself! Assistant Moderators don’t even get paid!","Doesn’t the Moderator also work for free?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I receive transaction fees! I’m using them to improve the Gallery!","What exactly does \"improving the Gallery\" mean?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I should be able to add minigames soon!","Moderators really do have all kinds of interesting abilities. So you’re still not appointing an Assistant Moderator?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: You’re right above me at the moment!","I’m not even a registered user lol.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I can use the transaction fees to purchase the authority to appoint someone by force!","I’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorryI’m sorry.","LMAOOOOOO.","***","Title: How Does Someone Become the Moderator?","If the Moderator appoints Assistant Moderators, then who appoints the Moderator?","According to previous Moderators, it just happened one day. They suddenly received a notice saying they’d become the manager of the Continental Integrated Gallery.","So it’s completely random?","Yeah.","Then how does someone else become Moderator?","When the current Moderator doesn’t access the Gallery for a long time. Or when they die.","I’m pretty sure getting imprisoned also strips you of the armband.","One needed either an extraordinarily strong mentality or an absurd amount of free time and boredom.","As it happened, someone who satisfied those conditions had appeared.","There had always been interest in the armband, but nobody clearly understood how it worked.","Even the current Moderator had admitted that he didn’t fully understand the Gallery’s systems, which said everything.","Most authority in the Gallery was concentrated in the Moderator’s hands, while Assistant Moderators were practically slaves.","Who would willingly become both the leader of a group project and a serf under a feudal system?","It was a thankless position where doing well earned nothing and doing poorly invited endless abuse.","Anyone who genuinely wanted the role had to be one of two things.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Are you really certain?! I can handle all the difficult work alone!","Heavenly Demon: This Queen has already decided. However, only if you accept my condition. Are you not busy yourself? You do not seem to have visited the Gallery often lately.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ve shaken off my pursuers, so I’m fine for now! And if I accept that condition, everyone else will criticize you!","Heavenly Demon: Do not worry. This Queen does not care.","It was a conversation between the Moderator, Don’t Abandon the Hero, and the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","Yu Sowol waited patiently for the Moderator to continue.","On the surface, it looked like they were negotiating a trade.","In reality, it was something similar.","The only difference was that this was not a transaction chat window, but a private one-on-one conversation.","The Moderator possessed every restricted authority.","Therefore, if the Moderator initiated the request, a private conversation became possible.","To make that happen, the Heavenly Demon had repeatedly sent him trade requests.","She had done it so often that even the Moderator could no longer ignore her.","Heavenly Demon: Rather than hiding it, I intend to reveal it openly. It is better to endure the criticism sooner rather than later.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I see! I understand what you mean!","Heavenly Demon: Then, will you grant me the armband?","If she slowly investigated this authority, she was certain to find some kind of opening.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Very well! I’ll give you the armband! However, if you abuse your power, I will revoke it immediately!","Heavenly Demon: Do not concern yourself. This Queen shall govern with great tolerance. Besides, are private conversations not visible to you as well?","Yu Sowol waited in anticipation.","Would the Moderator truly grant her the armband?","She had two goals.","The first was to have private one-on-one conversations with Grylls.","Every time she left a comment, some fly-like wench named SwordMaster would swarm in, so she had decided that speaking privately would be better.","Her second goal was to understand the Gallery’s structure more clearly.","An Assistant Moderator possessed less authority than the Moderator, but it still had some privileges.","Every private conversation in the Gallery was visible to the Moderator.","Normally, this referred to trade conversations between registered users, but the Heavenly Demon was about to receive administrative authority.","That meant the profound cultivation verses of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art might also be exposed to the Moderator.","However, she wasn’t particularly worried about that.","The Moderator has already seen them once.","The Moderator even possessed the privilege of reading private posts.","There were no secrets one could hide from the Moderator.","In that case, it was better to speak openly through private conversations instead.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: That’s right! It’s unavoidable, even if only to prevent crimes! Is that a problem?!","Heavenly Demon: It matters not. In exchange, I shall grant you the honor of contemplating the profound meaning of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’m fine! I already have a blessing from the Goddess!","When their conversation ended, a blue badge appeared beside the Heavenly Demon’s username.","The moment she received it, she checked Grylls’s post first.","Something seemed to have happened while she was persuading the Moderator.","The Heavenly Demon smiled in anticipation and left a comment.","Besides, nobody would believe her anyway.","Yu Sowol knew exactly how people regarded her in the Gallery.","She was a famous registered user who posted nonsense or shitposts every single day.","The important part was that those seemingly meaningless posts actually contained the enlightenment of the Heavenly Demon.","Nobody believed that.","The Moderator was no exception.","Yu Sowol had already taken that into account.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I look forward to working with you, Assistant Moderator!","Heavenly Demon: Likewise.","Heavenly Demon: Ah. I nearly forgot. From now on, you may address me as the Assistant Moderator.","Why all of a sudden?","What the hell happened?","We’re fucked. They gave the armband to someone with nothing but free time. ;;","EMERGENCYYYYY!","Excellent reactions appeared one after another.","Everyone seemed utterly shocked that Yu Sowol had become an Assistant Moderator.","This feels strangely satisfying.","Yu Sowol’s chin lifted slightly.","Look at them trembling in fear.","Normally, they treated her like some outdated martial-arts old-timer.","But look at them now.","The moment she obtained great power—the blue badge—the Gallery users began quaking in terror.","In reality, the Heavenly Demon Yu Sowol could wipe out entire groups with a single gesture.","Yet receiving this sort of treatment in the Gallery made her strangely happy.","It felt as though she had stepped out of the shell of the Heavenly Demon and obtained power and authority as an ordinary human being.","This was why she couldn’t quit the Gallery.","For Yu Sowol, whose days had once been endlessly dull, it was an enormous source of stimulation.","I should proudly announce my emergence.","In the martial world, it was customary to openly declare one’s name and origin when making an entrance.","The Gallery was no different.","She happily announced her emergence.","However, she restrained her arrogant tone as much as possible.","She might otherwise upset the Moderator.","***","Title: Hear Me, My Subjects","Heavenly Demon","By the grace of the Moderator, this Queen has received the armband.","However, merely possessing the armband does not mean I intend to oppress you like an emperor.","I shall only ban those for justified reasons, so you need not worry.","Ask whatever you wish. For today alone, I shall graciously permit it.","She really got the armband? The world is ending. ;;","Why did the Moderator give it to that old fossil?","Isn’t she going to ban anyone she dislikes?","The Moderator wouldn’t have appointed her if she were like that.","Should we start begging for mercy now?","SwordMaster: Why did you become an Assistant Moderator? I don’t understand.","She could ignore the other comments, but not SwordMaster’s.","Yu Sowol began writing a response, then quietly deleted it.","An amusing idea had occurred to her.","After thinking for a while, she smiled and replied.","Heavenly Demon: You may ponder that question yourself.","SwordMaster: ??? You told us to ask questions. ;;","Heavenly Demon: I said I would answer. I never said I would give you the answer you wanted.","SwordMaster: Are you messing with me right now?","Heavenly Demon: This Queen is entirely serious.","SwordMaster: I already want to impeach you. ;;","That was something she could worry about when the time came.","She possessed time in abundance, like the vast sea.","There was no shortage whatsoever.","Then the Heavenly Demon noticed another comment.","What color are your panties today?","\"Hehe.\"","This was the experience she had been waiting for.","Yu Sowol let out a faint laugh.","Truthfully, she wanted to inflict heavenly punishment—meaning a permanent ban—upon SwordMaster.","That registered user was constantly filling her benefactor’s head with strange ideas.","But she endured it.","With mercy as vast as the heavens, she refrained from delivering divine punishment.","The initiative was now hers anyway.","There was no longer any need to concern herself with SwordMaster.","Unless that woman also receives a blue badge.","The urge to deliver heavenly punishment surged again.","But who was she?","\"Hehe.\"","Yu Sowol forgave her with boundless generosity.","Compared to the others, that comment was relatively mild.","This place truly is overflowing with idiots.","Once again, she realized just how extraordinary the Gallery was.","***","The news that the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator spread throughout the entire Gallery.","With the blue badge displayed prominently beside her username, it was impossible not to notice.","To make matters worse, she had even created a post, and the comment section was overflowing.","The problem was that a considerable number of those comments were idiotic.","Questions about the color of her panties were practically mandatory.","That was normal everyday behavior in the Gallery, but the appearance of a new Assistant Moderator seemed to attract even more people than usual.","She must be lonely in her old age.","Judging by all the strange posts she regularly made, that seemed likely.","I’d heard that old people tended to spend their days reminiscing about the past.","Otherwise, there was no explaining how she managed to attract so much attention.","Or maybe she’s starved for attention.","In that case, I should treat her with a little more courtesy from now on."]},{"title":"Chapter 36","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (3)","The news that the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator spread like wildfire.","She had already been a well-known registered user, so it was only natural that the Gallery would erupt into an uproar.","An Assistant Moderator might be an inferior version of the Moderator, but they were still a manager.","Anyone who broke the rules or angered the Heavenly Demon now faced a high chance of being banned.","The Heavenly Demon probably won’t do that, though.","She had a strong tendency to follow her own path.","No matter what anyone said, she simply continued forward without wavering.","You could call it a mentality of steel.","Or perhaps it was the tolerance that came with old age.","To genuinely anger the Heavenly Demon, someone would probably have to hurl insults too vile to repeat.","And if someone did that, they couldn’t complain about getting banned.","In any case, from my perspective, it was little more than an ordinary incident.","The Heavenly Demon becoming an Assistant Moderator probably wouldn’t change much.","It simply meant that the Gallery had gained another manager.","Since I was acquainted with her, I might receive a few minor conveniences.","Not that I intend to rely on her.","If I depended too heavily on the Heavenly Demon, I would inevitably grow lazy.","I was already receiving plenty of help.","Rather than clinging to her, it was better to become stronger on my own.","Now that she’s an Assistant Moderator, she’ll probably be busy.","Assistant Moderators were essentially volunteers.","Unpaid slaves.","Yet if they neglected their duties, they could lose the position and even get banned.","The Moderator was especially rigid and placed great importance on rules and principles, so she couldn’t afford to be careless.","\"I should focus on my own work.\"","I had escaped from the muscular mushroom, and the Heavenly Demon had become an Assistant Moderator, but I still had things to do.","I needed to receive the barricades from Passing Dwarf and reinforce my shelter.","He had said he would send them around lunchtime, so the trade request should arrive soon.","After I finish installing the barricades...","Just as I began thinking about what to do afterward—","Passing Dwarf has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?","A trade request arrived from the dwarf.","Apparently, speaking of the devil really did summon him.","I accepted.","Passing Dwarf: You accepted immediately. Guess you’ve got some free time?","Wild Grylls: I was waiting for you.","Passing Dwarf: Ah, sorry. I’m into women. It’s hard being this popular.","Wild Grylls: You lunatic lol. Did you finish the barricades?","Passing Dwarf: I did, but there are a lot of them, and they’re big. Do you have somewhere to store them?","At his question, I looked around.","Perhaps because the Mad Dog pack had once lived here, the area surrounding the cave was surprisingly spacious.","The interior was large as well.","Three enormous beasts had once lived inside it, after all.","If necessary, I could store some of the barricades inside the cave after installing a few outside.","I admired the photos the dwarf sent.","One showed an ordinary wooden defensive wall.","It consisted of sharpened wooden posts placed tightly beside one another.","The other was closer to a barricade.","A wall and a barricade were technically similar, but their shapes were different.","The wall stood vertically, while the barricade leaned at an angle.","It consisted of pointed wooden stakes arranged diagonally and tightly bound together.","Wild Grylls: I have space. About how big are they?","Passing Dwarf: Look at these first.","Passing Dwarf: (Photo of a wooden wall.)","(Second photo of a wooden barricade.)","Passing Dwarf: Which one looks better?","\"Oh?\"","Passing Dwarf: You’re not planning to live there permanently. If you only need something temporary, the spikes are probably better. They’re easier to install too.","Wild Grylls: Those do look better. I dug all those fucking holes for nothing lol.","Passing Dwarf: Just bury them roughly. I’ll make the rest in this style.","Wild Grylls: How long will it take to make more?","Passing Dwarf: What I’ve already sent should provide decent protection. If that’s not enough, make some yourself. They’re easy as long as you know how to tie rope.","Wild Grylls: I’ll think about it. Can you send these now?","Passing Dwarf: Yep.","Passing Dwarf has registered the trade items.","Passing Dwarf: Take them.","Wild Grylls: Is there anything you need?","Passing Dwarf: Just give me booze lol.","Wild Grylls: Can’t give you alcohol, but I’ll find you something to eat with it. Fish okay?","Passing Dwarf: Not bad. Don’t you need a fish trap to catch them?","Wild Grylls: It’d be useful, but the fish are so huge that I think it’d be difficult.","Passing Dwarf: I’ll make one. You’d better give me the food. Deal?","Wild Grylls: Deal.","The items the dwarf had sent arrived as soon as the trade ended.","I had assumed the barricades wouldn’t be very tall.","I was wrong.","Even when placed diagonally, they stood slightly taller than I did.","If anything, building them this way must have required even more effort.","They’re bigger than I expected.","There was no time to stand around in surprise.","More barricades would arrive shortly.","Fortunately, the delay between each delivery allowed me to position them one at a time.","Their size probably caused them to take longer to transfer.","Or perhaps there wasn’t enough open space for them to appear all at once.","\"Whew.\"","After some time, I finished placing and adjusting everything.","I didn’t know exactly how the system determined where traded items would appear, so the process was somewhat awkward, but no accidents occurred.","There’s no inventory system or anything like that, is there?","Large deliveries like these would probably cause trouble every time.","It would be convenient if there were a separate space where traded items could be stored temporarily.","***","Title: Work Finished!","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the shelter with the barricades installed.)","Finally finished installing the barricades. I still have more to do, but this feels satisfying.","By the way, isn’t there some kind of space for temporarily storing traded items? They kept appearing out of nowhere, and positioning them was a pain.","Good work. That feature actually used to exist, but it’s restricted now.","Wild Grylls: Why was it restricted?","Smuggling. People used to complain that the system handled things like the military, but then the Moderator from two generations ago ruined an entire territory with it, so the feature was blocked.","Isn’t that restriction meaningless for the Moderator? They can do whatever they want.","Yeah. The Moderator could remove the restriction. But do you really think the current one would?","Wild Grylls: Couldn’t they allow storage for just ten minutes? That would be enough.","There are people who hide drugs up their asses to transport them. Like hell the Moderator will approve that lol.","They might make an exception for you, Grylls. But is there even a system for removing restrictions for only one registered user?","No. Maybe for an Assistant Moderator. And even then, you’d have to suck up to the Moderator lol.","One thing’s certain: the current Moderator is an old-fashioned hard-ass, so he won’t allow it.","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’m not old-fashioned! I merely value rules and principles! Calling someone old-fashioned just because they uphold order is the other person’s fault! The technical term for that is antisocial behavior!","The Moderator’s here?","Moderator, why not remove the restriction, then? You can decide now, can’t you?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: I’ve actually been considering it! I’ll review the matter positively, so please wait! Now, if you’ll excuse me!","He was reviewing it positively.","Perhaps there was reason to hope.","Even being able to store items for five minutes would help.","Although I had arranged the barricades, they were still scattered around somewhat messily.","No. I’m asking for too much. What am I thinking?","I quickly shook my head.","This wasn’t good.","I had resolved to reduce my dependence on the Gallery, yet here I was becoming annoyed by a minor inconvenience.","Its functionality was truly like a drug.","No wonder people couldn’t stop using the Gallery.","I could only grow by overcoming difficulties myself.","I renewed my resolve.","First, I should inspect the barricades properly.","Someday, I might have to build barricades by myself.","Perhaps something would happen to the dwarf, or I might lose access to the Gallery.","I needed to understand the structure of the barricades in preparation for that possibility.","He carved grooves into the wood and fitted the stakes into them. Then he secured everything tightly with rope, just in case.","When I had some free time, it might be a good idea to practice by making a small barricade.","There were trees everywhere, so I would never run out of materials.","The only thing lacking would be my craftsmanship.","Whatever I made would probably be far inferior to the dwarf’s work.","Aren’t dwarves supposed to be short? He made all of this by himself?","The dwarf’s physique suddenly came to mind.","The barricades stood slightly taller than I did.","It was surprising that a dwarf had built defensive structures this tall all by himself.","He constantly pestered me for alcohol, but perhaps Passing Dwarf was actually someone important.","\"Kyuu.\"","\"Are you hungry?\"","Wonmo approached and looked up at me with his bright, round eyes.","While I was installing the barricades, lunchtime had arrived before I knew it.","There was no fish left, so I would probably have to settle for a fasting pill today.","I gave Wonmo a large piece of meat that I had bought through the Gallery.","His eyes sparkled, and he immediately began devouring it.","I also need to learn how to set traps.","The problem was whether ordinary animals would fall for ordinary traps.","The only small animals I had seen so far were squirrels and rabbits.","Even those were considerably larger than normal.","The rabbits were about the size of medium-sized dogs.","They were also incredibly fast, fleeing the instant they sensed my presence.","Then I’ll just make the traps bigger.","It was a simple but effective solution.","Instead of setting a trap for a rabbit, I could build one as though I were trying to catch a wild boar.","While chewing on the bitter fasting pill, I glanced behind me.","I had felt something climbing onto my back, and sure enough, it was the Swift Sloth.","\"Do you want one too?\"","\"...\"","It nodded at its usual painfully slow pace.","I handed it a fasting pill and browsed the Gallery.","After taking a brief rest, I planned to circulate the cultivation method.","Heavenly Demon has requested a private conversation! Would you like to accept?","\"Huh?\"","A message caught my eye while I was browsing.","The Heavenly Demon hadn’t sent me a trade request.","She had requested a private one-on-one conversation.","As far as I knew, ordinary users and even registered users couldn’t use private conversations.","Apparently, the feature had been restricted to prevent cliques from forming.","So why could the Heavenly Demon use it?","Is it different for an Assistant Moderator?","I had my doubts, but I couldn’t exactly reject a request from the Heavenly Demon.","I accepted.","A window similar to the trade interface appeared.","Heavenly Demon: Benefactor, can you see my message?","Wild Grylls: Hello. I can see it clearly. Can Assistant Moderators use private conversations?","Heavenly Demon: Normally, they cannot. However, I persuaded the armband holder to grant me this authority. I must be the one to initiate the conversation, though.","Wild Grylls: I see. How are you finding the Assistant Moderator job?","Heavenly Demon: There are many images that please the eye. However, those with shallow enlightenment like yourself would fall prey to inner demons upon seeing them.","I roughly understood what she meant.","The last time I had wandered in without knowing anything, I had been thoroughly blinded by what I saw.","But the Heavenly Demon was a true Gallery addict among Gallery addicts.","She would easily brush such things aside.","In a way, she possessed all the qualities of an excellent Assistant Moderator.","She had plenty of free time, was immune to inner demons, and possessed a rock-solid mentality.","From the Moderator’s perspective, appointing her had probably seemed like a good idea.","Wild Grylls: Sounds like you’re having a hard time. Is there no time limit on private conversations?","Heavenly Demon: There is none. However, the entire conversation will be visible to the Moderator. That does not concern me. What I intend to teach you is only the foundation.","Wild Grylls: The foundation? Didn’t you already teach me everything? You said I’d even opened something called the upper dantian.","Heavenly Demon: That is true. However, the problem is that you opened it far too quickly. Without a proper foundation, one will inevitably become unstable. Even a bridgehead that appears sturdy will eventually collapse if it was built carelessly.","The language was clearly related to martial arts, yet strangely enough, I understood it.","The part about shoddy construction especially resonated with me.","This must have been what people called wisdom.","She was an excellent teacher.","Wild Grylls: That makes perfect sense. You’re saying my body could collapse because it was built carelessly, right?","Heavenly Demon: Correct. From now on, I intend to teach you the fundamentals. No matter how sturdy the stem may be, it will quickly wither if its roots are weak.","Wild Grylls: Thank you. I’m just not sure I’ll be able to understand everything.","Heavenly Demon: Do not worry. I shall explain it in terms you can understand. First, sit in the lotus position.","I followed her instructions and sat cross-legged.","Perhaps because I had grown accustomed to it, the posture no longer hurt.","It actually felt refreshing.","Later, I should practice other positions as well.","There was no downside to becoming more flexible.","Heavenly Demon: Good. However, I would prefer that you call it internal energy rather than mana. It is not necessarily incorrect, but hearing you call it mana bothers me for some reason.","So it bothers her.","She must have taken tremendous pride in internal-energy cultivation.","Well, she was an old woman who had experienced everything the world had to offer, so her pride was understandable.","It was something I ought to respect.","I would have to be more careful from now on.","Heavenly Demon: Ah, there is one thing I wish to ask. What did it feel like when you circulated the cultivation method? Did you feel any obstruction at the crown of your head?","Wild Grylls: Not at all. It just felt like the energy traveled throughout my entire body and completed a full circuit.","Heavenly Demon: Then it seems you truly have opened the Gate of Life and Death. Your internal energy appears to flow freely through the Governing and Conception Vessels.","I had no idea what any of that meant.","Still, I could tell she was impressed.","Wild Grylls: That’s a good thing, right?","Heavenly Demon: It is exceedingly good. In terms of cultivation, you have reached the late stage of the Peak Realm. However, your advancement was far too abrupt, so you likely cannot even manifest sword energy properly.","Wild Grylls: Sword energy? You mean putting mana into a sword?","Heavenly Demon: Internal energy.","Wild Grylls: I’ll be careful. Anyway, I can’t do it. This is the first time I’ve heard of it.","Heavenly Demon: You would likely struggle not only to manifest sword energy, but even to reinforce your own body. That is precisely why the fundamentals are important.","Wild Grylls: I see. Understood.","Heavenly Demon: Therefore, understanding the route will make matters easier. Read carefully. When circulating your cultivation method, the internal energy flows through the lower dantian, the perineum, the coccyx...","The Heavenly Demon’s lesson continued.","At considerable length.","I could only stare blankly with my mouth hanging open.","I didn’t understand a single word.","It felt like I had started with the basics of one plus one, only for her to suddenly throw calculus at me.","The Heavenly Demon’s intensive tutoring continued.","Heavenly Demon: If this is too difficult, I can show you through a drawing.","Wild Grylls: Can you do that?","Heavenly Demon: (A rough diagram of the circulation route.) How is it? Can you see it clearly?","I could certainly see it.","It was roughly a side view of a human body with the internal circulation route drawn inside.","What language is this?","The problem was that I couldn’t understand any of the writing.","At least the route itself was illustrated, so I could more or less guess where it went.","Is this really going to be okay?","It was far too difficult.","Meanwhile—","SwordMaster: Moderator, you traded with the Heavenly Demon, didn’t you?","Don’t Abandon the Hero: Huh?!"]},{"title":"Chapter 37","paragraphs":["Assistant Moderator (4)","At present, SwordMaster—Ash—is what people would call an unemployed bum who gets smacked on the back by her mother practically every day.","An unemployed bum who spends all day browsing the gallery and snickers whenever something amusing happens.","However, she was someone who had, strictly speaking, experienced \"working life.\"","And not just ordinary working life, but life in the political world, where conspiracies, schemes, and power struggles were everyday occurrences.","Since ancient times, politics had gradually developed as a means of keeping overwhelming power in check.","Ash, in particular, had been nothing more than a commoner until the Emperor bestowed a title upon her.","Until then, she had worked hard at navigating society so she would not find herself in politically troublesome situations—watching the moods of nobles, flattering them, agreeing with them, and so on.","In truth, marriage would have been the easiest option, but because Ash was simply too strong, every attempt had fallen through.","And after she became captain of the Imperial Guard, there was no longer much room for political problems to arise around her anyway.","In any case, Ash had experience with society—and, more specifically, with the dark and murky world of politics.","That was why the Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod set off a few alarm bells in her head.","She definitely made some kind of deal. There’s no way that old fossil would’ve become a sub-mod otherwise. Same goes for the head mod.","The instant Ash heard that the Heavenly Demon had become a sub-mod, she started thinking.","Unlike certain people, she actually had experience dealing with society.","She grasped the situation faster than anyone else.","What kind of deal did she make?","Ash had been a regular fixture in the gallery for a long time. In terms of seniority alone, she had been around for nearly ten years.","Unlike the previous head mod, the current head mod placed great importance on principles and rules.","On top of that, they had such a strong self-sacrificing streak that they would never force the sub-mod position onto somebody else.","For someone like that to appoint a sub-mod—and a well-known fixed-nickname user at that—meant there had to be something behind it.","The Heavenly Demon was probably the one who proposed the deal first...","In truth, the Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod was not much of a problem for Ash.","What if the Heavenly Demon started abusing her authority however she pleased?","Her privileges would be stripped immediately, and she would probably be banned for several weeks.","The Heavenly Demon knew that as well, so on the surface, she seemed to be diligently doing her job.","But Ash tried to discern the intention hidden beneath it.","Why had the Heavenly Demon decided to become a sub-mod at this particular moment?","The timing is way too convenient.","Ash had clashed with the Heavenly Demon quite a few times recently.","They had bickered over whether mana cultivation was better or whether an internal energy cultivation method was superior.","Though, to be fair, it had been closer to Ash picking fights one-sidedly, so Grylls had sided with the Heavenly Demon.","Ash was aware of how embarrassing her own behavior had been, so she limited herself to giving advice and stopped interfering beyond that.","Still, what a waste...","That did not mean she intended to give up easily.","It was simply too much of a waste. It had been a long time since she had seen someone with that much potential.","Ash had once trained countless disciples.","Of course, the reason had been the thoroughly impure intention of finding someone suitable to marry, but that was beside the point.","Regardless, she was confident in her ability to judge people.","All of those disciples had eventually fallen for other women and gotten married, but Grylls was different.","As she had said before, his life might constantly be in danger, but at least there was no need to worry about him getting distracted by women.","Even the ones I personally trained weren’t this exceptional. I have to teach him somehow.","Whenever she looked at Grylls, Ash felt as though she were looking at her past self.","A constitution that accumulated mana simply by breathing.","Because of his unusual environment, Grylls accumulated mana just by breathing.","And for mana to circulate throughout the entire body was ordinarily something that should only become possible after reaching the intermediate level of Sword Expert.","But I really don’t want to become a sub-mod.","Even so, becoming a sub-mod herself was something she absolutely wanted to avoid.","It was not as if the gallery was free of politics.","If anything, it was full of something even worse than politics: \"gallery politics.\"","And what was the difference?","Gallery politics consisted of agitation, fabrication, trolling, and finally, infighting.","Sub-mods, in particular, attracted far more attention than ordinary fixed-nickname users.","Just look at the Heavenly Demon.","The moment she became a sub-mod, she was subjected to all sorts of attacks.","She had managed to brush them all off thanks to her uniquely domineering personality.","Besides, mental fortitude was not an issue for Ash.","She simply hated it.","Ash just hated being a sub-mod!","Whatever the case, that makes me the latecomer.","In the end, Ash could only let out a small laugh.","The Heavenly Demon had put her in a perfect bind.","Who could have predicted she would become a sub-mod?","Still, Ash could not suppress her curiosity.","She wanted to know what had possessed the head mod to place the Heavenly Demon in that position.","I should find out.","The method for contacting the head mod was extremely simple.","All she had to do was send a trade request.","Only fixed-nickname users could send trade requests anyway, so the head mod usually accepted them.","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: Hello! What can I do for you?!]","The moment the request was accepted, the head mod greeted her energetically.","Ash smiled at the head mod, who never seemed to lose that energy, and spoke.","[SwordMaster: Head mod. You made a deal with the Heavenly Demon, didn’t you?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: W-What?!]","Despite her smile, Ash’s question went straight for the throat.","The head mod must have been thoroughly flustered, considering the bizarre response.","The head mod Ash knew was terrible at lying.","That remained true even in a gallery where anonymity was the norm.","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: How did you know?! Did the sub-mod tell you?!]","[SwordMaster: No. I just figured something like that had probably happened and took a shot in the dark. Then you confessed. So, what kind of deal did you make?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: She asked me to make one-on-one conversations possible!]","[SwordMaster: Oh.]","So that was it.","What a greedy woman.","Ash nodded at the head mod’s painfully honest answer.","Thanks to that, she was able to piece together the whole story.","As expected, the Heavenly Demon had become a sub-mod for Grylls.","But couldn’t she just use private posts? That seems way too simplistic.","Yet one question still remained unanswered.","What was the point of private posts, then?","Ash wanted to know the reason.","[SwordMaster: Aren’t one-on-one conversations still visible to you, head mod?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: Yes! I’m watching right now too!]","[SwordMaster: What are they talking about? The internal energy cultivation method?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I can’t tell you the details, but I can answer \"yes\" to that!]","That much was within her expectations.","But she still did not understand.","The reward was far too small compared to the responsibilities that came with being a sub-mod.","Then again, was the Heavenly Demon the sort of person who would recklessly abuse authority?","No.","The Heavenly Demon was the type to say what she wanted to say and nothing more.","She was not easily swayed by other people’s opinions.","If anything, she was similar to the head mod in that she was not the type to become tyrannical simply because something displeased her.","And with the head mod still above her, she did not even have the conditions necessary for that.","Suspicious. Way too suspicious. What is she actually after?","Ash’s thoughts grew longer.","It was difficult to figure out the Heavenly Demon’s intentions.","Still, the conversation had not been entirely fruitless.","Ash nodded and thanked the head mod.","[SwordMaster: Thank you, head mod. Is there anything you want in return?]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I don’t need a bribe! If you want to become a sub-mod, you can just tell me!]","[SwordMaster: No, I’m fine without being a sub-mod. That’s not why I contacted you. I was just curious about why she was acting like that.]","[Don’tAbandonTheHero: I see! Understood!]","Their conversation ended there.","Ash slowly organized her thoughts.","It doesn’t seem like she has any political motive.","Given the Heavenly Demon’s personality, she almost certainly had no political intentions.","Becoming a sub-mod was probably partly to make it easier to help Grylls, while also serving some other purpose.","Ash did not know what that purpose was, but at the very least, it was unlikely to harm her.","Was I worrying for nothing?","The Heavenly Demon becoming a sub-mod was a massive issue in and of itself.","Especially since Ash had even gotten into a war of nerves with her recently.","There was no way she could simply ignore it.","This is complicated. Really complicated.","Maybe she was overcomplicating things.","She had never abandoned the idea of helping Grylls, after all.","She could simply step in quietly whenever he ran into trouble.","Internal energy cultivation methods contain a lot of terms that are difficult to understand unless you’re from the Central Plains. He’ll definitely make a post saying it’s too hard.","That would be her chance to give him tips on mana cultivation.","Since mana cultivation methods were specialized for training others, there were plenty of useful tricks she could teach him.","She just had to wait for the right timing.","Ash focused on the gallery.","She refreshed the page once every ten seconds, waiting for Grylls to make a post.","[Internal energy cultivation is way too hard.]","There it is!","Before long, Grylls made a post.","And the title was exactly what Ash wanted to see.","A post complaining about how difficult internal energy cultivation was.","She immediately opened it.","Title: Internal energy cultivation is way too hard","Wild Grylls","I’m learning an internal energy cultivation method from the Heavenly Demon, but there are so many words I don’t know that it’s really hard.","She says this is just the basics, but if even the basics are like this, I’m scared of what the advanced stuff will be like ;;","└ The Heavenly Demon taught you? How? She didn’t even make a post.","└ Wild Grylls) She requested a one-on-one chat with me?","└ Sub-mods can do that too? The head mod allowed it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. She said the head mod gave permission. Also said she didn’t care if people knew.","└ Wow ;; look at that special treatment. I’m already getting jealous.","└ Lmao, makes me want to start trolling.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) If you want, I can appoint you as a sub-mod too!","└ That threat doesn’t work anymore lol. We figured out anonymous users can’t become mods.","└ Anonymous users can’t do it anyway lol.","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Then I’ll come find you in person and threaten you!","└ Sorrysorrysorrysorrysorry","└ Damn, when the head mod says that it actually sounds scary lmaoooo.","└ Reminds me of when the head mod used to stalk people back in the day lol.","└ Police? Open up?","└ SwordMaster) Which part are you having trouble with?","└ Wild Grylls) It’s hard to understand the route. The Heavenly Demon even showed me a diagram while explaining it, but maybe I’m just too dumb because I still can’t get it.","└ SwordMaster) I understand what you mean. I can help you with that.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you.","Ash stared at the post, unable to hide her sense of emptiness.","She had gone so far as to initiate a trade with the head mod just to figure out what was going on, yet the person involved had simply revealed everything himself.","It made all the effort she had put in feel pointless.","Then again, perhaps that was just like the Heavenly Demon.","...I should just teach him some tips.","Still, there was work to be done.","Ash pulled herself together.","Then she started typing comments so she could pass on various useful tricks.","She smiled when Grylls thanked her so politely.","Unlike internal energy cultivation, mana cultivation was a breathing method specialized for training others.","It was perfect for teaching the fundamentals in painstaking detail.","But why isn’t the Heavenly Demon interrupting me?","Normally, she should have butted in by now.","Yet there was not even a glimpse of her.","Just what was she plotting?","Ash remained suspicious as she continued typing.","└ SwordMaster) Mana cultivation and internal energy cultivation may have different branches, but they share the same roots. Start with your breathing first.","└ Wild Grylls) I already am.","└ SwordMaster) While maintaining that state, send the energy in your lower abdomen toward the perineum. You know where the perineum is, right?","└ Wild Grylls) More or less?","└ SwordMaster) \"More or less\" isn’t enough. Since you’re a man, Grylls, just think of it as the area between your testicles and your anus. Send the energy there and you should feel something.","└ Wild Grylls) Hmm... yeah. I can feel it. It’s itchy though. Can I scratch it a little?","Could this be why the Heavenly Demon did it too?","Her reasonable suspicion steadily grew.","***","This was strangely frustrating.","Ash furrowed her elegant brows.","It was not because Grylls was having trouble understanding.","Nor was it because she had to cram so much text into the narrow comment section...","└ Teach us too~","└ Why are you keeping all the good tips to yourselves?","└ SwordMaster, I’ve hit a wall in my cultivation recently. Could you help me too?","└ Unlocktheprivatecommentsunlocktheprivatecommentsunlocktheprivatecomments","The jackals had smelled something sweet and come running.","They were getting in the way of her concentration.","They kept invading Grylls’s comment section, making it harder for her to teach him properly.","Meanwhile, at that very moment, in the Demonic Cult—","I can feel her frustration from here.","Yu Sowol smiled as she read SwordMaster’s private comments.","The moment she had been given a moderator badge, she had gained the authority to view private comments as well.","It was only natural.","That meant Yu Sowol could also see all the useful tips SwordMaster was passing on.","Calling these \"tips\" is somewhat generous.","SwordMaster’s advice could barely even be called advice.","Because it was no different from what Yu Sowol had already taught him.","This problem stemmed from SwordMaster—Ash—being far too talented herself.","Unlike swordsmanship, which she had built up from the very bottom, she had possessed a constitution that accumulated mana merely by breathing.","She might have been exceptional at swordsmanship, but she had very little talent when it came to teaching breathing methods.","I suppose it only works because the benefactor’s potential is exceptional.","Still, geniuses had ways of understanding other geniuses.","Grylls gradually absorbed what SwordMaster considered \"useful tips.\"","Even though Yu Sowol herself had dismissed the method, Grylls devoured it eagerly.","SwordMaster. As expected, this person is extraordinary as well.","But it did not matter.","Yu Sowol shifted her gaze.","Where she looked, the message window containing the conversation she had just exchanged with Grylls was still open.","Unlike trades, one-on-one conversations allowed them to communicate in real time.","The entire conversation history remained as well, meaning she could review it whenever she pleased.","For fruit to grow, the roots must first be strong.","What Yu Sowol wanted was simple.","For Grylls to fully understand every insight of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art and eventually bear fruit.","She planned to use SwordMaster’s advice to strengthen his weak foundations.","In the end, people are always more interested in sweet fruit than in the roots beneath it.","Even if Grylls received SwordMaster’s advice, the foundation itself remained the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","That had not changed.","Eventually, he would realize the greatness of the Heavenly Demon Divine Art, and his respect for her would naturally grow.","SwordMaster was merely an assistant.","The one who would ultimately pass everything on to him was the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol.","It is only proper that I do this for my benefactor.","Now it was time to fulfill her duties as a sub-mod.","Yu Sowol turned her attention back to the board.","But even then, she did not yet realize—","└ Wild Grylls) Oh? It worked? My sword is glowing!","└ SwordMaster) Holy shit. Seriously? How did you do that?","└ Wild Grylls) Why are you asking me that? ;;","└ SwordMaster) I’m more amazed that you actually do everything I tell you just from hearing it ;;","When the roots changed, the branches growing from them were bound to change little by little as well.","Especially because SwordMaster’s true specialty was not breathing techniques—","but swordsmanship itself.","└ SwordMaster) With a little more practice, you might be able to stop carrying a shield and just use a sword. But seriously, how did you do that?","└ Wild Grylls) I told you, I don’t know either ;;","Very slowly, it was beginning to seep into him."]},{"title":"Chapter 38","paragraphs":["Fireball (1)","Would you believe me if I said a strange haze started rising from a sword?","It was the sort of phenomenon you would expect to see in fantasy or martial arts fiction, so even I had a hard time believing it.","According to SwordMaster, once you got the feel for it, it was actually very easy.","But apparently, I was the first person she’d ever seen who managed to release energy immediately after hearing a few tips.","SwordMaster herself said it had taken her around an hour just to get the hang of it.","Of course, maybe that was because her advice was packed with all the know-how she had accumulated over the years.","Title: Is this really aura?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a sword with a shimmering haze rising from it)","I did what SwordMaster told me to do. Is this really aura?","Asking because it worked way too easily.","└ SwordMaster) That really is aura ;; I thought maybe, but you actually did it.","└ Wild Grylls) That’s a good thing, right?","└ Stop humblebragging. It’s pissing me off.","└ Some people take months and this guy does it in one day lmao.","└ Months, my ass. It took me three years, damn it lol.","└ How the hell did SwordMaster teach him? Tell me too.","└ Wild Grylls) She just told me to reproduce the sensation I feel when circulating mana, then imagine letting that mana flow into the sword. So I did exactly that.","└ Ha ;; I can’t decide what’s more ridiculous, someone explaining it like that or someone actually succeeding from that explanation.","└ Fuck, if you could emit aura from an explanation like that, every random idiot would be using it lmaooo.","└ Starlight Princess) Wow. That’s amazing. If you compared it to a mage, what Circle would that be?","└ For a mage, it’d be like starting at the 3rd Circle immediately.","└ Starlight Princess) I see. So it really is impressive, right?","└ What Circle did you start at, then?","└ Starlight Princess) The 5th Circle. I could have started higher under normal circumstances, but my illness prevented me from doing so.","└ This one’s flexing too lmaooo.","└ That’s basically like saying you started with an Aura Blade lol.","└ It’s not an Aura Blade. It’s Sword Force.","└ Same damn thing, asshole. Do you really have to nitpick?","└ Pride.","└ Wild Grylls) Anyway, if I think of compressing this stuff, that makes it an Aura Blade, right? Lol, I’ll practice.","└ SwordMaster) Practicing is good, but maintaining the sensation is more important. Sometimes people forget it.","└ Wild Grylls) You can forget it?","└ SwordMaster) It works on the same principle as consciously thinking about your breathing.","The comment section exploded the moment I showed them the aura.","Maybe the Heavenly Demon was busy carrying out her duties as a sub-mod, because she did not leave a comment.","Well, now that she could have one-on-one conversations, I figured she would just message me directly if she had anything to say.","Is this really that impressive?","I stared closely at the sword with the shimmering haze rising from it.","I could definitely feel mana leaving my body.","But since it replenished every time I breathed, it did not feel particularly significant.","SwordMaster told me to compress it as tightly as possible, right?","She had advised me to keep practicing until the haze took on a sharp, defined form.","From that point onward, she said it entered the realm of talent, so there was only so much she could do for me.","Even so, SwordMaster said she would help me as much as she could.","Feels like I’m only ever receiving things from her...","I wanted to give SwordMaster something in return for all the useful tips she kept teaching me.","But she was the kind of person who had even refused rare medicinal herbs because she did not want to become healthier.","Then what could I give her that she would willingly accept?","Would she take something material, as long as it was not an herb?","This is difficult.","SwordMaster was especially troublesome compared to the Heavenly Demon.","I did not like continuing to receive things without giving anything back.","She claimed that all she wanted was for me to marry her, but that was obviously a joke.","Besides, I did not even know whether I would ever be able to leave this place.","For now, should I test this out?","Instead of the Heavenly Demon’s sword, I brought out an ordinary logging axe.","Wonmo was taking a nap, while Tree Sloth was riding on my back.","There was no better way to test the performance of aura—or sword energy—than chopping wood.","How many swings did this usually take?","I recalled the sensation of channeling mana into the sword.","First, I had to become aware of the mana stored in my dantian.","SwordMaster had told me to think of the mana stored in my lower abdomen as a kind of reservoir.","All I had to do was draw mana from that reservoir and send it into my weapon.","She said that once the mana in the reservoir runs dry, I’d need to circulate the cultivation method to refill it...","SwordMaster said she had never once suffered from a mana shortage in her entire life.","Because mana accumulated in her body every time she breathed, it apparently functioned almost like a perpetual-motion machine.","She said that given my environment, I might eventually become similar, but I had no idea whether that would really happen.","I should keep circulating the internal energy cultivation method consistently.","I let mana flow into the axe.","A faint haze began rising from it.","In the Central Plains, this energy was called sword energy.","In other countries, it was called aura.","Apparently, with this energy, you could produce several times the power of an ordinary person.","\"Hup!\"","Then just how powerful was it?","I swung the axe with all my strength.","The target was a thick tree trunk.","It was a tree that had taken several axe swings to bring down just yesterday.","Crack!","The axe blade sank deeply into the trunk—","and kept going.","It did not slice through it like tofu, but the entire center of the tree was torn apart.","Crrraack!","With its trunk practically shattered, the enormous tree began toppling over on its own.","It leaned farther and farther until—","THUD!","—it crashed to the ground with a deafening noise.","Good thing I had been chopping from the side opposite the cave.","Otherwise, I might have destroyed the barricade the dwarf had gone through all that trouble to give me.","It doesn’t cut. It explodes.","I carefully examined the fallen tree trunk.","I knew the weapon’s destructive power would increase, but I had not expected it to be this extreme.","According to SwordMaster, the shimmering haze was simply evidence of mana leaking out.","She had specifically mentioned that the fundamental nature of the weapon itself did not change.","Considering the characteristics of an axe, I guess it makes sense.","An axe was a weapon specialized more for smashing than cutting.","So it made sense that the tree trunk had been ripped apart rather than neatly sliced through.","If I had put the same energy into a sword, I probably could have cut through it like tofu.","...Could I really?","The moment that thought occurred to me, I went back into the cave and brought out the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","To test it, I placed the sword against a tree trunk without channeling any mana into it.","Before, I had never even tried this because I was worried I might chip the blade.","But I was not trying to saw through the tree with a sword.","I only wanted to check whether the blade could cut into the trunk as a basic performance test.","Sssshk—","\"Huh?\"","My eyes widened.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword sank deep into the tree with only the slightest bit of force.","Then it slid smoothly through the trunk as though there were hardly any resistance at all.","Rumble—","I was so busy staring at the Heavenly Demon’s sword that I barely cared about the tree falling over.","I knew it was a good weapon, but I had never expected it to be this ridiculous.","What kind of absurdly broken item is this?","With a sword like this, there was barely any need to emit aura in the first place.","Of course, I had absolutely no intention of using the Heavenly Demon’s sword for logging.","If I accidentally chipped the blade, that would be a disaster.","She just gave me a sword like this without hesitation?","My respect for the Heavenly Demon shot upward.","At the same time, I started to worry.","Hadn’t she given me something far too valuable?","Part of me wanted to return it immediately, but the Heavenly Demon would probably refuse.","If I find a good sword later, I’ll return this one to her.","This sword was simply too excessive.","It was something that ought to go back to its owner someday.","I put all but one of the fallen trees up on the auction house.","Since I was already there, I checked the price of the inner core I had listed that morning.","[Inner Core: 500 taels of silver]","\"Whoa.\"","The price just kept climbing.","I stared at the current bid in admiration.","Five hundred taels of silver converted to 5,000 gold.","The owlbear corpse had sold for 250 taels, so this was already twice as much.","It seemed the price had risen this high because the Heavenly Demon herself had vouched that it was an inner core.","What if it turns out to be fake after all?","Would I have to refund the money?","I had no idea.","Still, with the Heavenly Demon backing me up, the buyer probably would not be able to make a fuss.","And even if they did, there should not be a problem as long as the Heavenly Demon testified for me.","Let’s see. What time is it...?","I opened the gallery and checked the time.","More than an hour had flown by while I practiced the cultivation method and aura.","It was currently 1:30 in the afternoon.","There was still plenty of time before sunset.","Should I try making some traps?","It seemed like a good idea.","I could improve my handiwork and get some meat at the same time.","As for how to make traps, I could find everything I needed just by searching the gallery.","Adventurers occasionally uploaded guides on making hunting traps.","Some of them had even made it into the recommended-post section, so I should be able to make one without much trouble.","The problem is the area where the small animals live...","I knew where little animals like rabbits tended to pass through.","The problem was that Muscle Mushroom was located in that direction.","It should be fine as long as I did not provoke it, but there was no guarantee.","It might still be awake and wandering around nearby.","For safety’s sake, it would be better to eliminate Muscle Mushroom first.","There was a cave there too, so I can check that out while I’m at it.","Decision made.","I would deal with Muscle Mushroom first.","Its individual attacks were powerful, but it was slow.","And since I had heard that it was weak against fire, defeating it should not be too difficult.","Wait, did they actually say it was weak against fire? They said fire was essential because of those spores or whatever.","It looked like I would have to hold a sword in one hand and a torch in the other.","I remembered the golden shield that had been crushed by a single Beng Quan punch.","If I took a direct hit from something like that, there was a good chance there would not even be enough of my bones left to collect.","So fighting from a distance would be better.","It didn’t look like arrows would work, though.","Even ants had clearly distinguishable heads, thoraxes, and abdomens.","Muscle Mushroom was different.","Aside from its arms and legs, its body was long and narrow like a branch.","It was essentially closer to a plant, which meant I would probably have to either smash it apart or burn it.","...They said magic exists too, right?","Something suddenly occurred to me.","Magic.","The iconic power that appeared in practically every fantasy story.","It was supposedly an ability only geniuses were qualified to learn.","Maybe I could learn just a little?","If I could use magic, it would be useful in all sorts of ways.","Not just for ranged attacks, but for everyday survival as well.","The moment the thought occurred to me, I immediately opened the gallery.","Title: Is magic easy to learn?","Wild Grylls","I just want to learn some simple fire or water magic. Is it difficult?","└ Heavenly Demon) Ahem. One must devote oneself to a single path in order to achieve greatness. Are you already allowing your mind to wander elsewhere?","└ SwordMaster) The sub-mod is right. Even I gave up on magic almost immediately because of how difficult it is, so don’t even try.","└ Guess he has no idea how many aspiring mages there are in the gallery lol.","└ Grylls, you’re going to get yourself in serious trouble messing with that. Don’t do it.","└ Seriously, we’re only telling you this because we’re nice.","Everyone reacted negatively.","Even the Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster.","I could not understand why they were all so against it.","└ Wild Grylls) Didn’t you say elves and demons can use magic just fine?","└ Their starting point is high enough that they can usually reach the 3rd Circle. Going beyond that is difficult.","└ Didn’t you say you were human, Grylls?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah. I was just curious.","└ Magic is difficult enough to make even demons and elves grind their teeth. In terms of theory, they’re actually worse than humans.","└ Wild Grylls) Why?","└ Do you carefully analyze the theory behind how you breathe? Humans just happen to be unusually curious. Other races usually aren’t.","└ Wild Grylls) Oh. Got it.","└ Princess Chaenggu) But our Mephisto is still better when it comes to magic! You can tell just by looking at broadcast magic!","└ Demonic-race utility magic really is impressive. Life has gotten way more comfortable thanks to them lol.","└ Praise the demon who invented air-conditioning magic!","└ What’s air-conditioning magic?","└ Air conditioning.","└ Oh lmao, yeah, that deserves praise.","└ Refrigeration magic for me lol. I get to drink cold alcohol every day now.","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Elves are inventing all kinds of magic too!","└ What kinds of magic are they inventing?","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Communication and reconnaissance magic, as well as explosive magic!","└ Whoa, shit ;; that sounds scary as hell.","└ Are those bastards seriously not preparing to start a war?","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Don’t worry. Elves love peace.","└ Wild Grylls) How is that any different from \"If you want peace, prepare for war\"? ;;","└ Let’sGrowTrees) Ooooh! That’s a wonderful saying. I’ll take it to heart.","└ Wild Grylls) What?","There seemed to be someone seriously wrong in the head, but it would probably be fine.","Anyway, magic appeared to be used in all sorts of fields.","It was quite literally magic replacing science.","No.","In this world, perhaps magic itself was science.","└ Starlight Princess) Are you trying to learn magic? I can help you.","└ Wild Grylls) Aren’t you busy exercising?","└ Starlight Princess) Other than the time I spend exercising, I’m pretty free. Forgive me for asking, but you do know arithmetic, right?","└ Wild Grylls) I graduated high school ;;","Was she looking down on me too much?","Or maybe there were simply a lot of people in this world who could not even do basic arithmetic.","Given the era, there was no reason to expect anything like universal public education.","Then again, they did have academies, so perhaps she was accounting for people from underdeveloped regions.","└ Starlight Princess) \"Graduated high school\"? I don’t know what that means, but I assume it means you can do arithmetic. Good. Then you should be able to express fire mathematically.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? Express what mathematically?","└ Starlight Princess) Fire. You formulate it mathematically. It’s very easy. It works like this—","As Starlight Princess continued explaining, all I could do was stare with my mouth hanging open.","There were plenty of symbols.","There were just no numbers.","My knowledge of mathematics had reset itself the instant the college entrance exam ended.","And since I had been a humanities student on top of that, I understood absolutely none of it.","└ Starlight Princess) Well? Do you understand?","└ Wild Grylls) That’s the basics?","└ Starlight Princess) Yes. You learn this before even entering the academy.","└ Anyone else feel like their head is going to explode just looking at that?","└ Me first lol.","└ Ah lmao, you don’t need this crap to live normally.","Were all the mages in this world Newton or Einstein?","Then again, scientists on Earth were geniuses compared to ordinary people too.","I decided to cleanly give up on learning magic.","└ Wild Grylls) Uh... I’ll just give up. Starlight Princess, do you find math easy?","└ Starlight Princess) I love mathematics. You can express everything in the world through mathematics, can’t you? Someday, I’m going to express the Forest of Four Seasons mathematically too.","└ Wild Grylls) You don’t have calculators here, right?","└ Starlight Princess) Why would I need a calculator? I can just calculate it in my head.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;","└ God, that’s obnoxious lmao.","└ You’d be surprised how many people like that actually exist.","└ Their entire thought process is different from ours.","Yeah.","I should give up on magic completely.","If I kept entertaining pointless hope, I was only going to hurt myself.","Still, I should thank Starlight Princess for offering to help.","Seeing how disappointed she seemed made me feel a little guilty.","In the end, I guess I’ll have to solve this physically.","Was there really no other way?","I looked around the cave.","Then one particular object caught my eye.","Something I had left untouched until now.","That’s it!","It was the alcohol the dwarf had given me as a gift."]},{"title":"Chapter 39","paragraphs":["Fireball (2)","There was a saying: if you had no teeth, you made do with your gums.","In other words, if the best option was unavailable, you came up with the next best thing.","Since my best option—magic—was gone, I needed to settle for an alternative too.","It was technically magic.","Just... magic with a little physics mixed in.","Similar to a Fireball, but slightly different in nature.","Pop!","I struggled to pull out the cork that had been wedged deep inside the bottle.","Fortunately, the dwarf had given me an opener along with the alcohol, so I was able to get it out.","\"Ugh...!\"","The instant I uncorked it, I couldn’t help but grimace.","I had no idea how to describe the sensation.","It felt like the overpowering smell of alcohol was beating my sense of smell into submission.","Like a hired thug barging in and forcibly driving every other scent out of the place.","\"Grragh!\"","Even Tree Sloth, who was clinging to my back, recoiled in horror.","The little guy barely ever made a sound, yet even he was clutching his nose.","That alone showed how vicious the smell was.","He gave me this to drink? This is basically poison.","I was seriously curious about the alcohol content.","It had to be absurdly high.","At this level, I could probably mix in just a little oil and still get what I wanted.","Should I at least taste it once?","Still, it seemed like a waste to throw it away without trying it, so I decided to take a single sip.","Even if I got drunk, it shouldn’t be a problem.","I had an internal energy cultivation method now.","I vaguely remembered hearing that circulating a cultivation method could sober you up.","I stared at the alcohol, which was still reeking like pure ethanol, then quietly brought the bottle to my lips.","Gulp.","Surprisingly, the first thing I tasted was sweetness.","There was the characteristic bitterness of alcohol too, but the sweet aroma was much stronger.","This is actually pretty good.","At this level, I could drink it like a beverage.","That was what I thought.","For exactly two seconds.","\"HUARGH! UUUUAGH!\"","Something was wrong.","I had clearly swallowed a liquid, so why did it feel like my throat was on fire?","Had I swallowed flames?","No, forget flames. Had I just swallowed hydrochloric acid?","I clutched my throat in agony.","And then I realized the truth.","That dwarf bastard had finally gone and poisoned me!","Right after that realization came the distinct sensation that my life was in danger.","I couldn’t die like this.","I started feeling around the floor for an elixir, but before long, the pain gradually began to subside.","If it hadn’t, I genuinely would have used up one of my elixirs.","That was how bad it hurt.","\"Ugh...\"","I rubbed my still-stinging throat.","Tears had formed in the corners of my eyes.","I had no idea what the hell that dwarf had given me, but it wasn’t alcohol.","It was poison in liquid form.","Otherwise, there was no reason my throat should hurt like I had suddenly developed severe acid reflux.","And I wasn’t even exaggerating.","I felt like drinking actual hydrochloric acid couldn’t possibly hurt this much.","It’s not like the dwarf is crazy enough to actually give me poison.","So they really drank this stuff as alcohol?","My respect for dwarves rose dramatically.","I sighed and stepped outside for a moment to drink some water.","After drinking from the hose, the burning pain finally eased.","I feel like this would catch fire even without oil.","There was probably no need to fill the whole thing with oil.","Muscle Mushroom was still a mushroom in the end, so it should burn fairly well.","If I filled the bottle entirely with oil and the fire spread, I’d be in trouble.","Let’s check whether this stuff ignites first.","I went back into the cave and poured a little alcohol onto the ground.","Then I picked up a random twig and touched an ignition stone to it.","The dry branch caught fire easily.","It might have been dangerous to put the ignition stone directly against the alcohol, so precautions like this were necessary.","Whoosh!","\"Oh.\"","The moment I brought the flame close, the alcohol flared up.","Apparently, with an alcohol content that high, it ignited extremely well too.","In that case, there shouldn’t be any problem throwing the bottle as-is.","Come to think of it, the bottle’s glass too. Perfect.","Now that I’d confirmed it worked, all that remained was making the actual weapon.","Making a Molotov cocktail was simple, yet surprisingly tricky.","If I screwed up, I could end up setting myself on fire.","Its destructive power wasn’t something to underestimate either.","I had heard they were useful enough to be used against tanks in wartime.","First, I need oil.","I planned to mix oil and alcohol in suitable proportions.","Like I said before, filling the whole bottle with nothing but oil could cause all sorts of problems.","At the very least, I needed to be able to put the fire out relatively easily.","And I’ll add sand too.","Sticky oil and sand.","Just hearing the combination made it sound perfect.","I bought vegetable oil from the auction house.","Apparently, people sold that there.","As for sand, I just gathered some from around the area, dried it, and poured it in.","The last and most important part was the wick.","That was the part I wasn’t completely sure about.","If it burns too fast, I’m the one in danger.","It needed to burn slowly enough while still catching fire easily.","Considering all of that, cloth seemed like the best choice.","Still, I needed to test it.","I bought wastepaper, old newspapers, cloth, and various other flammable materials from the auction house.","As expected, cloth is the safest.","After testing them, cloth turned out to be the most suitable.","I immediately stuffed a strip of cloth into the mouth of the bottle.","Even using a chopstick to force it in took some effort.","Finally, I turned the bottle upside down to check whether any liquid leaked out.","The cloth was thick, so there didn’t seem to be any problem.","Title: Learned Fireball.","(Photo of a hastily made Molotov cocktail)","From now on, call me a fire mage.","└ Passing Dwarf) ??? Isn’t that the alcohol I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, yeah. That shit’s insanely strong lmao.","└ Passing Dwarf) Don’t tell me you threw it away without even drinking it.","└ Wild Grylls) Nah, I took one sip. Thought I was gonna die lol.","└ Passing Dwarf) Assassination successful.","└ Wild Grylls) Are you insane? lmao. You call that alcohol? I’d rather drink rubbing alcohol.","└ Passing Dwarf) It’s still pretty expensive stuff lol.","└ Why’d you make a Molotov cocktail? What are you planning to do with it?","└ Wild Grylls) Gonna kill that mushroom man. If its whole body catches fire, won’t the spores burn too?","└ That’s certainly the straightforward method. Didn’t expect you to make a Molotov cocktail though ;;","└ Wild Grylls) How do people normally kill them? With mages?","└ Just throw a bottle of oil and then toss a torch. That’s safer.","└ Grylls is alone, though, so this probably works better for him.","└ Mage (Physical) lmaoooo.","└ Starlight Princess) Fireball is really easy... It’s not difficult at all.","└ Wild Grylls) Teacher?","└ Starlight Princess) It’s nothing. I’m just a little disappointed. It’s incredibly satisfying to understand the principles of magic one by one.","└ Is this magic (mathematics)?","└ Magic is basically advanced mathematics to begin with.","└ What did you mix into it? Did you add oil?","└ Wild Grylls) About half oil. The rest is alcohol and sand. I’d be screwed if the fire spread somewhere else.","└ You’re not seriously planning to put it out with water after burning everything, right?","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll smother it with sand. I’m not that stupid.","└ You know your stuff, huh? I was about to report you for arson lol.","└ Wild Grylls) Go ahead and report me. That’d be great for me lmao.","└ Allfather) You should be careful once the mushroom man catches fire. It will explode the moment it releases its spores.","└ Wild Grylls) I’ll be careful. Are its spores especially weak to fire?","└ Allfather) They are weak to it, but it’s also instinct. Spreading offspring when one’s life is in danger is an instinct shared by living creatures.","└ Wild Grylls) Thanks for the advice. I’m heading out to kill it now.","└ Do you really have to kill it?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. Rabbits pass through that area, so I need it gone if I want to set traps there.","└ Then I guess you don’t have much choice.","└ PraiseTheSun) Are you going to use the golden shield I gave you?","└ Wild Grylls) I’m taking it with me for now. It can block at least one hit.","└ PraiseTheSun) I’ll give you a better shield later. Just wait.","└ Wild Grylls) I’m fine, though.","└ PraiseTheSun) Well, I’m not.","The preparations were complete.","All that remained was to get properly equipped.","I didn’t need the crossbow, so I packed everything else.","The Molotov cocktail was a little cumbersome, though. It looked like I needed to buy a small bag.","I’ll just grab something suitable.","I bought a small pouch from the auction house, one that could be hung from my waist.","I stored the Molotov cocktail and an elixir inside it. Just in case, I also packed the bottle containing extra oil.","I thought that was everything, but then I remembered one more thing I needed.","Ah. I need a shovel too.","A shovel for smothering the fire.","That was necessary.","Sword and shield in my hands, shovel strapped to my back.","Now it was time to go hunt Muscle Mushroom.","\"Guard the house.\"","\"...\"","I entrusted the cave to Tree Sloth, who had already climbed down from my back, and started walking.","Wonmo was still peacefully taking a nap even as I left.","He was cute, so I’d let it slide.","Everything was ready.","I set off with a slight sense of tension.","I needed to eliminate Muscle Mushroom before I could set traps and hunt the smaller animals in the area.","And while I was at it, I could also inspect the inside of the cave the mushroom had been blocking.","I wonder what’s inside.","Honestly, I was curious about the cave just as much as I was interested in setting traps.","There had to be a reason Muscle Mushroom was guarding it.","It’s not some kind of dungeon, right? And the mushroom is literally the gatekeeper?","If that were the case, going inside would be no different from poking a hornet’s nest.","There was a reason people said curiosity killed the cat.","Half worried and half excited, I headed toward the place where Muscle Mushroom was located.","Rustle—","Something suddenly sprang out of the bushes while I was walking.","Long ears and an adorable, tiny appearance.","\"Squeak?\"","A rabbit.","A rabbit had suddenly appeared.","The moment it saw me, it raised its body high, and its long ears shot upright as well.","Anyone could tell it was on guard.","Even so, the way its mouth kept twitching was ridiculously cute.","\"Hey, hey. Go on. Shoo. Shoo.\"","I had no intention of hunting it right now, so I lightly nudged it with my sword.","Maybe even that felt threatening to the rabbit.","CLANG!","The rabbit suddenly kicked the sword with all its strength.","Not the edge, but the flat of the blade.","Judging by the clear metallic sound, the kick carried considerable force.","It was strong enough to throw me off balance and make me stagger.","\"What the hell...?\"","I stared in disbelief as the rabbit fled into the bushes.","I had almost fallen over from a single kick.","Apparently, even rabbits were different when they lived in the Forest of Four Seasons.","If that kick hit me directly, I’d probably end up with a cracked bone at minimum.","What kind of ridiculous forest is this?","Now even the rabbits were dangerous.","This was absurd.","If I wanted to set traps, I would probably need to use something with serious killing power.","Otherwise, those rabbits might just destroy every trap I set.","My head was already starting to hurt, but hunting the mushroom came first.","\"...Found it.\"","Following the familiar path, I arrived at Muscle Mushroom’s location.","It was still stationed in front of the cave like a gatekeeper.","As long as I didn’t approach too closely, it probably wouldn’t wake up.","I carefully pulled the Molotov cocktail out of my bag.","Crackle!","I lit the wick with the ignition stone, and flames immediately began licking upward.","I stared at Muscle Mushroom.","It still hadn’t moved an inch.","Apparently, it really did only wake up when something came close.","\"Hraaah!\"","With a forceful shout, I hurled the Molotov cocktail as hard as I could.","It flew through the air while spinning, leaving a ring of flame behind it.","Muscle Mushroom remained rooted to the ground right up until the bottle reached it.","Crash!","The Molotov smashed against the mushroom’s body and shattered.","WHOOOSH!","A huge blaze engulfed the entire mushroom.","The easily ignited oil and alcohol fed the flames, while the sand clung thickly to its body.","\"Kuuuuuu!\"","Sensing danger, Muscle Mushroom began pulling its arms and legs out of the ground.","I didn’t miss the opening.","I charged forward exactly as planned.","The flames were hot, but I only needed to get close once.","Slash!","Before one of its legs could completely pull free, I severed it with my sword.","No matter how muscular it was, losing a leg was enough to make it fall.","BOOM!","Muscle Mushroom crashed to the ground.","The flames intensified.","Pop-pop-pop!","\"Ugh!\"","Then a series of small explosions suddenly erupted.","Fortunately, I had already backed away.","Otherwise, I might have been caught in them.","They were only about as powerful as firecrackers, but burns were still serious injuries.","It released its spores.","Allfather’s advice had been right.","Apparently, it had tried to scatter spores to reproduce, only for them to explode in the flames.","The creature thrashed around for a while.","Only after its entire body was engulfed in fire did it gradually grow still.","Perhaps because it was a mushroom, the smell of it burning wasn’t particularly unpleasant.","If anything, it had a strangely appetizing aroma.","That doesn’t mean I’m going to eat it.","Thanks to the strategy I had prepared in advance, I defeated it without much trouble.","Still, I planned to wait a little longer to make sure it was truly dead.","Crackle. Crackle.","After some time, Muscle Mushroom had been burned completely black.","The flames gradually began to die down as well.","Deciding that was enough, I pulled the shovel off my back.","Then I covered the remains with sand and completely extinguished the fire.","Animals might come because of the smell.","The aroma was pleasant enough that it might attract beasts.","I thought about what to do before deciding to move the mushroom corpse.","There might still be embers, so I’ll push it somewhere with less grass.","I shoved it along with the shovel until it was tucked away in a corner.","Even if an animal came, it would probably be more interested in the mushroom than the cave.","With the cleanup finished, I finally looked into the cave Muscle Mushroom had been guarding.","Because of the angle of the sunlight, the interior was extremely dark.","I could see reasonably well even in darkness.","But if I wanted to investigate properly, I would probably need a torch.","Good thing I brought some cloth.","I picked up a large branch from the ground.","After wrapping it tightly with cloth, I lit it using the ignition stone.","Whoosh!","The moment the torch flared to life, the inside of the cave became much brighter.","Overall, the interior resembled the cave where I lived.","It was spacious in every direction, giving it a surprisingly comfortable atmosphere.","\"Not bad...\"","I stopped halfway through looking around.","Thanks to the torchlight, I could now see what was at the far end of the cave.","It wasn’t some dangerous beast.","It had just caught me off guard because it stood out so much.","Sparkle. Sparkle.","\"...A mushroom?\"","A golden mushroom was shining brilliantly.","Is it poisonous?","It looked like the kind of thing no sane person would ever want to eat."]},{"title":"Chapter 40","paragraphs":["Scammer (1)","I stared at the golden mushroom sparkling in front of me.","Even after I extinguished the torch, the mushroom continued emitting its own golden light.","Apparently, this was what Muscle Mushroom had been guarding.","It looks poisonous just from looking at it.","As a rule of thumb, it was safer to assume most mushrooms were poisonous.","And brightly colored plants and animals were poisonous nine times out of ten.","So there was a very high chance this golden mushroom contained poison.","It is pretty fascinating, though.","I slowly approached the golden mushroom.","Only after getting closer did I realize it was much larger than I had expected.","It was only slightly smaller than the fish I had caught before.","For a mushroom, it was enormous.","This seriously looks like something that mustached character would eat.","A certain plumber in overalls suddenly came to mind.","Would he grow bigger or stronger if he ate this mushroom?","Maybe he could just run straight into monsters and send them flying.","Even while entertaining those pointless thoughts, I didn’t lower my guard.","For all I knew, this thing might suddenly start moving like Muscle Mushroom had.","Fortunately, the golden mushroom did not spring to its feet.","It merely continued sparkling.","What the hell is this thing?","Even as I examined the mushroom, I kept watch behind me.","For safety’s sake, it would probably be best to pick it and return to the shelter.","I should put on gloves, just in case.","I put on the gloves I had stored in my pouch.","The mushroom was large enough that I would need both hands to carry it, but that wasn’t a problem.","I could hang the sword at my waist and strap the shovel and shield to my back.","Come to think of it, I need a scabbard.","Normally, swords came with scabbards, but the Heavenly Demon’s sword did not.","Either it had never had one to begin with, or she had simply forgotten to include it when she gave me the sword.","I was planning to trade fasting pills with her soon anyway, so I could ask through the one-on-one chat.","Tug!","\"Hm?\"","My eyes widened.","It seemed firmly embedded and wouldn’t come out easily.","No, wait.","As far as I knew, mushrooms didn’t have roots.","So it was simply stuck.","\"GRAAAAH!\"","Pop!","Only after putting almost all my strength into it did I finally manage to pull it free.","The recoil nearly made me fall backward, but I barely managed to regain my balance.","Then I looked at the spot where it had been growing and noticed a round hole in the ground.","Was it growing here for a really long time?","Apparently, it had stayed there long enough to bore a hole into solid stone.","I carefully carried the golden mushroom outside with both hands.","The moment I stepped out, a rich, savory aroma tickled my nose.","It was coming from the charred remains of Muscle Mushroom.","\"Let’s get out of here.\"","I hurried away before some beast was attracted by the smell.","Part of me wanted to poke around inside the cave with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","But any further curiosity might genuinely put my life in danger.","It was better to restrain myself.","Throb!","As I hurried along, a sudden headache struck me.","I frowned at the unexpected pain, but it wasn’t something I could easily ignore.","\"What is this?\"","Even while grimacing, I kept moving.","The headache disappeared before long, but the uneasy feeling remained.","Maybe the golden mushroom was the cause.","I should probably get back to the shelter as quickly as possible.","At least nothing attacked me on the way back.","After arriving at the shelter, I examined the golden mushroom again.","It really was huge.","And I was curious about what exactly it was.","I took a photo of the mushroom and posted it on the gallery.","Title: Anyone know this mushroom?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of the golden mushroom compared to a hand)","Found this in the cave Muscle Mushroom was blocking.","It shines this beautiful golden color. It’s poisonous, right? It’s also freaking huge.","└ Starlight Princess) What a pretty mushroom. But you really shouldn’t eat mushrooms.","└ Wild Grylls) I only brought it back because it looked interesting. I have absolutely no intention of eating it.","└ Eat that and I’ll give you 100 billion euros lol.","└ I’ll give you 100,000 gold lmao.","└ Starlight Princess) You people are terrible.","└ PraiseTheSun) Look at that brilliant glow. You found it in a cave?","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah. It was really hard to pull out too.","└ PraiseTheSun) That thing looks like it’s literally advertising, \"I’m poisonous.\"","└ Wild Grylls) That’s why I’m thinking about keeping it as decoration.","└ PraiseTheSun) Wouldn’t be bad as an ornament.","But everyone only commented on how pretty it was.","Apparently, none of them knew what the mushroom actually was.","That left only one person.","Allfather.","└ Allfather) Hoho. You’ve found another unusual thing this time.","└ Wild Grylls) Do you know what this mushroom is?","└ Allfather) Of course I do. Throw it away immediately.","└ Wild Grylls) Huh?","A comment telling me to get rid of it immediately appeared.","Naturally, I couldn’t help but wonder why.","Then Allfather’s following comment hit me with quite a shock.","Everyone else had simply thought the golden mushroom looked fascinating.","└ Allfather) Did you experience any headaches or dizziness while bringing it back?","└ Wild Grylls) I did get a slight headache, but it disappeared right away.","└ Allfather) It seems the medicine I gave you before was effective. Simply being near it should normally cause symptoms.","└ Wild Grylls) What kind of mushroom is this?","└ Allfather) Its name is quite ordinary. It’s called the Golden Mushroom. It’s one of the rarest mushrooms in existence and is sometimes called the King of Mushrooms.","As expected of the Forest of Four Seasons.","It truly was a place inhabited by all sorts of bizarre plants and animals.","This thing was even called the King of Mushrooms.","I became curious about exactly what made it a \"king.\"","└ Wild Grylls) If it’s the king, doesn’t that mean it’s good?","└ Allfather) With mushrooms, that title carries both positive and negative meanings. Which would you like to hear first?","└ Wild Grylls) Tell me the negative part first.","└ Allfather) A single bite will cause all your internal organs to melt. Your bones and muscles as well.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;;","That sounded horrifying just from reading it.","Not only your bones and muscles, but even your organs would melt?","Even drinking a bucket of hydrochloric acid probably wouldn’t do that much damage.","That meant the mushroom contained an unimaginably potent poison.","Naturally, I wanted to stay far away from it.","└ Wild Grylls) What’s the positive part?","└ Allfather) If you’re lucky, those melted organs, bones, and muscles can be restored. And not merely restored—your entire body would advance several stages beyond what it was before.","└ Isn’t that basically Body Reformation?","└ From the sound of it, yeah.","└ Allfather) It isn’t merely Body Reformation. According to legend, one can obtain the body of a god.","└ Wild Grylls) Whoa.","So there was a reason it was called the King of Mushrooms.","High risk, high reward.","Which meant I definitely wasn’t eating it.","There was absolutely no reason for me to take that gamble.","Just imagining my entire body melting was horrifying enough.","└ Allfather) It would likely be dangerous even for someone with complete immunity to poison. I recommend throwing it away.","└ Wild Grylls) So even poison immunity doesn’t matter?","└ Allfather) According to legend, the odds are fifty-fifty. It makes no distinction between people.","└ Wild Grylls) Guess I should throw it away, then. Unless you want it for research?","└ Why don’t you give it to us?","└ I’ll eat it and tell you what happens.","└ Do you seriously not value your life?","└ My life’s already ruined, so I might as well try eating that thing lol.","└ Why is your life ruined?","└ I went all-in on Kaspel Mine stock and got wiped out.","└ Why?","└ The mine collapsed.","└ Ah... damn. Hang in there.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is certainly intriguing, but it seems far too dangerous. This lady is not particularly interested either.","└ SwordMaster) Scared?","└ Heavenly Demon) Hm. I suddenly feel like bringing down the banhammer.","└ SwordMaster) Shit ;;","└ Lmaoooo, she’s already getting drunk on power.","└ Isn’t she going to develop bad habits like this?","└ The head mod will deal with it somehow.","└ Passing Dwarf) Can’t you make alcohol out of that?","└ Wild Grylls) Probably not with mushrooms. There was a guy who died after drinking water he’d boiled mushrooms in.","└ Passing Dwarf) Who was that? What a fucking idiot.","└ Wild Grylls) My father, asshole.","└ Passing Dwarf) Ah. I’m seriously sorry ;;","└ Wild Grylls) I’m kidding lol. My dad died in an accident.","└ Passing Dwarf) You bastard.","└ Passing Dwarf) No, wait ;; sorry. I’m just sorry ;;","└ He sobered up the second he cursed at him lmaoooo.","└ That panic lmaooo.","└ PraiseTheSun) Can’t you at least keep it as decoration?","└ Wild Grylls) Apparently just being near it causes headaches and dizziness.","└ PraiseTheSun) Then put it behind glass. I really like the golden color.","└ Allfather) Forgive me for saying so, but I believe researching it would be far more valuable. If you give it to me, I’ll compensate you well enough that you won’t feel disappointed.","└ PraiseTheSun) I can make sure you’re not disappointed either. How much money do you need?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t really need money, though...","At the moment, money was the one thing I had in abundance.","The owlbear corpse alone had left me quite well-off.","The real problem was that even with plenty of money, I still couldn’t buy most of the things I actually needed.","PraiseTheSun seemed to realize that too and immediately left another comment.","└ PraiseTheSun) Now that I think about it, you’re right. Is there anything you want?","└ Wild Grylls) I want to get out of here.","└ PraiseTheSun) Uh... sorry. Don’t think I can help with that. Just give the mushroom to that mage.","└ Allfather) I don’t seem to have anything particularly suitable to give you either. Is there anything you need?","There they go fighting again.","Why are these people always so eager to tear into each other?","But as everyone knew, the Heavenly Demon was currently a sub-mod.","And sub-mods had the authority to ban people too.","I couldn’t put the Golden Mushroom up on the auction house either.","I didn’t want to hear the next day that someone had eaten it and died.","But selling it for money also felt awkward.","The risk was simply too high.","It was, quite literally, more trouble than it was worth.","After thinking for a while, I left another comment.","└ Wild Grylls) If anything, maybe armor? I think that’d be useful.","└ SwordMaster) That’s a good idea. Since you’re in a forest, leather armor would probably be better than metal armor.","└ Heavenly Demon) Rather than that, why not learn protective qi?","└ Wild Grylls) How do I use that?","└ SwordMaster) Grylls still can’t even use an Aura Blade. It’ll be a long time before he can use an Aura Shield.","└ Heavenly Demon) It is not an Aura Blade, but Sword Force. And it is not an Aura Shield, but protective qi.","└ SwordMaster) Same thing. Do you really have to nitpick every time?","└ Heavenly Demon) What did you say? To this lady, that sounded very much like you were asking for the banhammer.","└ SwordMaster) Ha, shit ;; That’s seriously too much. Head mod, are you watching this?","└ Don’tAbandonTheHero) Sub-mod! Please restrain yourself a little!","└ Heavenly Demon) Hm. Very well. This lady shall overlook it out of her boundless generosity.","└ SwordMaster) ;;","└ Princess Chaenggu) Huh? Why do you need armor? I already gave you a uniform!","└ Wild Grylls) This thing actually provides protection?","└ Princess Chaenggu) That’s hurtful! The uniforms developed by Mephisto perform even better than leather armor!","└ Wild Grylls) Seriously?","└ That’s actually true. Sometimes people even wear the uniform into dungeons lol.","└ It’s expensive, but it’s more convenient and performs better than leather armor.","└ Wild Grylls) Why is it made like that?","└ Because there were way too many people stabbing each other.","└ It’s for protecting the players. Sports are basically miniature battlefields here.","└ You’d probably be fine even after getting hit by a magic arrow lmao.","└ Wild Grylls) ;;","Apparently, no matter how advanced the culture was, the savagery of the era still showed through.","Just in case, I looked for another uniform.","I couldn’t exactly test it with the Heavenly Demon’s sword, so I used an ordinary dagger.","Scrape! Scrape!","\"Oh.\"","Even after dragging the dagger firmly across the uniform several times, it remained intact.","Curious, I stretched the uniform taut and stabbed at it with the dagger.","Still nothing.","This was perfect for me.","Beasts are dangerous in the forest, but minor injuries are even more dangerous.","Even a tiny cut could cause serious trouble if poison or germs got inside.","That said, the uniform was still far too thin despite its performance.","If I wore leather armor over it, the protection would probably be even better.","└ Wild Grylls) The uniform really is good. Still, I think I should have leather armor too, just in case. This is too thin.","└ Princess Chaenggu) Then how about wearing several uniforms on top of each other?","└ Wild Grylls) Are you a genius?","└ Princess Chaenggu) Hehe. I’m pretty smart.","└ Sure. Still an idiot who cheers for Chaeyu though lol.","└ Just wear the uniforms lol. Whatever the hell you put on, you’ll probably die in one hit anyway.","└ One hit and you’re off to join Aragon~","In the end, even the extra armor was replaced with more uniforms.","Afterward, I tried offering the mushroom to Princess Chaenggu, but she immediately refused.","She had no interest in buying it as decoration either and simply said she’d give me a few more uniforms.","I’m receiving way too much from this person.","She said supporting her team was enough, but I still felt guilty.","If I found something good later, I was definitely giving it to her.","Anyway, I decided to postpone figuring out what to do with the Golden Mushroom.","It was such a high-risk item that its position was awkward.","Wonmo might eat it too...","I needed to store it somewhere as inconspicuous as possible.","Granted, something golden would stand out no matter where I put it, but I had somewhere in mind.","The box that had come with the items the dwarf gave me last time.","I stored the mushroom inside it.","Then, so Wonmo’s sharp sense of smell wouldn’t pick it up, I placed the box outside the cave.","The elixirs were stored in a different box, so there wasn’t much of a problem.","If I ran low on them, I could just buy more from the auction house.","Good. That’s settled.","With the Golden Mushroom dealt with, I raised my head.","The sun had already begun to sink, if only slightly.","It looked like I should start preparing for the night.","There might be spores on my clothes, so I should wash immediately.","And just like that, another day came to an end.","***","Deep in the night, when everyone was asleep, only the sounds of insects filled the forest.","Inside the cave, the faint crackling of the campfire could be heard.","Beyond that were the quiet breathing of a person, the breathing of beasts, and other gentle sounds.","Everyone was asleep in their own way.","It was an extremely peaceful scene.","Clatter! Clatter!","A rough noise suddenly broke through the silence.","It wasn’t coming from inside the cave.","It came from the box outside.","The box continued rattling several times before eventually toppling onto its side.","Roll—","Its contents spilled out.","Among them was the mushroom that glowed golden even beneath the darkness of night.","Rustle—","Amazingly, the Golden Mushroom, which had fallen onto its side, pushed itself upright.","Tiny arms and legs had sprouted from its body.","They were infinitely more pitiful and adorable than the limbs of Muscle Mushroom.","But the fact that it had limbs meant one thing.","It could move.","Pitter-patter-pitter-patter—","The Golden Mushroom moved its short little legs and headed into the dark forest.","Quietly.","Secretly.","So that no one would ever find it.","Until the Golden Mushroom completely disappeared, nothing but peaceful breathing could be heard from the cave.","Time passed.","Morning came.","\"What the hell? Where’d the mushroom go?\"","Only then did Grylls realize the mushroom had disappeared.","He had already sensed something was wrong when he saw the box outside lying on its side.","When he immediately checked inside—","the Golden Mushroom he had stored there was gone.","\"N-No way...!\"","Grylls’s eyes widened.","He thought he knew why the mushroom had disappeared.","He stopped rummaging through the box and hurried back into the cave.","\"Wonmo! Open your mouth!\"","\"Kkyuu...?\"","\"What did you eat yesterday? You didn’t eat the mushroom, did you?!\"","Grylls forcibly opened poor Wonmo’s beak for no reason.","Fortunately, Wonmo hadn’t eaten the mushroom.","He had simply slept peacefully through the night.","After thoroughly checking him over, Grylls sighed in relief.","He didn’t bother inspecting Tree Sloth separately.","That creature had absurdly sharp instincts and hadn’t gone anywhere near the mushroom in the first place.","Relieved, Grylls was left with a new question.","\"No, seriously. It’s not like the thing had legs. Where the hell did it go?\"","It actually had grown legs.","Grylls simply had no idea.","Such was the mysterious Forest of Four Seasons."]},{"title":"Chapter 41","paragraphs":["Scammer (2)","It was enough to make a ghost wail in disbelief.","I stared at the empty box.","No matter how many times I searched through it, the golden mushroom was nowhere to be found.","Wonmo hadn’t secretly eaten it either.","Unless it had somehow grown arms and legs, it had practically vanished on its own.","I couldn’t make sense of it at all.","’Did some thieving bastard like the Tree Sloth steal it?’","I stared at the Tree Sloth.","It had one of the fasting pills I had given it hooked on its claw and was nibbling away at it.","I wasn’t saying that thing had eaten the golden mushroom.","If something had eaten it, it was probably some other animal.","The Tree Sloth had tried stealing fish before.","It had failed, though.","Considering that, there were probably beasts out there that specifically targeted plants and animals rich in nutrients.","’Even so, wouldn’t the golden mushroom be way too risky?’","Even wild animals generally avoided mushrooms.","And the golden mushroom practically screamed:","I’m poisonous! Eat me and you’ll die!","Bright colors usually meant deadly poison.","Animals knew that much too.","Even if something had eaten it, there should have been some traces left behind.","The mystery refused to clear up.","’Strange.’","Then again, maybe this was for the best.","I had already been wondering what I was supposed to do with it.","Still, since there were people who wanted the golden mushroom, I made a post on the Gallery.","Title: Mushroom Disappeared","Wild Grylls","(Photo of an empty box)","I put the mushroom I picked up yesterday in this box, but when I woke up today, it was gone ;;","I thought maybe Wonmo ate it, but apparently not.","This is seriously weird.","└ Heavenly Demon: To think a mushroom escaped. Truly astonishing. Did it perhaps grow feet?","└ Wild Grylls: I’m not sure either. I looked around, but I can’t even find footprints.","└ Heavenly Demon: Surely a mushroom cannot perform Void-Stepping.","└ Wild Grylls: What’s Void-Stepping now?","└ Heavenly Demon: It is a technique that allows one to walk or run through empty air. The pinnacle of lightness techniques.","└ Wild Grylls: Can you do that too, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon: This Lady has surpassed mere Void-Stepping and reached the realm of Treading the Empty Sky. I can fly freely through the heavens.","└ Wild Grylls: Oh ;;","└ SwordMaster: Aren’t you exaggerating a little too much? If you’re really at that level, wouldn’t that be Grand Master territory?","└ Heavenly Demon: What does that mean? Explain it in terms this Lady can understand.","└ Wouldn’t that be equivalent to the Profound Realm in the Central Plains?","└ Probably around there. Has anyone in the Central Plains even reached the Profound Realm?","└ You’d probably have to dig through historical records to find one.","└ Even someone in the Transformation Realm could destroy an entire city, so the Profound Realm is just lol.","└ Heavenly Demon: I understand. This Lady has reached that so-called Profound Realm.","└ SwordMaster: Yes, yes~ I’m sure you have.","└ Allfather: Perhaps the mushroom really did have legs.","└ Wild Grylls: Seriously?","└ Allfather: Considering muscular mushrooms exist, arms and legs would practically be standard equipment for a golden mushroom.","└ Wild Grylls: But it was completely still when I caught it?","└ Allfather: It would be a mistake to judge the laws of nature by your common sense, Mr. Grylls. Think of the Tree Sloth.","└ Wild Grylls: Ah.","After hearing the wisdom of the sage Allfather, I realized something.","Maybe it really did have legs.","This world was fantasy.","And the Forest of Four Seasons was a place where even the common sense of people from this world didn’t apply.","And I was stuck suffering there.","Putting it that way made me a little sad.","Anyway, no matter what happened, I couldn’t afford to judge things by common sense.","I didn’t even need to look far.","There was a sloth around here that could snatch arrows out of the air.","└ Wild Grylls: Guess I should just consider it lost.","└ Allfather: A shame. I wanted to study it.","It was unfortunate, but there was nothing I could do.","It had happened because of carelessness that wasn’t exactly carelessness.","I should probably just be thankful that nobody had raided me in the middle of the night.","I closed the Gallery and approached the hose to wash my face.","Trickle, trickle—","The stream of water coming through the hose was weak.","The moment I saw it, I realized what had happened.","Another fish had been caught.","Apparently, one got stuck at least once every day.","This was great.","’Once I get a fish trap from the dwarf too, I won’t have to worry about food anymore.’","It looked like I could stop worrying about food for the time being.","I was planning to set more traps soon too, so things would only become more plentiful.","If I learned even a half-decent method of hunting, starving to death probably wouldn’t be an issue.","I’d die from poison, disease, or getting eaten by a beast instead.","Or maybe I’d step into some bizarre place and die a pointless death.","There were plenty of ways to die.","’...Right. Better than starving, I guess?’","I suddenly felt depressed, but quickly shook it off.","The important thing was the fish.","I gathered the necessary gear and headed toward the river.","I didn’t forget to feed Wonmo before leaving.","Splash! Splash!","When I eventually reached the river, just as I expected, a fish was trapped in the narrow passage.","It was huge, large enough to completely block the hose’s intake.","Until now, the fish I had caught had all been red.","This one was golden.","’...Does this one have poison too?’","The only poisonous fish I knew of was the pufferfish.","And as far as I knew, even those lived in the ocean.","’It doesn’t have spines either.’","More importantly, there were no spines.","Its body was completely smooth.","It was golden, but it wasn’t covered in flashy multicolored patterns.","After thinking about it for a moment, I decided to take it back as it was.","If I stayed here too long and the golden frog showed up, things would get troublesome.","\"Heave-ho.\"","This one was big enough that I had to wrap both arms around it too.","Were all the fish living in the Forest of Four Seasons this huge?","From my perspective, that was nothing but a blessing.","It meant I could eat my fill.","’I should bring a big container with me from now on.’","I made plans while wrestling with the thrashing golden fish.","For convenience, I really needed at least a container or a net.","It wasn’t because I lacked strength.","The fish was simply so large that I needed both hands to carry it.","’Or I could bring the Tree Sloth.’","The Tree Sloth was surprisingly useful.","It was practically perfect as a bodyguard.","I returned to the cave and started preparing my meal.","I was getting used to cleaning fish by now, so it didn’t take long.","’Another one?’","Out of curiosity, I searched through the organs.","Sure enough, there was another inner core.","This time, instead of red, the inner core was closer to golden in color.","Did every fish living in the Forest of Four Seasons carry an inner core?","This wasn’t just once or twice anymore.","It was already the third time.","I was seriously starting to suspect something.","’Doesn’t this mean I can become stronger just by eating fish? Then why is the survival rate here supposedly so atrocious?’","While the fish grilled to a golden brown, I stared at the inner core.","The Heavenly Demon had said they were more like inferior versions of elixirs, but an inner core was still an inner core.","The fact that eating one could make me stronger in a short amount of time hadn’t changed.","’Maybe it’s because you still can’t escape, regardless of how strong you become?’","That seemed highly likely.","What good was getting stronger if you couldn’t get out?","’And I’m an unusual case too.’","More importantly, I was an unusual case.","I could still use the Gallery perfectly fine despite being trapped in the Forest of Four Seasons.","Unlike everyone else, I could at least ask for advice.","Other people had nothing like that.","They were basically smashing their heads against a wall with no information whatsoever.","Even I would have been torn to pieces by the Mad Dog if I hadn’t had the Gallery.","’I should flip the fish.’","At this rate, it was going to burn.","I flipped the fish cooking on the broad stone slab.","I could decide what to do with the inner core later.","There was no rush.","If nothing else worked, I could always put it up on the auction house.","The Heavenly Demon had advised me not to eat one until I reached at least the Peak Realm.","’I don’t even know exactly how strong the Peak Realm is.’","More importantly, my fundamentals were still lacking.","Right now, strengthening my foundation was more important.","Eating the inner core probably wouldn’t hurt me permanently, but I could end up bedridden and feverish for several days.","For someone whose survival was the top priority, a high fever was extremely dangerous.","I had felt how serious it was the last time I suffered from one.","’Come to think of it, the auction should be ending soon.’","The thought occurred to me while I tore into the deliciously grilled fish.","I had listed it around lunchtime yesterday, so the auction should finish in a few hours.","[Inner Core: 750 silver taels]","The price had risen considerably.","Judging by how much the frequency of new bids had slowed, there was a good chance it would stay around that amount.","’Trust really is important, huh?’","The auction house had a review system.","There was no numerical rating, but by reading reviews, you could more or less judge how trustworthy someone was.","Without something like that, the auction house would have become a paradise for scammers.","And considering the brutal transaction fees, scamming people wasn’t exactly a smart idea anyway.","’For me, trust is everything.’","Once trust was lost, it was difficult to recover.","For someone like me who obtained most things through the Gallery, losing credibility would be devastating.","And this wasn’t some tiny amount of money either.","It was an enormous sum.","I couldn’t afford to treat it like a joke.","’Even if what I gave the Heavenly Demon really was an inner core, if the one on the auction house isn’t...’","There was a high probability that it really was an inner core.","Still, I couldn’t completely rule out the possibility that someone was lying.","You might say I distrusted people too much, but at the very least, I didn’t trust anonymous users.","When I first fell into the Forest of Four Seasons, there had even been bastards telling me to die and become fertilizer.","That said everything.","A person’s true malice emerged when they could hide behind anonymity.","’Let’s see how the auction turns out first.’","For now, what mattered was eating this delicious fish.","I gave Wonmo a few chunks of meat and finished off the rest.","It tasted far better than the red fish.","I wasn’t exaggerating when I said it tasted almost like pork.","\"Now that was filling.\"","After finishing off such a huge catch, I entered the cave and began circulating my cultivation technique.","It was the method I practiced based on the fundamentals the Heavenly Demon had taught me and SwordMaster’s advice.","Was it because I had just eaten the golden fish?","I could feel an energy like raging waves coursing through my body.","’Rather than waves... what should I call it? A storm?’","The cultivation technique the Heavenly Demon had taught me was called the Heavenly Demon Divine Art.","So maybe it was more appropriate to describe the sensation as a storm rather than waves.","Eventually, I brought that storm-like energy completely under control and raised my hand.","A faint blue energy shimmered above it like heat haze.","’It amazes me every time I see it.’","I had definitely been an ordinary person.","A completely average man with nothing particularly remarkable about him.","And yet I had somehow fallen into this bizarre forest, and now I could even manipulate mana.","I constantly reminded myself that this place was reality, but sometimes I still wondered.","Was I actually dreaming?","The haze rising from my hand was fantasy itself.","That only made the feeling stronger.","’Considering what it felt like when the Mad Dog bit me, this is definitely real.’","I extinguished the haze and stepped outside the cave.","I planned to spend the morning making traps and exploring.","As for where I would explore—","The muscular mushrooms I had burned yesterday with fire magic (physical), and the cave they had come from.","Continuing with the same glossary and style, including Wild Grylls, Heavenly Demon, SwordMaster, Allfather, Forest of Four Seasons, Tree Sloth, Wonmo, inner core, Gallery , and the established martial-arts terminology.","If the golden mushroom really had grown two legs and run away, there was a chance it had gone back to the cave.","Title: Want to Make a Trap, Any Advice?","Wild Grylls","I found a place where rabbits show up yesterday. Anyone know how to make a decent trap?","They’re not ordinary rabbits, though. Their back kicks are insanely strong, so take that into consideration.","└ Why not just buy a bear trap and set it up?","└ If you use a bear trap, a rabbit will just get split in half ;;","└ Just dig a decent-sized pit and stick spears in it.","└ That’s dangerous. Better to aim for capturing them alive rather than using something lethal.","As expected of the Gallery.","They generously shared all kinds of useful tips.","└ Why don’t you use yourself as bait? You might catch a big one that way lol.","└ Sounds fun lol.","└ If you fail, you die. If you succeed, you feast. Isn’t that perfect?!","As expected of the Gallery.","Idiots and morons appeared occasionally—","No, frequently.","I ignored all the nonsense and started designing a trap.","The best option seemed to be a pitfall.","Dig a hole and cover it with a board.","Once enough weight was placed on top of it, the board would give way and whatever stepped on it would fall into the pit.","’Considering how powerful those rabbits’ back kicks are, they’d jump right out of a shallow pit.’","Digging the pit deep enough was important, but the board covering it mattered just as much.","I didn’t want the board to simply collapse and fall into the pit.","I wanted a trap that worked through weight.","’Step on the board, the board opens, you fall into the pit, and then the board closes again.’","This seemed like the best method.","I decided on that design.","Of course, choosing a design and actually building it were two different things.","I squeezed my brain as hard as I could while planning the mechanism.","’The board has to open and close depending on the weight. I need to account for the rabbit’s weight too.’","Securing the board in place was essential.","I bought some large iron nails from the auction house.","I planned to use them to anchor one side of the board.","’And I’ll need a counterweight to pull the board back up.’","I set up two sturdy branches and placed another branch horizontally between them.","The easiest way to picture it was like a rotisserie barbecue.","The kind where you put meat on a spit and rotate it while roasting.","This wasn’t a barbecue, though.","It was a trap.","So instead of meat, I fitted a metal cylinder onto it.","Finally, I tied a rock to a cord to serve as the counterweight.","Clunk!","I pressed down firmly on the board with one finger.","It lowered.","The instant I removed my finger, the counterweight pulled the board back up.","Perfect.","The trap was complete.","Now all I had to do was move this design over there.","’Though I’ll need to make it bigger.’","For that, aside from the nails and hammer, I would have to make several trips back and forth.","I told the Tree Sloth to guard the house properly and finished preparing.","A weapon to protect myself.","A shovel for digging.","An elixir in case something went wrong.","And various other necessities.","Once everything was ready, I headed toward the area where the rabbits appeared.","’After moving the trap, I should check whether the mushroom is there first.’","Unfortunately, the golden mushroom wasn’t inside the cave.","The muscular mushrooms that had been burned completely black were still there too.","Apparently, despite their appetizing smell, they still looked too suspicious to eat.","Now that I had checked for the mushroom, only the trap remained.","Digging the pit wasn’t particularly difficult either.","A while later, after finishing the entire trap setup, an indescribable sense of accomplishment washed over me.","Soon, I would finally be able to eat meat instead of fish.","’As for butchering it... well, I’ll have to do that myself.’","To prevent the animals from becoming suspicious, I scattered some dirt over the board and even placed grass on top.","Now all that remained was patience.","I gathered all my equipment and returned to the cave.","’It’s already eleven.’","Time had flown while I was busy doing this and that.","I wondered what I should do until the inner core auction ended, then rummaged through my pocket.","The golden inner core came out.","I briefly considered putting this one on the auction house too.","’Let’s see how the first auction turns out before listing this one. Before that...’","Grrrrrgle—","My stomach hurt like hell.","It happened every time I ate fish.","Previously, my stomach had started hurting almost immediately after eating, but this time it had taken a while.","I really needed to build a toilet soon.","Digging a hole every single time was becoming exhausting.","After thoroughly emptying my bowels, I logged into the Gallery.","I wanted to check the current bid on the inner core.","[Inner Core: 750 silver taels]","The bid hadn’t changed.","It had been frozen at that amount for six hours.","I had a feeling the auction would probably end like this.","So I modified the remaining auction time.","[Would you like to change the auction end time to 30 minutes from now?]","[Once the deadline has been modified, it cannot be changed again.]","I accepted without hesitation.","Thirty minutes was still plenty of time.","And what was I going to do during those thirty minutes?","Practice my cultivation technique.","Not recklessly, either.","I planned to firmly establish my fundamentals, just as the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","If I somehow patched all the holes in my foundation, it would probably become easier to obtain something like an Aura Blade or Sword Gang or whatever it was called.","’This is hard. Really hard.’","Fundamentals weren’t something you simply memorized.","You had to understand them.","That was the hardest part for me, since I wasn’t originally from this world.","Even though I had grown stronger until now through what could almost be called shortcuts, the basics were still a problem.","’Just thirty minutes of practice.’","It took more than an hour.","Once I became immersed in it, I completely lost track of time.","And unless I logged into the Gallery, my sense of time became especially vague.","So I opened the Gallery to see how much the inner core had sold for.","[Why Grylls Is a Scammer]","[Grylls, Explain Yourself!]","[Grylls, Explain Yourself!]","[This bastard is just a scammer lol]","[Isn’t the whole \"I’m in the Forest of Four Seasons\" thing a lie too?]","[Honestly, I think he should be banned.]","[Upvote if Grylls is dead lol]","\"What the hell?\"","What had happened for the Gallery to become this much of a dumpster fire?","And most of the posts were about me.","I couldn’t understand it at all.","The easiest thing to do was check the trending posts.","Something must have been posted there to cause all this.","[Wild Grylls Is a Scammer. Don’t Trust This Bastard.]","It was the trending post with the highest number of upvotes.","Naturally, it was about me.","There was no way I could just ignore a title like that.","I opened it immediately.","Title: Wild Grylls Is a Scammer. Don’t Trust This Bastard.","(Photo of an inner core resting on someone’s palm)","This is supposed to be an inner core? LMAOOOO what kind of bullshit is this?","It’s just a normal marble.","I’m actually legendary for paying 750 silver taels for this shit.","You can’t trust this Grylls bastard.","Take responsibility, you son of a bitch.","Give me my money back.","└ Didn’t Heavenly Demon say it was real?","└ And you believed that? LMAO.","└ It was kind of weird that an inner core came out every time he caught a fish though~","└ I’m never buying anything from Grylls again lol.","└ You never bought anything from him in the first place.","└ Exactly lol.","└ Is this bastard some kind of scammer?","└ Are we sure this guy is actually the buyer?","└ Yeah. The number beside his name matches the winning bidder.","└ Holy shit lol. How much did he lose? LMAO.","└ At that price, he probably blew his entire fortune lol.","└ Damn. Poor bastard lol.","└ Shouldn’t Grylls refund him?","└ What about the transaction fee?","└ Why should that matter? If you scammed someone, you should return all the money, dumbass.","└ Doesn’t the Moderator ban people for scamming?","└ Yeah. Permanent ban at minimum.","Just what exactly are you trying to do?","’Is he going to ban me?’","***","I had suspected it.","And sure enough, things unfolded exactly as I feared.","Apparently, I had trusted people too much.","Fortunately, this was at least one of the possibilities I had already anticipated.","I was just about to leave a comment when—","[Heavenly Demon: You need not worry, sir. This Lady shall resolve the matter.]","[Wild Grylls: What?]","[Heavenly Demon: That ungrateful wretch requires divine punishment. Wait there.]","A private message from the Heavenly Demon arrived.","The strategist and brains of the Demonic Cult.","The Demon Brain was currently extremely confused.","Being summoned by the Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, wasn’t particularly confusing.","When Heaven called, one naturally answered.","But even the Demon Brain, famed throughout the world for his intellect, couldn’t help being flustered by the order Heaven itself had just given him.","\"H-Heavenly One. May I... ask you to repeat what you just said?\"","\"How strange for you to ask twice. Very well. In this Lady’s boundless generosity, I shall command you once more.\"","Yu Sowol, seated upon her jade throne, spoke in a deliberately irritated tone.","\"Log into the Gallery.\"","\"...\"","\"You ate the inner core this Lady gave you and advanced in your realm. All you need do is make a post proving it.\"","In other words, she wanted him to log into the Gallery and upload what people commonly called a verification post .","On the surface, it sounded extremely simple.","But who was the Demon Brain?","Wasn’t he a hardcore Gallery addict who spent most of his time there insulting his superior—the Heavenly Demon?","’I’m fucked.’","The Demon Brain.","The Clever Demonic Cultist.","Wi Seorak.","’I’m seriously fucked.’","He had found himself in a life-or-death crisis."]},{"title":"Chapter 42","paragraphs":["Scammer (3)","The Demon Brain, Wi Seorak, had survived countless crises throughout his life.","The greatest among them had been the oppression of those in power.","With his extraordinary intellect, Wi Seorak was a threat to them.","A mere commoner like Wi Seorak being vastly superior to the proud scions of prestigious families?","That was something they could never tolerate.","So whenever they found an opportunity, they kicked away the ladder beneath him.","But Wi Seorak had clawed his way upward through sheer spite and grit.","He had never needed a ladder in the first place.","By this point, one might have expected them to acknowledge him.","Unfortunately, Wi Seorak had terrible luck with people.","All that came back to him was even more vicious oppression.","And through that process, bitterness took root inside him.","Carrying that bitterness with him, he entered the Demonic Cult and used his exceptional mind to rise all the way to the position of Demon Brain.","\"Why are you acting like that? Do you perhaps use the Gallery as well?\"","\"That is...\"","And today, Wi Seorak found himself facing yet another crisis of a lifetime.","It was an order from the Heavenly Demon, the one who stood above all men and beneath only the heavens.","Wi Seorak’s mind spun furiously as he processed the Heavenly Demon’s command.","And after all that frantic calculation, he arrived at a single conclusion.","’I’m fucked.’","He was seriously screwed.","For an utterly ridiculous reason, he had come face-to-face with the greatest crisis of his life.","Since Wi Seorak himself was an avid Gallery user, he understood the current situation perfectly well.","The inner core listed on the auction house had supposedly been fake.","And the incident involved Wild Grylls, the man who had recently caused one uproar after another.","’Wild Grylls. She must have stepped in to help him.’","Yu Sowol had obviously summoned him because she wanted to help Wild Grylls.","That much, Wi Seorak could have predicted.","But ordering him to log into the Gallery was completely outside his expectations.","Wi Seorak rapidly worked his mind and opened his mouth.","If even a single second of silence passed, Yu Sowol might grow suspicious.","\"Heavenly One, by the Gallery... do you mean the Continental Integrated Gallery?\"","\"That is correct.\"","\"As this is Heaven’s command, I shall obey. However, with my foolish mind, I find it difficult to grasp the situation. Please enlighten me as to your reason.\"","Even as he stalled for time, Wi Seorak’s brain never stopped turning.","If he obeyed the order, logged into the Gallery, and uploaded a verification post...","All the posts he had written insulting Yu Sowol would be exposed.","What made matters worse was that he hadn’t been using a semi-anonymous nickname.","He had been using a fully registered account.","’Damn it. I only made a registered account because I needed one, and now it’s come back to bite me like this...’","Why had Wi Seorak used a registered account?","For trading and the auction house.","The Demonic Cult was located in a fairly remote region.","As a result, maintaining a stable supply chain was critically important.","In the old days, the place had been practically abandoned, and quite a few people had gone hungry.","Things had improved considerably only after Wi Seorak restructured everything and Yu Sowol began venturing into the martial world.","’I need to resolve this without getting caught.’","At the time, he had created the account out of necessity and hadn’t thought much of it.","But who could have predicted that Yu Sowol would one day bluntly tell him, \"Reveal your username\"?","It had been Wi Seorak’s mistake not to anticipate just how different her way of thinking was from everyone else’s.","’Will Heaven respect my privacy?’","The Heavenly Demon, Yu Sowol, had a domineering and overbearing personality.","She was the type who did whatever she wanted without caring what others thought.","And because she possessed the overwhelming strength to back up that attitude, the demonic practitioners revered her.","’She has to. Otherwise, I’m dead.’","On the other hand, the Heavenly Demon on the Gallery was subtly different.","Her characteristic arrogance and self-centered nature were still there, but she had a certain humanity to her.","One only had to look at how endlessly accommodating she was toward Grylls to see that.","Wi Seorak desperately prayed that some of that consideration would extend to him as well.","Otherwise, he was going to die.","Socially.","And physically.","\"A reason... Must this Lady explain even that much to you?\"","\"...\"","\"Or is there some truth you desperately need to keep hidden from me on the Gallery?\"","\"I do not use the Gallery, Heavenly One.\"","\"You lie without so much as wetting your lips.\"","Fuck.","Wi Seorak cursed internally.","He had spoken while doing his best to keep his voice from trembling, but she had seen through him anyway.","Still, he had no choice but to lie.","Only by doing so could he hope for Yu Sowol’s \"understanding.\"","If Yu Sowol had been a completely unrestrained tyrant, his head would have been flying through the air already.","Fortunately, she was not a tyrant.","At the very least, she knew how to respect those beneath her.","Otherwise, she would have ordered them long ago to force their way into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Of course, asking for understanding after lying to her was already unreasonable.","But if he wanted to grasp even the tiniest possibility of survival, he had no other choice.","The moment he logged into the Gallery, his physical death was practically guaranteed.","This was a gamble with his life as the stake.","\"I shall believe your lie. However, from now on, it would be wise to speak the truth.\"","\"I shall keep that in mind.\"","\"Good. You asked for the reason earlier, did you not? I shall tell you everything.\"","Thank goodness.","Seriously, thank goodness.","Wi Seorak inwardly breathed a sigh of relief.","His life-or-death gamble had ended successfully.","That did not mean the crisis itself was over, however.","\"This Lady’s benefactor is currently being falsely accused. Lend me the wisdom needed to resolve the situation.\"","\"All of this humble one’s wisdom belongs to Heaven. Simply give the command.\"","\"The situation is as follows...\"","Yu Sowol’s explanation was concise yet packed with all the important details.","Of course, Wi Seorak had already pieced together the entire situation, so he was mostly pretending to listen.","Countless hypotheses had already formed in his mind.","Testing and eliminating them one by one would not be difficult.","\"Do you understand?\"","\"I understand. To think there is someone who not only doubts Heaven’s discernment but even dares to spread falsehoods. Such a person deserves divine punishment.\"","Yu Sowol narrowed her eyes at Wi Seorak.","Her gaze seemed to say:","You, of all people, have the right to say that after lying to me just now?","Wi Seorak, who had his waist bowed, couldn’t see her expression.","But he could read the atmosphere well enough.","His conscience wasn’t merely pricking him.","It felt as though someone were repeatedly stabbing it with a dagger.","He did his best to ignore it.","If a single lie was enough to save his life, then it was an absurdly cheap price.","\"May I offer my opinion?\"","\"Speak.\"","\"First, we cannot rule out the possibility that the inner core purchased at auction truly has no effect whatsoever and is merely an ordinary bead. The one given to this humble servant was certainly genuine, but there is no absolute guarantee that the other one was an inner core as well.\"","\"Hmm.\"","Yu Sowol nodded.","In truth, that point had been bothering her too.","It was also why she had let Wi Seorak’s lie slide.","This was not a problem that could be solved through simple assumptions alone.","Yu Sowol had originally planned to first confirm whether Wi Seorak knew about the Gallery, then borrow his wisdom.","It was only because of her characteristically overbearing way of speaking that she had ordered him to reveal his username first, though Yu Sowol herself failed to realize that.","’Looks like he has something to hide.’","In any case, Yu Sowol understood him.","The Gallery was the perfect piece of culture for venting desire and stress.","He had probably done plenty of things there that he would be ashamed to show others.","Every Gallery user was like that.","It was perfectly understandable.","\"Then is there no solution?\"","\"The other side has latched onto uncertainty, so we should make clever use of that same uncertainty. It is ultimately a matter of credibility.\"","\"I would say my benefactor has greater credibility.\"","\"This is not something to take lightly. Gallery users are like jackals. Once they find prey, they tear into it without caring about what came before or after.\"","\"Jackals...\"","Yu Sowol nodded at the comparison.","Whenever something entertaining happened, Gallery users swarmed toward it like madmen.","Whether it was actually true or false didn’t matter.","They simply bit and tore at it because it was entertaining.","Conversely, if they could secure enough credibility, that entire pack of jackals could be turned into allies.","\"The one who framed your benefactor likely has only one objective. To force him into an amicable settlement.\"","\"An amicable settlement?\"","\"If he were suspended from the Gallery, his life itself could be placed in danger. That is what the culprit is exploiting.\"","\"So he is playing games with another person’s life.\"","Yu Sowol looked openly displeased.","If she had her way, she would track down the bastard’s location and beat him into the ground.","But location tracking was a privilege available only to the Moderator.","She doubted the Moderator would grant her that authority.","Especially not in a situation like this.","\"Is there a way to resolve it?\"","\"There is a simple and easy method.\"","\"And what would that be?\"","\"Heaven should make an appearance in the Gallery.\"","The phrase make an appearance in the Gallery sounded ridiculous, but his point was simple.","She should verify her identity on the Gallery.","In other words, she should prove that she really was the Heavenly Demon .","The registered user who had spent all this time posting nonsense—and who had now become a Sub-Moderator—should prove that she was actually the Heavenly Demon in real life.","\"You refused this Lady’s command, yet you dare recommend that this Lady do the same thing. What a contradiction.\"","\"My apologies, Heavenly One.\"","\"Speak your true feelings without a single lie. Do you have no intention of verifying your own identity?\"","\"I would rather hang myself.\"","\"Hmm.\"","So he hated the idea that much.","Yu Sowol nodded.","She had no desire to lose a talent as capable as Wi Seorak for such an absurd reason.","\"Besides, even if I verified my identity, it would likely mean little. They could simply claim that we coordinated our stories in advance.\"","\"I see.\"","\"As for Heaven, perhaps—\"","\"Denied.\"","The answer came from Yu Sowol without the slightest hesitation.","A flat refusal.","Wi Seorak found her reaction puzzling, but he did not dare ask why.","’Is she embarrassed?’","That possibility seemed quite plausible.","After all, he knew all about the Gallery activities of the Sub-Moderator known as Heavenly Demon.","Perhaps that was also why she had been so lenient about his lie.","Empathy was the beginning of understanding.","’Maybe if she reveals her identity, there would be no point in using the Gallery anymore?’","But Wi Seorak’s guess was completely wrong.","Was Yu Sowol refusing to reveal her identity because she was embarrassed?","Absolutely not.","’How could I possibly give up a place where I can act purely on instinct without any formality or dignity whatsoever?’","If anything, Yu Sowol was completely unashamed.","Her manner of speaking and behavior barely changed between reality and the Gallery.","What she treasured was the joy of existing as a single human being , free from the mold of the Heavenly Demon .","Yu Sowol liked that life immensely.","That was precisely why she was reluctant to reveal her identity.","If she had to live as the Heavenly Demon even inside the Gallery, it would become monotonous to the point of boredom.","’There would also be those who approach me only because of this Lady’s prestige.’","Kindness directed not toward a human being , but toward the Heavenly Demon .","That would be no different from reality.","If that happened, she would quit the Gallery immediately.","Therefore, Yu Sowol could never give up her anonymity.","Anonymity was normally used as a shield.","For her, however, it was a means of revealing her true self.","’Though my benefactor doesn’t seem to care who this Lady is anyway.’","That was also one of the reasons she liked Grylls.","His consideration and respect were filled with pure goodwill.","And courtesy.","It was a warmth Yu Sowol had never experienced throughout her entire life.","That was why she wanted to help him.","\"If there is no other choice, this Lady can stake her name upon it. However, I question whether the matter is truly worth that much.\"","\"Your words are most wise.\"","So even the Heavenly Demon was human after all.","She knew how to feel embarrassment.","While Wi Seorak continued along with his not-quite-correct misunderstanding, Yu Sowol opened her elegant lips.","\"Is there another method?\"","\"There is. We simply need to redirect the pack of jackals toward the one who lied. And since your benefactor has already built up credibility, it should be relatively easy.\"","\"Then explain—wait a moment.\"","With those words, Yu Sowol stared into empty space.","Wi Seorak glanced at her behavior and immediately entered the Gallery himself.","Something had definitely happened there.","She wouldn’t have reacted like that otherwise.","’Nothing special happened, though?’","The Gallery looked no different.","It was still filled with posts insulting Grylls.","There were occasionally people defending him, but they were only a small minority.","The posts had practically become spam at this point, enough that even the Moderator had issued a warning.","\"Demon Brain.\"","\"Yes, Heavenly One.\"","\"This Lady’s benefactor says he has obtained another inner core.\"","\"What?\"","Wi Seorak’s head snapped upward.","His widened eyes clearly revealed how startled he was.","But who was Wi Seorak?","He quickly regained his composure and set his mind racing.","A moment later, having reached a conclusion, he offered Yu Sowol a suggestion.","\"Heavenly One. I have thought of a good plan.\"","\"Speak.\"","\"Is there perhaps someone on the Gallery who possesses credibility and skill, while also having no major flaws in their personality?\"","\"Hmm...\"","At that question, Yu Sowol tapped a finger against her cheek before suddenly frowning.","She looked displeased just imagining the person.","Given her appearance, even that expression was beautiful.","\"There is. Why do you ask?\"","\"Because we will need that person’s help. Though I cannot say whether they will actually agree to assist us.\"","\"They will.\"","Yu Sowol answered with certainty.","\"This Lady guarantees it.\"","\"Understood. Then...\"","Wi Seorak bowed even more deeply before making his proposal.","\"Please persuade your benefactor to give the newly discovered inner core to that person as an assistant.\""]},{"title":"Chapter 43","paragraphs":["Scammer (4)","The Gallery could be used by anyone regardless of age, gender, or social status.","Along with anonymity, that was often both its greatest strength and its greatest weakness.","In particular, it was fairly common for scammers to use the Gallery to pull all sorts of cons.","Title: Ah, fuck. I got scammed.","There was some good wild ginseng on the auction house, so I bought it, but it turned out to be ordinary ginseng. Fuck.","└ LMAOOOO, you too? Me too!","└ Ginseng and wild ginseng do look pretty similar lol.","└ This fucking bastard deleted his account immediately.","One-on-one trades were only available to registered users, but the auction house could be used by everyone.","Naturally, that meant there were plenty of criminals—in other words, shameless scammers who had no problem ripping other people off.","Whenever a large amount of money was involved, most people immediately suspected a scam.","After all, most scammers were looking for one big score.","There was no helping the suspicion.","└ Why do scammers even bother scamming? You can’t withdraw Gallery money into the real world anyway.","└ You use that money to buy other stuff. The Gallery has almost everything.","└ Being able to ignore distribution networks is a huge advantage too. You can easily get things from other countries.","└ Don’t they get banned?","└ They do, but it depends on the moderators. Some of them go, \"You want me to ban someone over something that minor? lol,\" and let it slide.","└ At least the current Moderator is better. Scammers get permanently banned on the spot.","└ Couldn’t innocent people get caught up in that?","└ Then the parties involved have to settle it among themselves.","Thanks to that, the number of scams had decreased considerably.","But they had not disappeared entirely.","Title: This fucking registered user is a scammer. Don’t trust him.","(Photo of a bizarre plant)","I planted this using a seed I won for 1,000 gold.","I thought it was some rare plant, but it wasn’t. Fuck.","└ Ugh ;; what the hell is that? A Nepenthes? Why does the flower have teeth? LMAO.","└ Nepenthes don’t have teeth. What the hell even is that thing?","└ Allfather: That is a plant-type monster called a Deathmeros, which only grows in Mephisto. How did you manage to raise one?","└ Fuck, it was a monster lol.","└ Is the OP still alive?","Fortunately, while Don’t Abandon the Hero held moderator authority, scammers were brought down hard.","Even small-scale scams were not forgiven.","Permanent bans were handed out without exception.","That did not mean people were banned blindly, however.","If the parties involved reached an amicable settlement, forgiveness was possible.","What mattered was whether the offender showed genuine remorse.","After determining the truth, that was the next most important issue.","But those who wanted to scam people still did so, and their methods and scale only grew more vicious.","Registered users never scam?","That was complete bullshit.","There were plenty of people in the world willing to build up a registered account just for one huge payout.","Moreover, the winning bid from an auction was deposited immediately.","That was tied directly to the Gallery system itself, so even the Moderator could not interfere with it.","Because of that, people had no choice but to exercise extreme caution with auctions, especially when bidding.","Most users preferred placing small bids whenever possible and generally avoided large amounts.","Unless the seller was a highly reputable registered user, people rarely spent large sums.","Title: What if the Moderator scams people?","└ It doesn’t happen often, but wasn’t there a scammer Moderator about a hundred years ago?","└ A hundred years ago? lol. Must’ve been a demon or an elf.","└ If I remember correctly, it was an elf. Went around claiming stuff was leaves from the World Tree lol.","└ So what happened? It’s hard to remove a Moderator, isn’t it?","└ People just stopped buying anything the Moderator listed. Then at some point the Moderator changed. Probably died after scamming people in real life too.","└ LMAOOO, deserved.","In that way, fraud was a crime the Gallery could never completely eradicate no matter how much people wanted to.","As a result, Gallery users reacted with extreme disgust whenever they saw the word scam .","Rumors that someone had scammed people—","Especially a registered user?","They would condemn them immediately without caring whether the accusation was true.","Even if the person had been falsely accused through manipulation and fabricated claims.","That was simply how the Gallery worked.","\"Heh heh. Idiots.\"","A middle-aged man muttered to himself.","He had the distinctive appearance and clothing of someone from the Central Plains.","His mustache resembled a rat’s whiskers.","Combined with his narrow, slit-like eyes, it gave him a rather treacherous appearance.","\"They’re really so easy to manipulate.\"","The Gallery floated before his eyes.","The entire list was filled with hostility and condemnation directed at Grylls.","A single small post written by this man had created an enormous ripple.","\"He won’t be able to hold out much longer without agreeing to a settlement.\"","The man was a merchant.","Just one of the countless small and mid-sized merchants scattered across the Central Plains.","But after winning the item Grylls had listed this time, he had stumbled upon a tremendous opportunity.","Rattle.","The merchant looked away from the Gallery and opened a desk drawer.","Inside were various documents and a small ring box.","Click—","He carefully opened the case.","A faint mist carrying a trace of cold air drifted outward.","Inside rested a bead that shone brilliantly with a crimson glow.","It was the item the man had won through the Gallery auction house.","An inner core.","’I never thought it would actually be a real inner core.’","He had confirmed it through several rounds of appraisal.","There was no doubt.","This was an inner core.","It might not be one of those legendary inner cores spoken of in ancient tales, but it was still at least equivalent to a high-grade elixir.","In monetary terms, it could fetch no less than 1,000 silver taels.","’Heh. As long as I don’t reveal that, there’s no way they can know.’","But the merchant was greedy.","Extremely greedy.","He wasn’t satisfied with merely making a profit.","He wanted to manipulate the situation so that he could recover the money he had spent as well.","Even if Heavenly Demon vouched for Grylls, she was regarded as an eccentric even within the Gallery.","Unless she proved that she was the real Heavenly Demon , her testimony held little weight.","’Agitation and fabrication are easy. Clearing your name is hard.’","The merchant knew the Gallery quite well.","That was why he understood its hypocrisy.","People readily believed agitation and fabricated claims, but explanations were much harder to accept.","And even if Grylls tried to explain himself, with the Gallery already this inflamed, his defense would struggle to gain attention.","’If the Moderator tells him to settle, he’ll have no choice but to accept.’","For Grylls in particular, the Gallery was practically his lifeline.","Without it, his chances of surviving in the Forest of Four Seasons would plummet.","Rather than risk making a poor defense and getting permanently banned, he would be better off accepting a settlement.","Looking at it objectively, the merchant was effectively weighing another person’s life against money.","But he did not care.","’I don’t even know what the bastard looks like.’","His ugly true nature was hidden behind anonymity.","He felt no guilt whatsoever.","Perhaps things would have been different if he knew Grylls personally.","But in the Gallery, kindness was nothing more than a weakness.","Of course, there was always the possibility that Grylls could explain himself successfully and turn public opinion around.","Even then, the merchant didn’t care.","’Worst case, I just get permanently banned.’","Was the Gallery really more important than his real life?","To the merchant, money was what mattered most.","It would be a shame to lose access to the Gallery as entertainment, but that was fine.","He could simply use money to entertain himself instead.","The merchant waited happily.","No matter what kind of explanation Grylls offered, he was ready to respond.","[The thing Mr. Grylls gave me really is an inner core.]","\"Hmm?\"","He had been refreshing the Gallery endlessly when a particular title caught his eye.","It wasn’t a post from some ordinary anonymous user.","It had been written by one of the most famous registered users on the Gallery.","SwordMaster.","It wasn’t a post he could casually ignore, so he opened it immediately.","Title: The Thing Mr. Grylls Gave Me Really Is an Inner Core","SwordMaster","(Photo of a golden bead resting on a palm)","Mr. Grylls found another inner core and gave it to me.","This really is an inner core.","└ Wait ;; he found another inner core already?","└ Why are inner cores popping out like everyday meals? lol. That actually makes me trust him less lol.","└ Maybe it’s possible because it’s the Forest of Four Seasons?","└ Heavenly Demon is one thing, but SwordMaster verifying it is different.","└ This one’s golden. Did he catch a golden fish this time?","\"What?\"","There had been another inner core?","The merchant’s eyes widened.","This was completely unexpected.","He hurriedly typed a comment.","└ Ever consider that they coordinated their stories? Why would another inner core suddenly show up out of nowhere? lol.","└ Why would they coordinate? Like with a kiss? Smooch?","└ Oh my. How lewd.","└ There’s no reason for them to coordinate lol. And why would SwordMaster have any reason to lie?","└ Exactly lol. She’s the person who raised the average strength of swordsmen across the continent lol.","└ Heavenly Demon said one-on-one messages are possible, right? She probably threatened her through that.","└ And what would threatening her accomplish? She’d just get kicked out by the Moderator.","└ Why is this bastard’s imagination so pathetic? lol.","└ Looking at the address beside his name, isn’t this the bastard who posted that Grylls was a scammer?","└ Getting nervous? LMAO.","He had jumped in out of panic and only made things worse for himself.","The merchant frowned.","The appearance of a second inner core had been completely outside his calculations.","He felt somewhat anxious, but quickly calmed himself.","Thinking about it again, there was no reason to panic.","’I can just keep insisting that the one I received wasn’t real.’","It seemed the other side intended to fight manipulation with manipulation.","The only difference was that their version happened to contain the truth.","Even if the inner core SwordMaster had received was genuine, that didn’t prove the merchant’s inner core was genuine.","As long as he stubbornly denied everything until the end, the advantage would eventually return to him.","He simply had to exploit the uncertainty all the way through.","[I’ll Explain Everything.]","’There it is.’","Public opinion had just begun splitting roughly down the middle when Grylls finally made a post.","The merchant opened it without delay.","Title: Here’s My Explanation","Wild Grylls","Explanation, my ass.","If you’ve got a problem, reveal your address.","Reveal your address and let someone else check whether it’s an inner core or not. Simple, right?","If it’s an inner core, you’re fucking dead.","If it isn’t, I’ll return all your money.","What kind of half-assed propaganda are you trying to pull, you son of a bitch?","You parasite-looking bastard, sitting there running a scam yourself. Fuck.","SwordMaster already verified one too.","If you still have a problem, make a registered account first, you broke bastard.","└ Holy shit LMAOOOO. That felt good lol.","└ Upvote if this actually made you trust him more lol.","└ Starting with me LMAOOOO.","└ That’s the kind of rage you can only have when you know you’re innocent lololol.","└ Holy shit, I like this guy even more now lol.","└ Every single thing he said is right. Reveal the address and verify it lol.","└ I’m broke and somehow caught a stray bullet...","It wasn’t an explanation post at all.","It was just a wall of profanity.","In any normal place, that would have backfired horribly.","But this was the Gallery.","If anything, a post like this was perfect for gaining favor and credibility.","\"W-What the hell is wrong with this bastard?\"","As far as the merchant knew, Grylls hadn’t even been using the Gallery for very long.","But judging by the way he wrote, he looked like someone who had been active there for years.","After a moment of confusion, the merchant left a comment on the post.","He couldn’t retreat now.","└ I’m the one who received the inner core. Why the hell should I reveal my address? This is ridiculous lol.","└ Oh, the man himself is here.","└ Pathetic lol.","└ Seeing him act like this makes me think he really did scam him.","└ Wild Grylls: If you’re going to play games with someone else’s life, then you should put your own life on the line too, right? The Gallery is literally my lifeline.","└ Not my problem. And I’m telling you, this isn’t an inner core.","└ Wild Grylls: Say that after making a registered account first. Or just reveal your address lol.","└ You reveal yours first.","└ Wild Grylls: I’m in the Forest of Four Seasons, dumbass. Come here if you can.","He was trapped.","Completely trapped.","The merchant’s eyes darted up, down, left, and right before he backed out of the post.","[Anonymous Buyer Who Received the Inner Core, Reveal Your Address.]","[Can’t We Just Go Check It Ourselves?]","[Upvote if Grylls is Based as Hell lol.]","[Upvote if You Want All Scammers to Die lol.]","The moment he returned to the main page, he saw that public opinion had completely reversed.","Most posts were now demanding that the buyer reveal his address if he had nothing to hide.","’Are you insane? Why the hell would I reveal my address and get myself killed?’","Absolutely not.","The moment his location became public, his real-life life would be in danger.","The merchant deleted the post in which he had accused Grylls and logged out of the Gallery.","It seemed he would have to wait until things calmed down.","’What a shame. I could’ve made even more money.’","It was disappointing, but causing any more trouble now would probably make it impossible to reverse public opinion.","It would be better to simply sell the inner core instead.","About ten minutes later, the merchant cautiously logged back into the Gallery.","He had told himself that the Gallery was nothing important.","But in the end, he was just another hardcore Gallery addict.","A piece of culture like a drug—something he wanted to quit but couldn’t.","’Maybe things have calmed down a little?’","With that thought, he entered the Gallery and saw—","[Just Wait Right There. I’m in the Next Town Over LMAO.]","[Heading Over to Taste That Inner Core!]","[So Jealous of the People in the Central Plains.]","[Turns Out That Scammer Bastard Was a Merchant.]","The posts made him feel deeply uneasy.","The merchant immediately sensed something was wrong and opened the trending page.","A merchant who lacked sharp instincts was bound to be weeded out.","And the instant he entered the trending section, one post uploaded by the Moderator caught his eye.","Title: Here’s the Address!","Don’t Abandon the Hero","Mr. Grylls revealed his address, but one person refused to reveal theirs!","So I’ll kindly tell everyone the address myself!","It’s around XXX, Henan Province, Central Plains!","Mr. Grylls also said he’d return the money if it turns out not to be an inner core, so I hope you two can reach an amicable settlement!","\"Uh...\"","Only one thought entered the merchant’s mind when he saw the post.","’I’m fucked.’","He was seriously fucked.","He had never expected the Moderator to reveal his address.","Crash! Bang!","A loud commotion erupted outside.","The merchant’s head snapped upward.","A moment later, his secretary burst through the door in a panic.","\"W-What is all that noise?!\"","\"I-I don’t know either! For now, we need to evacuate—!\"","\"I heard there’s an inner core here!\"","\"We’ll just check it and give it back!\"","The voices drew closer and closer.","The merchant’s face turned deathly pale.","At this point, the Gallery no longer mattered at all.","’You’ve got to be fucking kidding me...!’","It looked like from now on, he would have no choice but to focus entirely on real life."]},{"title":"Chapter 44","paragraphs":["Scammer (5)","\"What a ridiculous bastard.\"","The inner core scam incident had flared up as quickly as gasoline catching fire, then died down just as fast.","With help from Heavenly Demon and SwordMaster, followed by the Moderator delivering the finishing blow, everything ended without too much trouble.","Things might have gotten a bit complicated without their help, but fortunately, most of the registered users had been on my side.","’So even in another world, the Gallery is still the Gallery.’","For the record, posting that \"explanation\" was entirely my own decision.","Instead of calmly explaining myself, I declared war while throwing in plenty of profanity.","No matter how carefully I explained things, the people who wanted to tear into me would do it anyway, so I chose that approach instead.","In the end, I gained favor with the Gallery users and won the battle of public opinion, so there was nothing bad about it.","Though calling it a battle of public opinion felt like an exaggeration, since the fire burned out so quickly.","It was just another ordinary day on the Gallery.","’Heavenly Demon seemed a little flustered, but it ended well.’","Looking at the Gallery now, most people were making a fuss about hunting down the scammer.","The Moderator had even revealed his address, so that bastard’s real life was probably about to become miserable.","Of all things, I never expected the Moderator to actually expose his address.","My guess was that Heavenly Demon had persuaded the Moderator.","From my perspective, this whole issue had practically put my life on the line, while the other side had risked nothing.","She probably thought that was unfair.","’I should send her a thank-you message first.’","No matter what, thanking her was necessary.","I sent her a private message.","[Wild Grylls: Is the address the Moderator gave far from you?]","[Heavenly Demon: Quite far. But this Lady can arrive there quickly.]","That made sense.","I wasn’t being sarcastic either.","I genuinely believed her.","At the very least, she was probably around SwordMaster’s level, if not stronger.","After thanking Heavenly Demon for various things, I asked her something I had been wondering about.","[Wild Grylls: Thanks to you, everything ended pretty smoothly. Seriously, thank you.]","[Heavenly Demon: It was nothing. If this Lady had her way, I would personally go there and rip out his tongue.]","[Wild Grylls: Whoa ;; that’s brutal. Heavenly Demon, you’re from the Central Plains, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: That is correct.]","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, even if you’re a Sub-Moderator, once you use a one-on-one trade, you still can’t trade again for twenty-four hours, right?]","[Heavenly Demon: Correct. Do you perhaps wish to trade frequently with this Lady?]","The way she said wish made it sound like I was desperately hoping for it.","Not that it bothered me.","That was just how she talked, so I let it slide.","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. From now on, I think it’ll be better to get important items verified before selling them. Someone could just take the item and shut their mouth like that bastard did.]","[Heavenly Demon: I understand. Permission granted. This Lady shall persuade the Moderator regarding the trade cooldown.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. Seriously, thank you. I feel like I’m always receiving help from you.]","[Heavenly Demon: Could it possibly outweigh what you did by saving this Lady’s life? If you ever need help, tell me at any time.]","[Wild Grylls: I appreciate the thought, but I’ll pass. I need to develop the strength to stand on my own too.]","As I had mentioned many times before, relying too heavily on others was never good.","The only thing I intended to use Heavenly Demon’s help for was verifying important items.","For most other things, Allfather usually identified them whenever I made a post.","So this was more like insurance.","[Wild Grylls: Then I’ll get going. I’ll message you again sometime.]","[Heavenly Demon: This Lady shall always await your messages. Ah, and the fasting pills can be prepared within a week.]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you.]","[Heavenly Demon: Good. If you ever require strength, contact me without hesitation. This Lady shall help you at any time.]","Was it just my imagination, or could I sense both satisfaction and disappointment in her words?","She seemed like a lonely person, so maybe I should talk to her more often.","Before that, though, I needed to deal with lunch.","Just in case, I turned on the hose.","Unfortunately, water poured out freely without any obstruction.","Which meant no fish was stuck inside.","’Guess I’ll have to settle for a fasting pill.’","It was disappointing, but there was nothing I could do.","Fishing directly in the river was out of the question.","Unless I wiped out every golden frog in the area, fishing there would be suicidal.","I chewed on the bitter fasting pill while thinking about what I should do after lunch.","’The trap... I’ll check it tomorrow. It’s way too soon.’","It was better not to expect too much from the trap.","That left only one thing.","Making a post on the Gallery.","After what had happened today, I wanted to let everyone know how I planned to handle things from now on.","Title: This Is Grylls","Wild Grylls","Hello, everyone.","I’m Wild Grylls, the guy who fell into the Forest of Four Seasons.","Because of some parasite today, I’m planning to have important items verified before listing them from now on.","Especially expensive items. I probably won’t put those on the auction house anymore.","Whenever possible, I’ll prioritize selling them to registered users, and only use the auction house when I don’t have another choice.","The Gallery is honestly terrifying.","For one person, this is literally a matter of life and death, while someone else can ruin that person with a single click.","I rambled on a bit.","Anyway, I’m going to do everything I can to escape this forest.","And if I want to do that, I’ll need the Gallery.","So please cheer me on.","Ah!","And SwordMaster, thank you so much for helping me.","Just keep the inner core.","Three-line summary:","I’ll prioritize trading with registered users from now on.The Gallery is scary, but I’ll keep using it so I can escape.Thank you, SwordMaster.","└ Forget everything else, the three-line summary is the best part lol.","└ Exactly. Just read the bottom lol.","└ Hang in there, Grylls. Just think of it as stepping in shit.","└ Weren’t you one of the guys trashing Grylls earlier?","└ Starlight Princess: I’m glad everything worked out. I was really disappointed because it seemed like there were nothing but awful people here. Mr. Grylls even helps complete strangers.","└ We’ve decided to call people like that suckers.","└ Isn’t that just being kind rather than being a sucker?","└ And didn’t he trade with Starlight Princess before anyway? He’s a good guy as long as you’re actually trading with him.","└ SwordMaster: Wait ;; you’re dumping this on me immediately? I don’t need this.","└ Wild Grylls: You’re going to send it back? Why not just sell it?","└ SwordMaster: I already have plenty of money. Besides, eating an inner core wouldn’t do much for me anyway ;;","└ Wild Grylls: Dun care. Just take ittt.","└ SwordMaster: ;_;","└ What even is this LMAO.","└ It’s not pickpocketing, it’s reverse-pickpocketing lol.","└ He really just said \"dun care\" LMAO.","As expected, SwordMaster looked seriously flustered.","I had no idea why she didn’t want to become healthier.","Starlight Princess had been desperate to improve her health.","The world really was unfair.","’Come to think of it, she used a military expression too. Is she a soldier?’","That would explain why she knew so much about swordsmanship and kept posting sword-training tips.","It made sense.","Since I was already thinking about swordsmanship, this seemed like a good opportunity to thoroughly reread her posts.","I trained diligently while studying SwordMaster’s beginner swordsmanship guide.","’I’m sticking with the sword-and-shield warrior build.’","The owlbear incident and the muscular mushroom incident had both taught me the same thing.","Carrying a shield along with a sword was far safer than relying on a sword alone.","People on the Gallery mocked me by saying I’d die in one hit anyway.","But the whole point of a shield was to block that one hit.","The fist-shaped dent clearly visible on the golden shield was proof enough.","If I had taken that attack directly with my body, my internal organs would have ruptured.","’I can’t really do anything about the proficiency issue, though.’","My swordsmanship itself was destined to hit a wall sooner or later.","The difference between wielding a weapon with one hand and two hands was as vast as heaven and earth.","In my case, I had no choice but to sacrifice technique in exchange for stability.","That was the only way to raise my survival rate significantly.","It wasn’t really a choice.","It was a necessity.","’Isn’t there anyone who’s good with a shield?’","SwordMaster focused almost entirely on swordsmanship, so there was barely any theory related to shields.","At most, it was something like, Block, then hit back.","There wasn’t much that could be done about that.","Well, I was still a complete beginner anyway, so there was no need to rush.","’Let’s see. Time the block properly, then slash immediately?’","I studied SwordMaster’s posts and trained until just before dinner.","Of course, I didn’t expect my skills to improve dramatically after only a few days.","Besides, it had only been a few days since I first picked up a sword and shield.","Getting used to them came first.","\"Hoo...\"","I slowly steadied my breathing.","Beads of sweat formed and rolled down my cheeks.","Even though I was practicing while reading the posts, I still felt uneasy.","It wasn’t that I doubted SwordMaster.","Her posts were said to have raised the average combat strength of the entire continent.","I simply had no idea whether I was doing things correctly.","With nobody beside me to watch and correct me, I couldn’t help feeling a little anxious.","’I heard martial arts are difficult without a teacher.’","Martial arts were techniques humanity had developed for combat.","They were the result of studying how to beat the hell out of an opponent as efficiently as possible.","There was an obvious difference between a punch thrown by an ordinary person and one thrown by a trained fighter.","Some random street brawler beating a professional martial artist?","That was complete bullshit.","That was how enormous the difference was between having martial training and having none.","And progressing properly without a teacher was almost impossible.","So naturally, I couldn’t help wondering whether I was simply swinging my weapons around however I pleased.","’For now, all I can do is study SwordMaster’s posts carefully and complete the goals she laid out.’","SwordMaster’s posts didn’t just contain advice.","They also provided specific goals.","The idea was that once you accomplished one goal, you were ready to move on to the next stage.","Drawing a perfectly straight line with the sword.","Slashing several times without taking a breath.","Thrusting through the inside of a long, hollow cylinder.","There were also some strange goals mixed in that somehow still seemed useful.","’So I should accomplish each goal two or three times over?’","Without a teacher, this was probably the best I could do.","I would simply have to make up for it through effort.","I continued practicing sword-and-shield techniques until evening.","I even visualized scenarios so I could subdue opponents more efficiently.","\"Huaa!\"","I had no idea how long I kept at it.","By the time I stopped, my entire body was drenched in sweat.","This should be enough for today.","I set down the sword and shield and entered the cave.","I planned to rest for a while in the cool interior before eating dinner.","’Come to think of it, I wonder what happened to that scammer. Someone said they lived in the next town over.’","Curious, I immediately logged into the Gallery.","There was nothing quite like the Gallery when it came to relaxing.","As always, the Gallery was a gathering place for idiots.","I figured I should check the trending posts.","The moment I entered, one post with an unusually high number of upvotes caught my eye.","It was related to me.","Naturally, I opened it.","└ Damn, I’m jealous. You guys didn’t kill each other or anything?","└ Nah. The authorities might’ve shown up, so we just settled it with rock-paper-scissors.","└ Rock-paper-scissors LMAOOOO.","└ Don’t underestimate rock-paper-scissors. Visual reaction speed is seriously important in that game lol.","└ You didn’t ask the merchant what he thought?","└ Why the hell would we care about a scammer’s opinion?","└ Guess we should buy everything Grylls lists on the auction house from now on.","└ Fuck. He used to list stuff without going through registered users first. This suddenly sucks.","└ What’s the scammer doing now? He must be furious.","└ What’s he gonna do about it? He ran away immediately LMAO.","└ Serves him right lol.","Title: Yep, This Really Is an Inner Core LMAO","That scammer bastard lived in the town right next to mine, so I stormed over there and ate the inner core.","Some other guys showed up too, but somehow I ended up being the one who ate it and verified it.","I was only at the Second-Rate Realm before, but I immediately broke through to the Peak Realm.","Grylls wasn’t the scammer.","That merchant bastard was.","Stop slandering Grylls from now on.","Looks like things had somehow been resolved.","I probably wouldn’t be mistaken for a scammer again after this.","Even so, I wasn’t going to start listing expensive things on the auction house again right away.","Like I said earlier, I planned to give registered users priority from now on.","I browsed around the Gallery for a while.","By then, my sweat had dried, so I got up.","The sun was starting to set.","It was about time to check the trap.","’It’d be nice if something got caught.’","Not even a full day had passed.","Maybe I was being greedy.","But greed was exactly what could make my dinner more plentiful.","After preparing some basic gear, I headed toward the place where I had set the trap.","I didn’t forget to ask the Tree Sloth to guard the house before leaving.","\"Oh?\"","The moment I reached the trap, I immediately noticed something different.","All the grass I had placed on top of the board was gone.","On top of that, I could faintly sense something moving beneath it.","’Caught something!’","Looks like I’d finally get to eat something greasy again.","Filled with anticipation, I slowly lifted the board.","\"Ta-da~ ta-da-da~ boom-cha-cha~ boom-cha...\"","Clunk—","\"Boom-cha...\"","Inside the trap was a rabbit.","Or rather—","No.","There wasn’t.","Instead, there was something else.","It was large enough to fill the entire pit, with striking pitch-black fur.","And it wasn’t even an ordinary animal.","This thing had eight legs .","Worse still, smaller versions of it were clinging all around its body.","They looked like babies.","Clunk—","I carefully lowered the board again.","Apparently, instead of digging a trap, I had dug myself a spider nest.","’...Should I roast that thing and eat it anyway?’","I immediately gave up on the idea.","If it bit me, I might die."]},{"title":"Chapter 45","paragraphs":["Scammer (6)","Title: Ditched the Spider Trap","Wild Grylls","I just went to check the pit trap, and there was a spider living inside it instead of a rabbit.","It was even covered in pitch-black hair. It was fucking hideous. Just looking at it scared me so much that I left it alone.","From now on, I think I should use snares instead of pit traps.","Heavenly Demon: Keep your spirits up. If things prove difficult, this lady shall send you some meat.","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s okay. I can still hold out for now.","↳ How big was the spider?","↳ Wild Grylls: I think it was at least a meter long? I almost fainted the moment I saw it ;;","↳ Ugh;; What kind of spider is that freaking huge?","↳ Wild Grylls: I was too scared to even take a picture. I think it’d be better to just ignore it lol.","↳ Why not roast that thing and eat it?","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s not like I didn’t think about it, but even if it has babies... I can’t just kill their mother.","↳ Lmaoooo, look at this fucking saint lmaoooo.","↳ Says the guy who killed Wonmo’s mom?","↳ Wild Grylls: Wonmo’s mom was trying to kill me, though ;;","↳ Lmaoooo, fair point.","↳ What would Wonmo think? The person raising him is actually the murderer who killed his mom... and his mom was someone who tried to kill that very person...","↳ Anyone got a novel like that to recommend? Sounds like it’d be fun.","↳ There’s a whole story premise right there lol. I’m off to write it.","↳ Allfather: What did it look like overall?","↳ Wild Grylls: I ran away the moment I saw it, so I’m not really sure either. It was just a spider covered in pitch-black hair.","↳ Allfather: Hmm. That alone makes it difficult to identify. It sounds like some kind of tarantula, so I recommend that you don’t try to catch it.","↳ Wild Grylls: I was already thinking of just burning it with fire.","Since it lived inside a pit, some oil and fire would probably burn it to death in no time.","But I had no intention of going through that much trouble for no reason. I wasn’t even planning on looking at it again.","Just imagine lifting the cover and seeing a whole swarm of grotesque spiders underneath. It wouldn’t be strange to come away traumatized.","’Where the hell did that spider even come from?’","Only a few hours had passed, yet it had already turned the pit trap into its habitat.","It was one of those mysteries of nature that somehow made sense and yet didn’t at the same time.","In the end, I had no choice but to make do with a fasting pill for dinner again.","I could only hope that a fish would be caught by tomorrow morning.","’Would it be better to smoke it instead?’","That wasn’t a bad idea. If I smoked the fish, bugs probably wouldn’t swarm around it as much.","What worried me were wild animals, but honestly, if any were going to come, they probably would have shown up already.","Considering no dangerous beasts had appeared so far, there had to be some reason for it.","’At least finding owlbear droppings gives me some hope...’","Wonmo’s mother, the owlbear, might have come here to scout the area just like I had.","After all, the owlbear had thoroughly chewed up, torn apart, tasted, and enjoyed the Mad Dog’s corpse.","Since the enemy that had once divided up the territory was gone, she might simply have come to check out its former base.","’I guess I have no choice but to keep exploring.’","The Forest of Four Seasons was a place where nothing that happened could be considered strange.","So preparing for every possible contingency wasn’t optional. It was essential.","As the sky gradually darkened, I picked up a few pieces of firewood and headed back inside the cave.","When I entered, Wonmo had woken up and was sitting there blankly.","\"You awake? Want some food?\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","What a cute little guy.","I bought a huge chunk of meat from the auction house.","I wouldn’t have to worry about money for a while. I’d made an enormous amount from selling the inner core.","The funny part was that the scammer hadn’t even gotten to eat the inner core.","Served him right.","’Allfather will need the frog tomorrow, right?’","My plan for tomorrow was simple.","I’d explore in the morning and return before lunchtime.","Then I’d hunt a Golden Poison Frog and trade it with Allfather, and if possible, get a fish trap from the dwarf.","If I could get a fish trap from the dwarf, I wouldn’t have to worry about food anymore.","And since it would be made by a dwarf, there was no reason to doubt its durability.","’The question is whether I should follow the river upstream or downstream...’","There was one of the easiest ways to escape when stranded.","Follow a river downstream.","Since ancient times, civilizations had often begun near rivers.","Even if there wasn’t a country nearby, there should at least be a small village somewhere.","’The problem is that space is all over the place here, so the river might suddenly get cut off halfway.’","Space being all over the place.","It might sound like a strange way to put it, but I wasn’t wrong.","The land on the other side of the river was literally changing in real time, going from snowy mountains to desert and back again.","Last time, it had even changed into an area completely shrouded in fog. I’d been utterly dumbfounded when I saw it.","So if the river ever seemed to come to an unnatural end, I planned to turn back without hesitation.","’Nothing is ever easy.’","I sighed.","That was also why I’d made adaptation my top priority instead of escape.","With space constantly changing, escaping was difficult even if I wanted to.","’At least it’s reassuring that my map is gradually getting bigger.’","I turned my head toward the wall.","A map had been drawn on a large sheet of paper.","With this cave at its center, various points of interest were marked in every direction.","The river where Golden Poison Frogs appeared. The colony of mature Mandrakes. The Golden Mushroom Cave I had recently discovered, and so on.","Since even compasses didn’t work in this place, it wasn’t perfectly reliable, but it was still a huge help.","’Tomorrow, I’ll follow the river downstream.’","As long as I followed the river, I wouldn’t get lost.","Once the sun had completely set, I lit a campfire.","Warmth slowly began spreading through the cave that had been growing increasingly chilly.","\"Nom, nom.\"","Wonmo happily munched away when I gave him the meat.","I stroked his head.","He flinched at first, but soon settled down and continued eating peacefully. It seemed like he had become completely accustomed to my touch.","’It’d be nice if he could just grow out of the cub stage.’","It took several years for an owlbear to reach adulthood. That was what the gallery had told me.","But it didn’t have to be fully grown before it could hunt independently.","If I remembered correctly, I’d heard that it would grow considerably bigger within about a year.","I watched Wonmo happily devouring the neatly butchered raw meat for a while before turning my head.","The Sloth was staring blankly at me with its usual dumb-looking face.","\"You’re fully grown, right?\"","\"...\"","\"Yeah. Thought so.\"","Can’t you tell just by looking?","That was what its expression seemed to be saying.","Of course, that was nothing more than my own guess.","Afterward, I had a simple meal of fasting pills and stepped outside for a moment.","It was better to wash up before going to sleep.","For hygiene.","’Why does this Sloth hate being washed so much?’","Thankfully, I hadn’t shown any symptoms of anything yet, but you never knew.","Until I managed to wash the little bastard, I had no choice but to keep myself as clean as possible.","After quickly washing up, I went back inside the cave.","’Oh. Right. The scabbard.’","The moment I saw the Heavenly Demon’s sword propped up against one side of the cave, I remembered.","I was going to be traveling around a lot from now on, so I couldn’t exactly carry it around like this.","I logged into the gallery and opened a private chat with the Heavenly Demon.","She replied in less than a second.","It caught me a little off guard.","[Wild Grylls: By the way, does the sword you gave me before not have a scabbard?]","[Heavenly Demon: It did. However, the blade was so exceedingly sharp that the scabbard ended up in tatters.]","[Wild Grylls: Hmm. That makes sense.]","In truth, a scabbard might not mean all that much.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword already had a record of cleanly slicing a Mad Dog in half, after all.","But if I just carried it around bare, it would inevitably become inconvenient whenever I was moving.","[Wild Grylls: Heavenly Demon, are you there?]","[Heavenly Demon: Speak.]","[Heavenly Demon: If you desire a scabbard, this lady shall command one of my close aides to prepare it.]","[Wild Grylls: No, that won’t be necessary. Do you happen to know Passing Dwarf?]","[Heavenly Demon: Do you mean that drunken dwarf? I have never spoken with him directly, but I know of him.]","[Wild Grylls: I was thinking of asking him. He seems to be an exceptionally skilled blacksmith.]","[Heavenly Demon: It is not a bad idea, but can you not simply carry the sword as it is?]","[Wild Grylls: I could, but I think I’ll still need a scabbard.]","I was talking about situations where I needed to investigate something or use my hands.","That happened fairly often.","Having one would be better than not having one. That was the conclusion I had reached from living here.","[Heavenly Demon: Your way of life differs from this lady’s, so I shall respect your judgment. But I can assure you that it will not be easy.]","[Wild Grylls: You said it was made from something called Ten-Thousand-Year Cold Iron, right? Is it a particularly good metal?]","[Heavenly Demon: That too, but it was also forged by an outstanding blacksmith.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah.]","So it was a masterpiece among masterpieces.","And the Heavenly Demon had given it to me.","No matter how many times I said I would return it, she adamantly refused.","[Heavenly Demon: If you are thinking of returning it, I forbid it. This lady has already reached a point where she no longer clings to weapons.]","[Wild Grylls: Is there anything you want?]","[Heavenly Demon: If you happen to find another inner core, could you give it to me? It is not for this lady, but for one of my close aides.]","[Wild Grylls: Ah. Of course. Understood. Could you pass along my thanks to them in return?]","[Heavenly Demon: Of course.]","That was where my conversation with the Heavenly Demon ended.","Now only one thing remained.","Asking Passing Dwarf to make me a scabbard.","The problem was, I had no idea whether he would accept.","He was making the fish trap under the pretext that I would provide him with drinking snacks, but a scabbard was another matter entirely.","Unless I found some high-quality mineral, there was a good chance he would refuse.","’In the end, I need something valuable.’","It looked like I would have to expand my exploration range from now on.","The best places to target would be areas where space became chaotically entangled, like on the other side of the river.","’Though finding places like that won’t be easy.’","I would just have to put in the effort.","If I wanted to escape, reckless challenges were sometimes necessary.","I took a picture of the campfire and posted it on the gallery.","Title: Day 4 Complete!","(Photo of the campfire)","Good night, everyone! See you tomorrow!","↳ Heavenly Demon: You have done well.","↳ SwordMaster: Good work today.","↳ Starlight Princess: See you again tomorrow!","↳ Praise the Sun: You had to suffer because of some pathetic bastard.","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Bye-bye! Don’t die! I’ll send you some pants tomorrow!","Receiving encouragement from the fixed users and bullshit from the anonymous users at the same time, I closed the gallery.","Now I planned to practice the internal energy cultivation method for a while before going to sleep.","’It really does feel like my fatigue disappears every time I circulate the cultivation method.’","I was basically forcing myself to sleep, but there was nothing else I could do.","Going outside in the middle of the pitch-black night was practically suicide.","Even if I could technically see ahead, the forest at night was completely different from the forest during the day.","’Then...’","A good idea suddenly occurred to me.","My fatigue disappeared whenever I practiced the internal energy cultivation method?","Then I could simply keep practicing until I became tired again.","I had nothing else to do anyway, so this was probably the best option for me.","’If I keep at it, I’ll get sleepy eventually, right?’","With that simple thought in mind, I began circulating the cultivation method.","The mana inside my body gradually began to circulate, accelerating with each breath as though it were being pumped through me.","’Start slowly from the basics...’","Time was the one thing I had plenty of.","Using that time, I carefully refined the foundation the Heavenly Demon had taught me.","Little by little, I sank into stillness.","By the time Grylls had become completely absorbed in his internal energy cultivation, the gallery was still as active as ever.","The disappearance of a single fixed user was nowhere near enough to bring the gallery to a halt.","However, most of the gallery’s discussion revolved around Grylls.","Title: From now on, I’m buying anything Grylls puts up for auction.","Nothing that bastard sells ever turns out to be bad lol.","At this rate, maybe mithril or something will pop up next instead of an inner core? lol","↳ Mithril, my ass lol. It’s not like mithril is some random rock lying by the roadside.","↳ Then is an inner core just some random marble?","↳ It’s not like it has that huge of an effect.","↳ It’s still an inner core. A second-rate warrior jumped straight to the peak realm after taking one, didn’t he?","↳ I’m telling you, there’s basically no downside to buying one.","↳ The fact that there’s already an entire colony of mature Mandrakes there is broken as hell lol.","↳ Damn it, if it weren’t for that fucking scammer, we could’ve gotten things cheaper.","↳ Seriously, it’s basically because of that bastard that everything has to pass through the fixed users now. Thinking about it is pissing me off again.","Title: Gallery bro is fucked in real time.","My boss told me to somehow build a connection with Grylls.","When I said I didn’t want to, he told me to leave the merchant company if I didn’t like it.","Can’t I do something about this legally? It’s closely connected to my private life ;;","↳ Smart Mind: Do you normally talk shit about your boss?","↳ You don’t?","↳ Smart Mind: I do too. My boss recently told me to reveal my gallery username and I almost got fucked lol.","↳ How’d you get out of it?","↳ Smart Mind: I just bullshitted my way through it. You should ask your boss to reveal his gallery username too. He’ll probably back off then.","↳ Lmao, useful tip.","↳ At this point, I think I’ll believe Grylls no matter what he discovers. What’ll it be next?","↳ I already told you. It’ll definitely be some kind of mineral. I believe it lol.","Title: Honestly, He’s Hard to Trade With","What does Grylls actually need?","Stuff directly related to survival.","He doesn’t really need money.","At this point, it’s basically barter, so isn’t trading with him ridiculously difficult?","Unless you’re willing to hand over some legendary weapon or something.","↳ The fact that threats don’t work on him anymore is huge too. Making even a single trade has gotten ridiculously difficult ;;","↳ Inner cores and elixirs are useless too if he can just eat the ones he finds there lol.","↳ Doesn’t he already have basically all the weapons he needs? What else could he possibly want?","↳ Porn?","↳ Oh.","↳ Ohohoho lol.","↳ That’s what you need, dumbass lmao.","↳ No, seriously, he might actually need it. I’m not even joking.","The gallery burned with what was less an argument and more a prolonged debate for quite some time.","Unlike before, everyone was taking a much more active stance."]},{"title":"Chapter 46","paragraphs":["Lakeside (1)","The internal energy cultivation method really did seem to have a fatigue-recovery effect.","Even if I replaced sleep with cultivation, I would still be full of energy the next day.","Well, it still wasn’t perfect, so mental fatigue was harder to get rid of.","Physical fatigue was manageable enough, but mental fatigue could only really be resolved through sleep.","[XXX has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","[@@@ has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","[I’ll Become a Duke has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","\"What is all this now?\"","The moment I logged into the gallery, countless trade request windows floated before my eyes.","Had something happened again while I was away?","Just in case, I searched my own name, but nothing particularly noteworthy came up.","The only thing was that my credibility had skyrocketed because of yesterday’s incident.","It seemed the fixed users who had previously hesitated because of trust issues were now sending me trade requests because of that.","’Seriously, these people... I keep telling them I’m as fragile as a sunfish.’","Or were they trying to suck me dry to the marrow before I actually ended up dead?","From what I had heard, even a single mature Mandrake was worth an enormous amount.","Apparently, they figured that even if I didn’t have another inner core, one mature Mandrake alone would be enough to make a trade worthwhile.","’At least offer something that would tempt me.’","I searched the names of the fixed users who had sent me trade requests.","Some of their accounts had only been created recently, while others had surprisingly long histories of activity.","Especially this I’ll Become a Duke person.","If I remembered correctly, they had sent me a trade request before too.","I had to admire the persistence, but right now, it was mostly just annoying.","’And they didn’t even make a post.’","I had already said this last time.","If someone offered something I needed, I would be the one to initiate the trade.","Apparently, they had already forgotten.","With no other choice, I made another post.","Title: Let Me Say This Again","Wild Grylls","I woke up to countless handshake requests... no, trade requests.","Like I said before, I have no intention of trading unless you offer something that will actually help me.","If you want to trade, post what you’re offering first.","I’ll look at it and decide.","↳ Heavenly Demon: You are awake. Is there anywhere that feels uncomfortable?","↳ Wild Grylls: I feel way more refreshed when I sleep while practicing the internal energy cultivation method.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Naturally. That is the effect of circulating and regulating your qi. Your foundation is still lacking, but once you reach full mastery, you will remain perfectly well even without sleep.","↳ Wild Grylls: Wow.","↳ Starlight Princess: You’re awake! Is today Day 5?","↳ Wild Grylls: Yeah. If I had my way, I’d escape as soon as possible.","↳ Starlight Princess: There’s a saying that the more urgent you are, the more you should take the long way around. I made another elixir today, so I’ll send you a trade request in a little while!","↳ Wild Grylls: Huh? Didn’t you already give me all the elixirs?","↳ Starlight Princess: This one is for animals. Please use it on Wonmo and the Sloth. One picture of Wonmo is more than enough payment, so please accept it!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you. You’ve been feeling healthy, right?","↳ Starlight Princess: Like I told you before, I feel like I’ve been reborn. My parents are still worried, though.","↳ Wild Grylls: Parents are always like that. Just in case, take your rehabilitation slowly.","↳ Starlight Princess: Thank you. I’ll keep cheering you on from now on. You can do it!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you, haha.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Hey. I finished the fish trap. Hurry up and present this great one with some drinking snacks.","↳ Wild Grylls: Before the snacks, there’s something I want to ask you for.","↳ Passing Dwarf: What is it? I’m not doing it for free.","↳ Wild Grylls: I do have a conscience. I need a scabbard, and I need one that’s seriously durable.","↳ Passing Dwarf: A scabbard? Just buy any old one.","↳ Wild Grylls: The sword the Heavenly Demon gave me is too good. It cuts through wood like tofu.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Ah. There are swords like that sometimes. I’ll send you one to use temporarily along with the fish trap. If you want a proper one, bring me something good in exchange.","↳ Wild Grylls: I’ll trade with Starlight Princess first, then I’ll take yours.","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Hellooo! The pants I mentioned yesterday are ready!","↳ Wild Grylls: Thank you so much. When’s your next match?","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Pretty soon! It’s Boxing Day, so we have one about every three days!","↳ Wild Grylls: I hope you win. Go, Cheonggu!","↳ Princess Cheonggu: Thank youuu!","It really did pay to live kindly.","There were people leaving comments for me first thing in the morning.","Of course, I wasn’t entirely without worries.","If the head moderator saw this, they might think it counted as excessive fraternizing.","The rules specifically said that too much personal bonding was prohibited.","That made things awkward.","’They must know the Heavenly Demon gives me special treatment too.’","Apparently, this much was tolerated.","Or maybe it was because my circumstances were unusual.","[Starlight Princess has requested a trade. Would you like to accept?]","After announcing the start of my day like that, Starlight Princess was the first to send a trade request.","Before accepting, I looked over at Wonmo.","He was still sprawled out asleep.","The funny part was that he had stretched his entire body out flat like a person.","Apparently, when an animal slept like that, it meant it felt safe in its surroundings.","That gave me a strange feeling.","[Starlight Princess has registered trade items.]","[Starlight Princess: I put in one animal-use elixir and another gift too!]","[Wild Grylls: Huh? Another gift?]","[Starlight Princess: I think you’ll like it. So, where’s the picture?]","[Wild Grylls: (Photo of Wonmo sleeping sprawled out flat) Is this enough?]","[Starlight Princess: He’s so cute! How can he even sleep like that?]","[Wild Grylls: I thought it was amazing too.]","[Starlight Princess: I hope you continue to stay safe! You can do it!]","That was the end of my conversation with Starlight Princess.","I checked the items she had given me.","She had called it an animal-use elixir, but judging by the way it glowed golden, it looked like an ordinary elixir no matter how I looked at it.","I wasn’t even sure whether animal-specific elixirs existed in the first place.","I decided to just think of it as a gift.","And then there was the other item.","The thing she had confidently claimed I would like was actually a little surprising.","’Cake?’","A slice of cake sat on top of a glass plate decorated with an elegant design.","Soft-looking sponge cake covered in whipped cream, with a small strawberry perched on top.","She had even thoughtfully included a fork to make it easier to eat.","I swallowed and picked it up.","\"Damn...\"","The moment I put a small bite of cake into my mouth, an exclamation escaped me.","The sweetness spread throughout my entire mouth.","The distinctive sugary taste stimulated my tongue.","I sprinkled salt on fish whenever I ate it, so I hadn’t forgotten what saltiness tasted like.","But it had been a long time since I’d tasted something so sweet it practically made my tongue tingle.","’She really knows what people like.’","I set the cake aside for a moment and logged back into the gallery.","There were still fixed users I needed to trade with.","The next person to send me a request after Starlight Princess was Passing Dwarf.","He seemed like the kind of person who would handle exactly what needed to be done and move on.","[Passing Dwarf has registered trade items.]","[Passing Dwarf: Put in the fish trap and a temporary scabbard. You know how to install the trap, right?]","[Wild Grylls: Yeah. I’m thinking of widening the spot where I inserted the hose.]","[Passing Dwarf: That should work. Deal with the scabbard however you want, but make sure you give me snacks for my drinks. Got it?]","[Wild Grylls: Do you like sashimi?]","[Passing Dwarf: My mouth’s already watering.]","[Wild Grylls: But I’m not very good at slicing sashimi lol.]","[Passing Dwarf: You fucking bastard.]","[Wild Grylls: Anyway, I’ll do my best. Thanks for the stuff.]","Once the trade was complete, I checked the items I had received from the dwarf.","’Why the hell is this fish trap so huge?’","The fish trap was enormous.","It was almost as big as my entire body.","I was a little taken aback, but that might actually be better.","Considering the size of the fish I had caught so far, it was probably about right.","’Installing this is going to take a while. I’ll do it after I’m done exploring.’","I decided to postpone setting up the fish trap.","It felt like I would waste the whole morning just installing it.","The next thing to check was the scabbard.","The temporary scabbard the dwarf had mentioned was inside the fish trap.","’It looks like an ordinary scabbard.’","It was a plain black scabbard, roughly the same size as the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","I picked up the Heavenly Demon’s sword from where it rested against the wall and slid it inside.","Shhk—click!","The sword went in smoothly without catching anywhere.","He had said it was only temporary, but I was more than satisfied.","It even came with a belt, so it looked useful in all sorts of situations.","’That dwarf is surprisingly nice, too.’","I chuckled and contacted the next person I had to trade with.","Next up was Princess Cheonggu.","[Wild Grylls: Go, Cheonggu! Don’t get too discouraged even if the slump lasts a while! No one stays on top forever!]","[Princess Cheonggu: Thank youuu! I’ll give you another special uniform too!]","[Wild Grylls: Whose is it this time?]","[Princess Cheonggu: It belonged to a legendary midfielder named Sun! He’s unusual because he’s from the Central Plains!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you! Can’t I watch Cheonggu’s matches through the gallery?]","[Princess Cheonggu: You have to pay for broadcast magic, so only the highlights will get uploaded!]","[Wild Grylls: That’s too bad. I wanted to watch one of your matches.]","[Princess Cheonggu: I’d love to let you watch too, but broadcasts probably won’t work in the Forest of Four Seasons. But why do you want to watch?]","[Wild Grylls: I feel like I’m always the one receiving things. I wanted to show you that I’m genuinely cheering for you.]","[Princess Cheonggu: Kyaaah...! What a wonderful attitude! Such an admirable mindset! I really hope you escape soon!]","[Wild Grylls: Thank you. If I find anything good, I’ll send it to you right away.]","What kind of item would Princess Cheonggu like?","That was something worth thinking about.","For now, I checked what she had sent me.","Just as she had said, there were long pants and a uniform shirt.","The pants were made of the same highly elastic material as the uniform.","And she had sent not one pair, but two.","I smiled in satisfaction and put them on.","They definitely felt different right away.","’I could probably live in just these.’","It reminded me of the days when I used to lounge around at home wearing nothing but tracksuits.","I tossed the pants I had been wearing until now into a corner of the cave.","From now on, those would be my emergency pair.","’Now that all the trades are done, time for the cake... Huh?’","My excitement at the thought of enjoying the cake lasted only a moment.","I had definitely eaten only one bite.","So why was the plate completely empty?","I blinked at the incomprehensible sight and looked around.","Wonmo was still sleeping soundly on the mat.","That only left the Sloth...","\"...\"","\"...Hey.\"","At my voice, the Sloth tilted its head.","The sheer shamelessness of its behavior made anger rise inside me.","\"Maybe wipe the cream off your mouth first?\"","\"...\"","Only then did the bastard start feeling around its mouth.","There wasn’t just a tiny speck of whipped cream there.","A huge glob was smeared all over it.","The Sloth looked at the cream now stuck to its claw, then very slowly brought it to its mouth.","\"...\"","\"Munch, munch.\"","Was there anything in the world more infuriating than this bastard?","The worst part was that I had no way to beat it in a fight.","In the end, there was only one thing I could do.","\"You little bastard!!!\"","Roar at it at the top of my lungs.","It seemed to work surprisingly well, because the Sloth covered its ears.","\"Kkyuak?!\"","Ah.","Right.","Wonmo was here too.","When Wonmo jolted awake in fright, I immediately felt terrible.","’This is all the Sloth’s fault.’","Thinking that to myself, I gently soothed Wonmo.","Fortunately, Wonmo just looked bewildered and didn’t seem to understand what had happened.","\"Wonmo. Want breakfast?\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","Even if he had understood, the whole incident probably would have ended the moment I offered him breakfast anyway.","I gave Wonmo some meat and stepped outside.","When I opened the hose, water came pouring out beautifully.","Unfortunately, it didn’t look like any fish had been caught.","’Guess I should get ready.’","I had another fasting pill for breakfast.","Maybe because I had tasted something sweet just moments ago, the bitterness seemed especially strong today.","’Should I ask her for another one?’","That felt far too shameless, so I gave up on the idea.","The day had only just started, yet I already felt drained.","’Please let me find somewhere with plenty of food.’","That was my small wish.","I sighed and finished preparing.","The Sloth might be annoying as hell, but it was the only one capable of protecting Wonmo while I was gone.","I decided to think of the cake as payment for all the time it had spent guarding the cave.","That made me feel a little better.","\"Hey, Sloth.\"","When I called out, it tilted its head.","\"I’m heading out. Guard the house properly while I’m gone, got it? You’ve got to earn the price of that cake.\"","\"...\"","Flap. Flap.","The Sloth lazily waved its arms as if to say it understood.","I chuckled at the response and finished the rest of my preparations.","At my waist were the scabbard containing the Heavenly Demon’s sword and a small bag.","In my left hand, I carried the Golden Shield in case I was suddenly attacked.","I kept my right hand free so I could maintain my balance if something unexpected happened.","’And I should circulate the cultivation method before leaving.’","Once I had properly circulated the internal energy cultivation method, all that remained was to depart.","With a tense heart, I started walking toward the river.","Once I reached it, I planned to follow the flow downstream.","’Hopefully I can find some clue that’ll help me escape.’","Whether the world understood my hopes or not...","Or perhaps some god of this world was deliberately screwing with me.","\"Ah, fuck.\"","After following the river downstream, I couldn’t help swearing at the environment spread out before me.","It wasn’t like the other side of the river, where space itself changed in real time.","This place was clearly connected to the river.","The problem was simply that the environment itself was ridiculous enough to make me curse.","\"Is this the ocean or a lake?\"","An immense lake stretched out before my eyes."]},{"title":"Chapter 47","paragraphs":["Lakeside (2)","I didn’t run into any dangerous animals while following the river downstream.","Normally, all kinds of animals would come to a river, but whether it was because the current was too strong or because of the Golden Poison Frogs, I didn’t see any.","That didn’t mean I encountered no animals at all, though.","Every now and then, I came across smaller creatures.","Title: This Is a Lizard, Right?","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a fucking huge lizard)","What species even is this? The size is ridiculous.","Of course, it only counted as a small animal by Forest of Four Seasons standards.","The lizard bolted the moment it saw me.","I was glad it avoided a fight, but I was still curious, so I asked the gallery.","↳ Heavenly Demon: What an enormous lizard. Why not catch it and eat it?","↳ Wild Grylls: Not a bad idea, but it ran away.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. It must have instinctively sensed your strength and fled.","↳ Wild Grylls: I don’t think that’s it lol ;;","↳ Allfather: Judging by its appearance, it is an iguana. It seems to have grown much larger because it lives in the Forest of Four Seasons.","↳ Wild Grylls: Is it a herbivore?","↳ Allfather: Yes. It is herbivorous, so you do not need to be wary of it. Still, given its size, you should remain careful.","↳ Wild Grylls: What does it taste like?","↳ Allfather: Probably like ordinary meat.","Damn.","I should’ve caught it instead of taking a picture.","But no matter how quickly you regret something, regret always comes too late.","I put my disappointment behind me and continued walking.","Trickle, trickle—","As I followed the river downstream, the current gradually slowed.","The river also grew considerably wider, so this was probably somewhere near the lower reaches.","There were no sudden distortions in space or drastic changes in the surrounding environment along the way.","Bzzzzzzzz—","The real problem was the gigantic mosquitoes flying around.","At first, I wondered if my sense of perspective was off.","But when one threatened me with its sharp proboscis, I finally realized it was a monster.","Clang!","I barely managed to block it with my shield in my panic.","The Golden Shield had been dented by the Muscle Mushroom, but it was still plenty useful.","The instant I blocked the attack, I drew the sword hanging from the left side of my waist.","Slash!","Then I swung it at the mosquito, which was about the size of my head.","Given how huge it was, the mosquito was cleanly sliced in two.","Watching its severed body twitch on the ground left me dumbfounded.","’Did I fall into some dark fantasy world?’","I shook my head.","It was probably better for my sanity to believe that this forest itself was just abnormal.","But there was one thing that worried me.","If mosquitoes were this huge...","What about bees?","How large would bees be when they formed enormous colonies?","Just imagining a swarm of bees the size of my head attacking me was horrifying.","’Thank god there isn’t a beehive near the cave.’","Thinking that, I walked past the mosquito corpse.","A few steps later, I suddenly heard a rustling sound from behind me.","Rustle! Rustle!","Since I had no choice but to react sensitively even to the smallest noise, I spun around in alarm.","I didn’t forget to raise my shield as I turned.","Scurry!","The iguana I had seen earlier was running away with the mosquito corpse in its mouth.","I stared blankly at the creature disappearing at high speed.","This place was impossible to get used to.","’There are probably things even weirder than that.’","Just how many more bizarre creatures would I end up seeing?","I could hardly wait.","I continued silently downstream.","This time, I kept my sword drawn so I could counterattack immediately.","I had no idea how long I continued following the river.","It felt like I had been walking for around an hour, but nothing particularly noteworthy appeared.","Splash!","The only thing that stood out was the fish.","Every now and then, an enormous fish would leap out of the water.","Maybe it was just my imagination, but they looked much bigger than the ones I had caught before.","Since this was downstream rather than the fast-flowing upper reaches, there were probably far more fish living here.","’It wouldn’t be bad to install the fish trap here—’","SPLASH!","I had just started thinking that when something burst out of the lower reaches of the river.","It was a little too small to call a whale, but far too large to call an ordinary fish.","Its entire body was pitch black, and just looking at it gave off an intimidating pressure.","SPLASH!","Its enormous body plunged back into the river, sending a column of water spraying into the air.","I could only stare at the scene in a daze.","’Do whales even live in rivers?’","The urge to turn around and go straight back to the cave rapidly grew.","I could probably deal with most beasts at this point, but there was absolutely no way I could take that thing down.","Still, I wanted to at least see where the river ended.","I couldn’t give up yet.","So I continued downstream in tense silence.","And when I finally reached the end—","\"Ah, fuck.\"","The words came from the very bottom of my heart.","It was less a curse and more an exhausted sigh caused by sheer disbelief.","\"Is this the ocean or a lake?\"","A vast lake stretched out at the end of the river.","Though calling it a lake felt a little strange.","Despite its incredible size, the water was extremely shallow.","The water was so clear that I could see the bottom perfectly.","’It’s practically stamping \"You’re not getting out\" right on my forehead.’","I could feel my spirit slowly breaking.","I sighed and made a post on the gallery.","I was feeling gloomy, so I wanted to post something and see how people reacted.","Title: Found a Pretty Lake","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a vast lake)","I followed the river downstream and found a lake.","Pretty, right?","How the hell am I supposed to escape now? Hahahaha.","↳ Heavenly Demon: What beautiful scenery. It makes this lady wish to take out a small boat and recite a poem.","↳ Wild Grylls: Teacher?","↳ Heavenly Demon: Is there some problem?","↳ SwordMaster: Read the room. Do you think Grylls has the luxury of taking a boat out there?","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm. That is true. This lady apologizes. I must have been momentarily captivated by the beautiful scenery.","↳ Wild Grylls: No, it’s fine. I guess that can happen...","↳ It really is pretty though lol.","↳ I’m gonna paint this.","↳ There are a lot of rocks in the lake.","↳ Looks really shallow too.","↳ Hey, what’s that faint thing way over there? Looks fucking huge.","↳ Isn’t it just a rock?","↳ Grylls, it’s hot out. Take a refreshing dive lol.","↳ Wild Grylls: It’s too shallow. If I dive in, I’ll crack my head open ;;","↳ It’s a lake but it’s shallow? Is it even a lake?","↳ Wild Grylls: I don’t know either. It’s way too wide to call a pond, but too shallow to feel like a proper lake.","↳ Normally something like that would be a wetland.","↳ Wild Grylls: There are too many pebbles for it to be a swamp.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Are your shoes any good? If you’re going to cross that place, you’ll definitely need boots.","↳ Wild Grylls: That’s what I’m worried about. I’d ask you, but I feel like I’ve already asked you for too much, so I’m thinking of asking someone else.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. I’m not that confident when it comes to shoes either. I don’t know about my own kind, but there are plenty of humans better at making them than me.","↳ Wild Grylls: Guess I’ll need to get myself a pair of proper shoes later.","Come to think of it, while I’d been focused on getting clothes, I had completely neglected getting proper shoes.","For someone like me who had to walk long distances, footwear was extremely important.","I wanted to ask the dwarf, but like I’d said myself, I felt like I was relying on him too much, so I decided against it.","The dwarf had also advised me that when it came to shoes, I was better off asking someone else.","’I thought I’d never wear combat boots again unless I was called up for reserve training.’","And now here I was, looking for combat boots.","Life really was unpredictable.","Still, more important than combat boots themselves right now was waterproofing.","If I wore soaked shoes for too long, I could get sick, and my feet would swell up from being waterlogged.","’There’s no rubber in the auction house... Should I just put up with it for today?’","I debated whether to endure it for just one day or turn back right now.","Going back would have been perfectly reasonable, but something about it felt unsatisfying.","I hadn’t even reached a true dead end yet.","I couldn’t give up that quickly.","’Yeah. If necessary, I can always build a boat. Let’s investigate a little more.’","If the water got even slightly deeper, I planned to turn back immediately.","I nodded to myself and moved around only where the water was as shallow as possible.","It felt like I was circling around the edge of the lake, but even this was yielding results.","’If I keep going like this, I might actually get around the lake.’","It seemed possible to reach the opposite side without needing a boat at all.","Of course, there were puddles here and there, so there was no avoiding getting my shoes wet.","I continued forward while carefully watching my surroundings.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk. Guruk.\"","\"Hm?\"","I heard a strange sound.","It came from directly ahead.","When I looked, I saw several large rocks clustered together.","It didn’t take me long to realize they weren’t rocks at all.","’Crabs? Why are there crabs here?’","They were crabs.","Crabs walking sideways.","And they were far bigger than lobsters.","Each one was roughly the size of my upper body.","The crabs twitched their stalk-like eyes and moved their claws around.","I cautiously approached.","Even when I got closer, they showed no sign of wariness and remained busy working their claws.","’Fish?’","It was fish.","The crabs were eating fish carcasses.","I vaguely remembered hearing that crabs sometimes acted as scavengers.","But that still didn’t explain why there were fish corpses here in the first place.","’The water’s so shallow that swimming should be difficult. Were they just unlucky?’","First, I should take a picture and figure out what species they were.","I photographed the crabs enjoying their meal and uploaded it to the gallery.","Title: Anyone Know What Species This Is?","(Photo of crabs happily eating)","I was walking around the lakeside and found these crabs eating.","They’re about the size of my torso.","Anyone know what species they are?","↳ Do crabs even live in lakes?","↳ Yeah. Those things are adaptation experts. As long as there’s water, they’ll live anywhere.","↳ I heard crab tastes amazing.","↳ They look ordinary enough. You could probably roast them and eat them.","↳ Allfather: They are edible Gophers Crabs. Normally, they are only about the size of a fist.","↳ Wild Grylls: No parasites or anything inside them?","↳ Allfather: There is nothing that cannot be killed by fire.","So as long as I didn’t eat them raw, I’d be fine.","Excellent.","I could take one of these things back with me on the way home.","’Their shells shouldn’t be too hard, right?’","Just in case, I stabbed one with the Heavenly Demon’s sword.","Crunch!","With a satisfying sound, the blade pierced straight through its shell.","The crab, now skewered through the back, flailed its claws and legs.","The other crabs didn’t care whether one of their own was dying.","They remained completely focused on eating the fish.","’As expected of the Heavenly Demon’s sword. I should never doubt it.’","I flicked the sword and shook the crab off.","The crab landed upside down and trembled for a while.","I felt a little sorry for it.","For about a moment.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk. Guruk.\"","More crabs slowly started approaching from elsewhere.","They were heading toward the crab whose shell I had pierced.","Curious about what they were doing, I stood still and watched.","Soon, the crabs surrounded their wounded companion and raised their enormous claws.","Crunch! Crunch!","They slammed their claws down onto the overturned crab.","Its shell shattered further with every strike.","Eventually, the crab even stopped trembling.","It was dead.","And the dead crab became a meal for its own kind.","\"...\"","Nature really was brutal.","I shook my head and kept moving.","Countless crabs inhabited the lakeside.","Almost all of them looked exactly the same.","Normally, a lake would support all sorts of life, so I couldn’t help finding this a little strange.","’How did these crabs take over the entire lakeside?’","Their claws were powerful, sure, but ultimately, these things were weak creatures.","While pondering that question, I suddenly came face-to-face with a large boulder.","It was much bigger than I was.","A random boulder jutting up here felt a little strange, but I could simply go around it.","\"Guruk.\"","\"Hm?\"","Except the boulder made a strange noise.","The exact same sound the crabs had been making earlier.","Confused, I stared at the boulder.","Rumble—","With a faint vibration, several legs suddenly protruded from underneath it.","Then two gigantic claws emerged from either side.","The boulder had already been huge.","Now it looked even bigger than before.","So large that I had to tilt my head all the way back just to look at it.","\"Guruk. Gururuk.\"","Its stalk-like eyes stared directly at me.","I couldn’t help slowly backing away.","The boulder—","No.","The gigantic crab stared at me for a while before rapidly scuttling its legs.","Thankfully, it wasn’t coming toward me.","Instead, it turned its whole body around.","It seemed to have lost interest.","’...Wait a second.’","Don’t crabs move sideways?","The moment that thought crossed my mind—","Whoosh!","A gigantic claw came crashing down toward my head.","As I said before, crabs were creatures that acted as scavengers.","BOOM!","\"Ugh!\"","In other words—","They were omnivores."]},{"title":"Chapter 48","paragraphs":["Lakeside (3)","The giant crab brought its claw crashing down.","I narrowly dodged the attack.","Its movements were large and surprisingly sluggish, so avoiding it wasn’t particularly difficult.","But the vibration that shook the ground when the claw struck...","That was no joke.","’F-First, the mana.’","I steadied my startled heart and circulated my mana.","A refreshing stimulation spread through my muscles.","Since I practiced whenever I had spare time, I was able to respond quickly.","\"Gururuk.\"","In the meantime, the giant crab raised its claw again.","For something that huge, it was surprisingly agile.","The moment I saw it, I moved both legs.","Trying to block that thing head-on was a bad idea.","Thud!","\"Ugh?!\"","But the unfamiliar terrain caused me to make a mistake.","Something caught my foot as I stepped backward.","For a moment, the world seemed to spin, and then the sky filled my vision.","Even as my body tipped backward, I reacted instinctively.","\"Urgh...!\"","A considerable impact traveled through my back.","Still, it was bearable.","Just before falling, I curled my body to minimize the impact.","It was the breakfall technique SwordMaster had explained in his post.","Rumble—","Even while I staggered and fell, the giant crab didn’t stop.","Maybe because it had so many legs, it closed the distance quickly despite its enormous body.","Slip—","I tried to force myself back up, but my footing slipped slightly.","In that brief moment, the giant crab slowly raised its claw, casting a shadow over my head.","Getting up in time would be difficult.","Acting on instinct, I raised my shield.","Praying that it would protect me, I drew out as much mana as possible from within my body.","BANG!","A sound like metal colliding with metal rang out.","Then came the impact transmitted through the shield.","My arm went numb, but I could endure it.","It was weaker than the Muscle Mushroom.","Before another blow could come, I hurriedly rolled away.","BOOM!","While I was rolling, the giant crab slammed its claw down again.","Feeling the vibration travel through my entire body, I silently got back to my feet.","The giant crab adjusted its direction by moving its countless legs and approached me again.","’Forget about blocking and counterattacking.’","If I kept blocking with the shield, my arm would give out first.","I had to exploit an opening somehow, but finding one wasn’t easy.","’Its attacks are simple, but the problem is that they’re fast.’","I kept moving my legs while thinking.","That was another tip SwordMaster had taught me.","Think while moving.","That way, you wouldn’t give your opponent an opening and could steer the situation in your favor.","BOOM!","And SwordMaster’s advice worked.","The giant crab missed.","Its claw smashed into the spot where I had been standing just moments earlier.","Now.","This was my chance.","I poured mana into the sword and swung with all my strength.","The blade shimmered like a heat haze before slicing straight through the claw.","Slash!","The pincer portion of the claw fell cleanly to the ground.","It wasn’t a particularly major hit.","I had only cut off the pincer itself, not the entire claw.","With something this huge, that couldn’t be helped.","It wasn’t like I could slice the whole thing apart with a single sword strike like someone else could.","’Just cut it apart piece by piece.’","But this was enough.","If I kept dismantling it little by little, I could kill it.","Whoosh!","The giant crab swung the claw that had lost its pincer.","The limb itself was still basically a gigantic blunt weapon, so it remained more than threatening enough.","I kept my legs moving while searching for a weakness.","’Wait a second. This thing...’","As I watched, I noticed one weakness.","A very serious one.","Crabs, by nature, could only walk sideways.","Even after growing enormous, that trait hadn’t changed.","In other words, its effective attack range was extremely limited.","No matter how wildly it swung its claws, there was still a clear limit.","’And especially... it turns incredibly slowly.’","While the giant crab flailed its claws, I quickly moved around and took its rear.","It tried desperately to turn around, but it was far too slow.","It couldn’t hit me with its claws either.","Such was the unfortunate fate of a creature designed only to move sideways.","Slash!","While it struggled to turn, I cut through its legs instead of attacking its claws.","Two legs were severed in a single strike.","It was the combined result of the Heavenly Demon’s sword and aura.","Thud!","Having lost two legs at once, the giant crab lost its balance.","One side of its body tilted awkwardly, making it difficult for the creature to stabilize itself.","My goal was to completely destroy its mobility.","Since the bastard turned as slowly as a turtle, I exploited that weakness thoroughly.","Slash! Slash!","Instead of standing in front of it, I continually stayed behind it and cut off its legs.","Once I severed two legs from each side, it completely lost even its ability to turn.","After that, cutting off the remaining legs was easy.","Slash!","Finally, I completely severed its prized claws as well.","The creature collapsed onto the ground with nothing but its torso remaining.","Maybe because it was a crustacean, its body was still twitching even after all of its limbs had been cut off.","Crunch!","I climbed onto the giant crab’s shell and drove my sword down.","I stabbed between its eyes, directly into the center of the upper shell.","Krrrrrk!","Then, as though pulling a lever, I dragged the sword downward.","The Heavenly Demon’s sword could split even solid wood like tofu, so the blade slid through surprisingly easily.","Eventually, the sword reached the very bottom of the shell.","I gripped it tightly and pulled with all my strength.","Slash!","Since all of its legs were already gone, the body didn’t split dramatically in half.","But I was satisfied simply seeing it stop moving entirely.","I lightly shook the bits of innards from the blade.","\"Haaah!\"","I exhaled heavily.","My heart was pounding violently from the adrenaline surging through me.","If I hadn’t figured out its weakness, that fight would have been much harder.","No.","Forget \"harder.\"","One wrong move and I could have lost my life.","Strangely enough, it was exhilarating.","\"Gururuk.\"","\"Guruk.\"","Before I knew it, the smaller crabs had gathered around and begun picking apart the giant crab’s corpse.","Even the giant ones seemed to faithfully fulfill their role as scavengers.","I watched them for a moment, then made a post on the gallery.","Title: Hunted a Giant Crab","(Photo of an enormous giant crab corpse)","A giant crab way bigger than a person jumped me at the lakeside ;; It used its claws like blunt weapons.","Luckily, it turned ridiculously slowly, so it wasn’t too hard to kill.","What the hell kind of creature is this ;;","I only posted the message and didn’t bother checking the comments.","Getting back to the cave was more urgent.","Not only had I fallen on my ass, I had rolled all over the ground.","If I left myself like this, the smell would be bad enough, but I could also get sick.","’Next time I come here, I need to bring proper shoes.’","This incident had made me realize just how important footwear was.","Especially when I slipped earlier.","For a second, I genuinely felt like my life flashed before my eyes.","I caught my breath again and started walking back.","’The fish corpse is... over there.’","I hadn’t forgotten the route back.","There were fish carcasses and partially eaten crab corpses along the way, after all.","Just thinking about walking back through all this filth made me feel sick, but I had no choice but to endure it.","\"Gururuk. Guruk.\"","\"...\"","When I spotted a crab along the way, I gently picked it up.","Then I bought a backpack from the auction house.","Not one of those small bags worn at the waist, but a proper backpack worn on the back.","’I can’t resist.’","The moment I got back to the cave, I was eating this.","I needed to give some to Wonmo and the Sloth too, so I stuffed two more crabs inside.","I considered taking one for the dwarf as well, but unfortunately, I wouldn’t be able to trade with him until tomorrow.","Crab was perfect as a drinking snack, so I planned to come back tomorrow anyway.","’Allfather said they’re edible, so they should taste good, right?’","I wasn’t particularly worried about parasites.","They probably wouldn’t kill each other and spoil inside the bag either.","So far, I had only seen them eat members of their own species after they were already dead.","Rrrrrumble.","Just as I was happily imagining the meal ahead, the ground began to shake.","Nothing good had ever happened to me when the earth started trembling.","The instant that thought crossed my mind, I hurriedly looked around.","Splash! Splash!","One giant crab after another began emerging from deeper inside the lake.","Each was about the same size as the one I had just fought, or slightly larger.","There were at least five of them.","I stared at the sight in disbelief.","I had barely managed to kill one, and now five had appeared.","If I had stayed there any longer, I would have been in serious danger.","’Is this really a lake? Not an ocean?’","There was no salty sea smell, so it definitely seemed to be a lake.","I moved carefully, worried that the giant crabs might notice me.","Thankfully, not one of them so much as glanced in my direction before I reached the mouth of the river.","They were too busy picking up and eating the corpse of their own kind with their claws.","’They really are slaves to their instincts.’","Judging by their behavior, corpses seemed to be their first priority.","\"Scavenger\" really was the perfect word for them.","I slowly backed away, then turned around.","It was about time I headed back to the cave.","RUMBLEEEEE!","That was when I felt a tremor on an entirely different level from before.","It was far stronger than the shaking caused by the giant crabs.","For a moment, I wondered if this was an actual earthquake.","Then a tremendous noise came from the lake, impossible to ignore.","ROOOOAR!","Water surged high into the air before crashing back down.","At the sound, I turned toward the lake.","The moment I looked back, I froze.","I had thought the giant crabs were already absurdly huge.","Apparently, something even worse lived in this lake.","’...Fuck. What the hell is that?’","If the giant crabs were the size of large trucks, the crab I was looking at now was the size of a building.","In terms of height alone, it was comparable to a small apartment building.","It was so absurdly huge that perspective itself felt meaningless.","Could I even call that thing a crab?","It was basically a walking building.","Title: Find What’s Wrong With This Video","Wild Grylls","(Video of a building-sized crab with giant crabs beside it)","What’s wrong with this picture?","Take a guess!","↳ Heavenly Demon: Hmm? Why does the sky look so small?","↳ Wild Grylls: Right? I wonder why it looks so small.","↳ SwordMaster: I’ve never seen a crab that huge in my life. Does something like that actually exist?","↳ Wild Grylls: Good eye. I’m looking at it myself and still can’t believe it.","↳ Heavenly Demon: Looking again, it truly is enormous. It has piqued this lady’s interest.","↳ Wild Grylls: Want to come over? We can catch it and steam it.","↳ Heavenly Demon: My close aides are desperately stopping me, so I cannot go. My apologies.","↳ Allfather: Oh ;; Ooooh;; Fuck, what is that?","↳ Wild Grylls: Lmaoooo, I don’t know either. First time seeing one too, Allfather?","↳ Allfather: The species is definitely a Gophers Crab... but I do not know whether that should be considered an entirely new species at this point. What on earth is that?","↳ Wild Grylls: I’m amazed too.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Looks like a mountain is walking around ;; Hey, can I ask you for something?","↳ Wild Grylls: You want a crab as drinking snacks? Trade cooldown means I can give you one tomorrow.","↳ Passing Dwarf: Yeah. And while you’re at it, give me that huge one.","↳ Wild Grylls: You fucking lunatic lmao.","↳ Whoa ;; I don’t even know what to say. Isn’t that thing basically a spirit beast at this point?","↳ Yeah, I bet there’s an inner core inside that shell.","↳ If it’s that huge, you could definitely call it a spirit beast lol.","↳ You planning to hunt it?","↳ Wild Grylls: You do it ;; There’s absolutely no way I can kill that thing. I already struggled just taking down one giant crab.","↳ Nothing in this world is impossible. You just have to try.","↳ If you kill that thing, the gallery’s gonna explode lmao.","↳ Wild Grylls: I’ll try if someone comes and helps me lol.","↳ (No replies)","↳ Wild Grylls: Answer me, you bastards.","I kept walking while looking at the gallery.","I wanted to get back as quickly as possible.","The dampness made my entire body feel heavier.","’Why is the back of my neck so itchy, though?’","Maybe because the tension had finally eased, my senses had become more sensitive.","And because of that, I could clearly feel every itchy spot.","Unable to stand it, I reached behind my neck with my right hand and scratched.","Squish.","Then I felt something soft.","The instant I felt it, I froze.","My instincts were screaming at me.","Whatever this squishy thing was, it was absolutely nothing good.","Worse yet, even when I flicked it with my fingers, it refused to come off.","I swallowed hard and grabbed it.","Then I pulled with force, tearing it off.","It stretched like jelly.","Pop!","Something detached from the back of my neck with a strange sound and a sharp sting.","It was big enough that I had to grip it in my hand.","And it was slippery.","Very slowly, I brought my right hand around in front of my face.","I needed to see what I was holding.","Wriggle. Wriggle.","Something red and slime-like squirmed in my hand—","No.","It was a grotesque brown leech.","An obviously disgusting one.","And it was enormous.","\"KYAAAAAAAAAAAH!!!\"","I wanted to get out of here as fast as possible."]},{"title":"Chapter 49","paragraphs":["Shoes (1)","The leech incident caused quite a commotion, so I hurriedly made a post on the Gallery.","I asked what I was supposed to do after getting bitten by a leech. I explained that I’d accidentally grabbed the one on the back of my neck and ripped it off.","The ever-so-kind veteran adventurers promptly told me what to do.","_What the fuck? Why would you remove a leech like that? Are you fucking desperate to get an infection?","└ Wild Grylls) I didn’t know anything about leeches...","_Whatever. If you have a potion, apply it to the bite. You might’ve gotten infected with a parasite, so take a deworming medicine too.","└ Wild Grylls) It’s not a potion, it’s an elixir. Is that okay? Does an elixir disinfect wounds too? I know it regenerates them.","_Just fucking put it on ;; Why are you asking such a weird question ;;","└ An elixir is literally a higher-tier item than a potion kekeke","└ Feels like watching a rich newbie kekeke","└ The fact that he ripped a leech off with his bare hand proves he’s got guts, at least.","_The teeth might still be stuck in there, so remove those before applying it.","Only after receiving their affectionate(?) advice was I able to treat the wound properly.","Normally, I would’ve needed to take deworming medicine too, but apparently the elixir alone was enough.","Next time I came here, I’d probably have to wrap something around my neck.","’Why the hell am I going through all this?’","I sighed. Still, it was some consolation that the trip hadn’t been completely fruitless.","Once I got back to the cave, I’d have to dry my damp clothes and shoes, make something to eat, and take care of a bunch of other things.","I’d wanted to install the fish trap too if possible, but with my shoes soaked through, that seemed unlikely.","’I absolutely need to get some shoes.’","The shoes I was currently wearing were sneakers. The same sneakers I’d been wearing before I fell into this place.","You might wonder why I’d been wearing shoes when I’d been at home before ending up here.","I didn’t really know either. The last thing I remembered was drinking.","’I don’t know if I should call that lucky or not.’","Still, at least I had sneakers.","I trudged along with the unpleasant dampness clinging to my feet.","The farther back I went, the narrower the river became and the stronger the current grew.","It wasn’t until I reached the section of the river where I’d installed the hose that it finally sank in that I was almost back.","’I really did go pretty far this time.’","I accessed the Gallery to check the time.","It was currently 12:20 p.m. It hadn’t taken as long as I’d expected.","I’d spent more time walking along the river than actually exploring the lakeshore.","’Wonmo’s probably going to be demanding food.’","Or maybe he’d gotten anxious because I’d disappeared.","The thought made me quicken my pace slightly.","Eventually, I arrived at the cave that had now begun to feel strangely familiar, and there I saw it with my own two eyes.","\"Kuu...\"","\"...\"","Wonmo was sprawled out asleep with his belly completely exposed.","He was even scratching his own stomach with his claws.","Apparently, he couldn’t care less whether I disappeared or not. He was perfectly content taking a nap.","\"...What, punk? What are you looking at?\"","The tree sloth was just sitting there stupidly too.","A sigh escaped me as I realized I’d worried for nothing.","Anyway, I still had to clean everything up.","I took off the backpack containing the crabs.","When I looked inside, the crabs were barely moving, just twitching their legs every now and then.","’First, let’s get a fire going.’","I had a mountain of things to do.","I stripped off the clothes that had partially dried.","Laundry could wait. Washing the grime off my body came first.","I also made sure to inspect myself thoroughly in case there were any other leeches hiding somewhere I couldn’t see.","’So there really was only one on my neck.’","It was honestly impressive that the thing had managed to latch onto me during the brief instant when I’d fallen.","I turned on the water from the hose and thoroughly washed every part of my body.","Soap was a must.","Following the advice of Gallery users—or, more specifically, the adventurers—I used unscented soap.","\"Phew.\"","After giving myself a quick wash, I used a towel to remove as much moisture as possible.","Then I approached the campfire I’d prepared beforehand and thoroughly dried myself by the heat.","’First, I should buy some shoes I can use temporarily.’","My sneakers were completely soaked, so I needed something to wear until they dried.","I entered the Auction House and bought a decent pair of leather shoes.","I didn’t bother worrying about the size. I was basically going to use them as slippers, so as long as they roughly fit, they’d be fine.","\"I’ll leave the laundry here, and now that I’m dry, I should change into something else.\"","I still had plenty of the uniforms Princess Cheonggu had given me.","The problem was that the pants were shorts.","Long pants were essential for exploring, so I planned to wash and dry mine today.","I also had plenty of charcoal for doing laundry. The veteran adventurers had told me I absolutely had to collect it.","’Now, all that’s left is...’","Grilling the crabs.","I took the crabs out of the backpack and put them into the metal container.","Then I filled it with water to keep them as fresh as possible.","Between the fish and now the crabs, that metal container was proving incredibly useful.","All that remained was asking the Gallery how to prepare them.","Apparently, I just had to pry open the mouth(?) or something, but I wasn’t exactly sure what that meant.","Title) Anyone know how to prepare crabs?","(Photo of crabs inside a metal container)","I’m planning to grill them instead of steaming them. Anyone know how I should prepare them?","└ Passing Dwarf) Wow. Those look fucking delicious. Can’t you give me just one?","└ Wild Grylls) I told you I’ll give you one tomorrow. We can’t even trade today anyway.","_ Passing Dwarf) Ha, seriously ;; If I’d known this would happen, I wouldn’t have used up my trade.","└ Wild Grylls) Just wait one day. You seriously can’t even manage that?","└ Passing Dwarf) Yeah yeah. The hand holding my beer is literally trembling right now.","└ Wild Grylls) Dude, those are symptoms of alcoholism. Lay off the booze.","└ Telling a dwarf to stop drinking kekeke","_ Might as well tell him to quit drugs lol","└ Wait, don’t tell me you actually do drugs?","└└└ It was just an example kekeke","└ This bastard’s suspicious, isn’t he?","└ Preparing crabs is actually pretty easy. There’s a part around the mouth that’s slightly open, right? Stick a knife in there and twist it to drain the blood and water.","_ If you’re grilling it instead of steaming it, don’t put it back in the water afterward. Just grill it as is.","└ Don’t worry about the body burning all the way through.","└ It’s best to drain as much moisture as possible. Otherwise, you might end up boiling it instead of grilling it.","So I had to twist open the mouth first.","I nodded and pulled out my dagger.","Then I took one of the crabs from the metal container and turned it around, examining it from different angles.","Just as the Gallery had explained, its mouth had a structure that opened toward both sides.","’If I stick the dagger in here and twist it sideways...’","Riiip!","With a satisfyingly sharp sound, the crab’s mouth was forcibly pried open.","The moment its mouth opened, I flipped it upside down.","Clear blood mixed with water dripped steadily from its mouth.","\"Kkyuu.\"","\"Ah. You’re awake?\"","While I was preparing the crab, Wonmo woke up from his nap.","The tree sloth also began inching closer, apparently asking for food.","\"Just wait a little. I’ll give you something really delicious.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","\"...\"","Wonmo’s eyes sparkled at the mention of something delicious.","The tree sloth didn’t show much of a reaction, but it was probably looking forward to it too.","’Now that all the blood’s drained...’","Straight onto the campfire!","The crab was so large that it more than covered the entire campfire.","I added more firewood so that not only the body but the legs would cook evenly.","At the same time, I didn’t want it completely charred, so I positioned it slightly away from the flames.","’They said to wait twenty to thirty minutes, right?’","In the meantime, I entered the Auction House and searched for shoes.","The shoes I wanted had to meet some fairly demanding requirements.","Since I’d be walking for long periods, they needed ventilation and comfort, as well as waterproofing.","Most importantly, they had to be durable. The moment I injured my feet, my chances of survival would plummet.","Like I’d told the dwarf, what I basically wanted was something close to combat boots, with \"durability\" as the foundation.","’Thinking about combat boots reminds me of the military.’","Back when I’d just become a recruit, I thought I was going to die during my first march.","Actually, the march itself wasn’t the worst part. The real mess came afterward.","Everyone else had blisters or patches of skin rubbed raw, but I was perfectly fine.","To me, combat boots were just slightly heavy shoes. I’d never found them particularly uncomfortable.","’No matter how much I search, there’s nothing.’","Even the expensive shoes didn’t meet the conditions I wanted.","Besides, most of those expensive ones were related to sports. Soccer cleats, basketball shoes, things like that.","In the end, it seemed I’d have no choice but to make a post.","Before doing that, I bought a measuring tape from the Auction House.","Since I wasn’t familiar with the units of measurement here, I planned to put the tape next to my foot for reference.","Title) Commissioning a Pair of Shoes","Wild Grylls","(Photo of a measuring tape placed beside my foot)","(Photo of a measuring tape placed over my foot)","Just like the title says, I’m looking for shoes suitable for exploration. However, the requirements are pretty demanding.","(Most important) They must be durable. An injury to my feet would be disastrous, so this is the highest priority. Waterproofing. I’ll often be in situations where my shoes could get wet. Ventilation and comfort. Honestly, comfort matters more than ventilation. I may have to travel through high-altitude areas. Slip resistance. I nearly died after slipping while trying to stand up. Preferably made of leather. Same reason as number three.","If someone can make shoes that roughly meet the conditions above, I’ll give them a mature Mandrake as payment.","I’d also appreciate it if you could upload videos and photos demonstrating their performance. I hope plenty of people see this.","_ Heavenly Demon) May this lady participate as well?","└ Wild Grylls) Huh? Why would you, Heavenly Demon?","└ Heavenly Demon) This lady is bored.","└ Wild Grylls) Teacher;;;","└ SwordMaster) If you’re bored, want to have a debate on swordsmanship with me? I’ll wipe the floor with you.","_ Heavenly Demon) Foolish one. Very well. This lady shall message you.","└ Passing Dwarf) Can I have someone else make these for me? I know a guy who’s damn good at making armor.","└ Wild Grylls) Yeah, do whatever you want. But do you even need a mature Mandrake? Planning to make more booze with it?","└ Passing Dwarf) That’s part of it, but my friend keeps pestering me for a drink. Wouldn’t it be easier to just give him one?","└ Wild Grylls) Do whatever you want. I’m fine as long as I get the shoes.","└ Passing Dwarf) Okay. By when do you need them?","└ Wild Grylls) The sooner, the better. I think I’ll need at least two pairs for now?","└ Passing Dwarf) Okay, got it.","└ I’llBeADuke) Are you truly offering a mature Mandrake as the prize?","└ Wild Grylls) I don’t really have anything else to offer. Or would you rather have some of the crab I’m grilling right now?","└ I’llBeADuke) No. I will procure them for you as quickly as possible.","└ Wild Grylls) Thank you.","_ I’llBeADuke) If I acquire shoes that outperform the winning pair, would you be willing to accept them as well?","└ Wild Grylls) Honestly, this is basically a trade anyway, so as long as I like them, I don’t mind.","└ I’llBeADuke) Understood.","There was something strangely refined about the way he spoke.","Even his username sounded ambitious.","You could call this an event of sorts, but in reality, it was closer to a trade. A straightforward exchange where both sides gave and received something.","It wasn’t as though I planned to stop exploring just because I didn’t have proper shoes.","There were still plenty of places left to investigate.","Still, I intended to avoid unnecessary exploration whenever possible.","After nearly dying yesterday, I needed to be careful.","Crackle! Pop!","\"Is it done... Hot, hot, hot, hot!\"","The moment I pressed it with my finger to check whether it was cooked, an incredible wave of heat hit me.","Thankfully, I pulled my hand away immediately. Otherwise, I would’ve burned myself.","I put on my gloves and lifted out the deliciously cooked crab.","It was supposedly an ordinary crab, yet it was even larger than a king crab. There had to be plenty of meat inside.","’Let’s start with a leg.’","One of the tastiest parts—the legs.","I cut through one of the crab’s legs with my knife.","Crack!","The crab leg came away with a satisfyingly crisp sound.","I cut along the side with my knife and slowly pried the shell apart, sending wisps of steam curling into the air.","\"Wow.\"","Just look at that plump meat.","My mouth watered just from looking at it.","Now, how would it taste?","I’d sprinkled some salt on it, but hadn’t added any other seasoning.","Since it was still hot enough to burn me, I blew on it several times.","\"Munch. Munch. Haa.\"","This was seriously delicious.","Even with nothing but salt, it was packed with savory flavor.","There wasn’t even a hint of fishiness, making it incredibly easy to eat.","For a moment, all the crabs I’d seen scattered around the lake flashed through my mind.","Crack!","\"Kiya!\"","Of course. You couldn’t eat crab without taking off the top shell.","I exclaimed in delight when I removed the shell and saw the innards underneath.","For a moment, I regretted grilling it instead of steaming it.","Then I immediately started eating.","’I thought the innards would taste fishy, but they don’t?’","Even the innards were delicious.","There wasn’t a single disappointing part of it. Everything tasted fantastic.","After finishing the innards, I tore off another leg.","This one was for Wonmo.","\"Wonmo. I’ll give you more later, so eat this for now.\"","\"Kkyuu!\"","\"Speedy, want some too?\"","The tree sloth gestured for me to hand some over.","I cut off a leg and gave it to him too.","The tree sloth accepted it without the slightest suspicion, only to immediately start flailing its arms.","Even its normally drowsy eyes shot wide open. It must have been seriously startled.","’Yeah. It’s pretty damn hot.’","I was wearing gloves, but the tree sloth had grabbed it barehanded.","Considering how much the bastard had messed with me until now, this much revenge was nothing.","I snickered.","Smack!","Except the bastard threw it straight back at me.","It hit me square in the face.","A collaboration between a sloth’s powerful shoulder and a scorching-hot crab leg.","Right after the pain came an intense blast of heat.","\"Aaaaaagh!\"","Just you wait, you bastard.","**","While Grylls was happily enjoying his crab feast—","\"I assume you saw the post uploaded to the Gallery as well.\"","\"You mean...\"","\"Bring the craftsman here immediately. As quickly as possible.\"","\"Yes!\"","A subtle undercurrent began to ripple through the world."]},{"title":"Chapter 50","paragraphs":["Shoes (2)","While Grylls was busy bickering with the tree sloth, the Gallery erupted into another commotion because of the post he’d uploaded.","Normally, whenever he needed something, he maintained the stance that he’d simply trade for it.","Money meant nothing to him, and even noble titles were useless in his life in the wilderness.","Pressure didn’t work on him either.","Title) What kind of item would Grylls like?","I really want to get my hands on one mature Mandrake.","└ Just draw him some porn. Honestly, I don’t think there’s anything else.","└ Stop fucking around and answer seriously.","└ I am being fucking serious. What else is there to relieve yourself with in the Forest of Four Seasons? kekeke","└ Tofu?","└ You crazy bastard kekekekeke","That was why the users—especially the named users who wanted to establish a connection with him—had been racking their brains.","What kind of item could they give Grylls that he would actually like?","And how could they use that item to trade for a mature Mandrake?","Continuous trade was difficult because of how unstable his situation was.","But a one-time trade was enough.","Even succeeding just once could bring an enormous profit.","Title) Grylls obviously has the advantage","Where the hell are you guys going to get a mature Mandrake? kekeke Right now, Grylls is literally the only one who can get one kekeke","└ If it were just a regular Mandrake, maybe, but this is a mature Mandrake kekeke","└ Ask people where they’re supposed to get one and they’ll all shut up.","└ That’s exactly why everyone’s asking him for one. Just one of those could seriously turn your whole life around.","└ Is a mature Mandrake really that good?","└ I heard you can make one top-grade elixir with a single mature Mandrake.","└ And Grylls can dig them up like they’re fucking radishes. They’re growing right near him.","A mature Mandrake was one of those medicinal herbs that couldn’t be bought even if you had the money.","Its sheer rarity alone was enough to prove its value.","Trust wasn’t an issue either.","After the inner core incident, the users’ trust in Grylls had skyrocketed.","As long as they could arrange a proper \"trade,\" they could obtain an incredibly rare item.","And if that trade also helped them establish a connection with Grylls?","Grylls benefited because he could receive all sorts of support, while the other party profited by obtaining rare goods.","It was a win-win situation.","More than anything else, Grylls possessed one particular advantage that belonged to him alone.","Rarity.","Title) Grylls’s commission is seriously demanding","The shoes Grylls wants are insanely demanding. I don’t think anyone short of a really skilled craftsman could make them.","But if you’re going to trade something like that for a mature Mandrake, wouldn’t it be better to just sell the shoes for money? kekeke","└ Gallery money can’t be converted into real-world cash. That’s why barter is actually better.","└ Ah, right. You can’t cash it out, can you?","└ Yeah. If you could, the world economy would be completely fucked kekeke","└ Maybe not completely fucked, but it’d definitely get shaken up badly. The high fees are part of why things are still under control.","└ Wouldn’t it be better to just make the shoes and sell them? Why bother exchanging them specifically for a Mandrake?","└ Exactly. Aren’t people sucking up to Grylls a little too much?","└ Try finding a mature Mandrake yourself. Then I’ll admit you’re right.","└ That’s not what I’m saying. From a craftsman’s perspective, it’d be better to sell the shoes for money. They don’t need a mature Mandrake.","└ Wouldn’t someone higher up just pay the craftsman to make them? Besides, a lot of craftsmen use the Gallery too, so this could turn into a pride contest between them.","└ Then who’s famous among shoemakers?","└ As always, dwarves are famous for it, but demons have the upper hand these days.","└ Why?","└ Because they’ve been making sports shoes lol","_ Yeah, that immediately makes sense kekekekeke","More importantly, money charged into the Gallery couldn’t be converted back into real cash.","If cashing it out had been possible, crimes such as money laundering would surely have become rampant.","Because of this structural limitation, physical goods carried even greater value.","The rarity of an item one might never see even once in a lifetime.","The advantage of barter rather than monetary payment.","And finally, trust.","Those three conditions combined to create a strange atmosphere throughout the Gallery.","It wasn’t just the named users who usually liked showing off their possessions.","Even people who wanted to establish ties with Grylls began to move.","\"I assume you’ve seen the Gallery as well.\"","\"Yes, Your Highness. Do you mean...\"","\"If this had been a matter of continuous supply, I would have ignored it. But this time, that man called Grylls personally posted a commission. And he has offered a mature Mandrake as the reward.\"","Arnold, the blond-haired, blue-eyed Crown Prince, explained the situation in a solemn voice.","At his explanation, Count Gorgon, a graying middle-aged man, broke into a radiant smile.","The man’s intentions were so obvious that Arnold chuckled inwardly, though he showed nothing on his face.","He couldn’t afford to stand by and watch this matter unfold either.","That was how important it was.","\"A long-term contract with this man Grylls would be unstable. But a one-time contract like this is extremely important. Especially since he was the one who made the request first.\"","\"Yes, Your Highness. Then I shall immediately gather the craftsmen—\"","\"Listen until I finish speaking. We mustn’t be too hasty.\"","Arnold stopped Count Gorgon from displaying excessive enthusiasm.","Count Gorgon was highly capable and otherwise perfectly satisfactory.","His only problem was that he tended to overdo things.","’That just means he’s equally ambitious.’","From the perspective of someone in power like Arnold, the most trustworthy kind of subordinate wasn’t someone utterly incorruptible.","A moderately corrupt, moderately righteous ambitious man.","That was just about perfect.","As long as you satisfied the ambition they desired, they would offer their loyalty in return.","That made them easy to trust.","’Of course, if he ever crosses the line beyond that, I’ll have his head...’","He hadn’t reached that point yet.","Count Gorgon was certainly ambitious, but he wasn’t excessively greedy.","\"If we pressure the craftsmen unnecessarily, we may only provoke resistance. Can a work produced by crushing someone under authority truly be called a proper masterpiece?\"","\"Would that not constitute disrespect toward the royal family?\"","\"Then we must make sure they never commit such an offense in the first place. We are the ones who need them, after all. And the same will be true elsewhere.\"","Anyone could use the Gallery as long as they met the necessary conditions.","There was no telling when shoes meeting Grylls’s desired quality might suddenly appear.","That was why Arnold had been thinking.","How could they break through this fierce competition?","\"Moreover, if we are too late, it may become difficult to trade with him at all. If that happens, all our effort will have been wasted.\"","\"Then shouldn’t we move even faster—\"","\"We will take a different approach. One that will force him to trade with us even if he has already obtained another pair of shoes.\"","\"Pardon?\"","Count Gorgon’s eyes widened.","He couldn’t understand what Arnold meant at all.","But Arnold wasn’t finished.","He willingly revealed the plan he’d devised.","\"Wild Grylls. What he wants is something close to an all-purpose pair of shoes. In particular, he emphasized durability above everything else.\"","\"Y-Yes. That’s correct. If he injures his feet, he could end up unable to go anywhere at all.\"","\"More than anything, what matters most to that man is trust. And in a matter like this, he will be even more cautious.\"","\"Now that you mention it, I heard rumors that he was recently scammed.\"","’I know.’","Arnold answered silently.","It wasn’t so much that Grylls had been scammed as that he’d nearly been scammed.","At the same time, it had been the incident that raised people’s trust in him.","Afterward, Grylls had become even more cautious. He’d gone so far as to declare that any item that looked expensive would only be listed on the Auction House after being verified by a named user.","Would someone like that readily agree to a trade?","Arnold was certain he wouldn’t.","Unlike the named users who had helped Grylls out of pure goodwill, trust would be crucial in this matter.","\"First, contact a craftsman. Preferably one under contract with the military. If we end up being too late, we can simply use the shoes as military boots.\"","\"Understood.\"","\"I hope for a favorable result. Once the shoes are finished, do not contact him directly. Report to me first.\"","\"I will live up to your expectations!\"","Count Gorgon strode out with a vigorous shout.","Arnold stared at the spot where he’d disappeared for a moment, then raised his head.","The Gallery window, which he’d finally started getting used to, floated before his eyes.","’Grylls will definitely check the posts of any named user he trades with. If their posting history is completely empty, he’ll obviously become suspicious.’","Arnold had spent some time analyzing Grylls’s personality.","It could be summed up like this:","He was the type who couldn’t feel satisfied unless he gave something back whenever he received something.","Kindness for kindness.","Malice for malice.","Perhaps because his personality had so few rough edges, quite a few named users had become friendly with him.","He occasionally bickered with Passing Dwarf, but they were more like bad friends who genuinely got along.","’At the very least, this man isn’t someone who deceives others. He’ll definitely hand over the mature Mandrake.’","Of course, that assumed Grylls actually received the shoes he wanted.","Someone could create a named account, hand him some bizarre pair of shoes, and then simply disappear.","It wasn’t as though there were no scammers among named users.","Human malice could be frightening.","’I’d prefer to step in personally, but...’","Arnold checked his own username again.","[AbsolutezZoneArnoldTheBest]","It was the sort of username that made him feel like coughing up blood every time he saw it.","Arnold squeezed his eyes shut.","He’d rather jump off a building than actually participate under such an embarrassing username.","Thankfully, he had the fiercely ambitious Count Gorgon available.","’We have to show him trust first if we want him to repay us with trust.’","Arnold’s plan was simple.","Instead of exchanging the items immediately during the trade, his side would send the shoes first.","Then they would receive the mature Mandrake the following day, thereby earning Grylls’s goodwill and trust.","’And to do that...’","Arnold glanced around.","The Gallery was invisible to everyone else, but he still couldn’t help feeling self-conscious.","Among all his private activities, browsing the Gallery was easily the most shameful.","After confirming that no one was around, he began writing a post.","Only moments ago, he’d thought he’d rather jump off a building than participate.","But sometimes, surviving in this world required the courage to jump.","\"...\"","Title) Grylls, please read this post.","AbsolutezZoneArnoldTheBest","There are plenty of people on the Gallery who create named accounts and still scam others.","So I recommend receiving the item from the other party first, then giving them the mature Mandrake the following day.","I believe Grylls has always conducted himself openly and honestly, so there should be nothing for you to feel guilty about.","└ Who the hell are you to tell him what to do?","└ Isn’t this bastard just trying to sabotage the competition?","└ Damn, you people live suspicious lives kekeke","_ It’s not really being suspicious. I’ve been scammed exactly like that before ;.;","└ Yeah, there are surprisingly a lot of people like that. Plenty of cases happen the other way around too.","└ Honestly, that is the standard way to do it. Makes you feel safer.","_ What if Grylls is the one who scams them?","└ Wild Grylls) If I can’t trade the next day, that means I’m already fucking dead, doesn’t it? Anyway, thanks for the advice.","Arnold smiled in satisfaction after reading Grylls’s reply.","As expected, the other party had to be the one to demonstrate trust first.","’One dwarf named user is bound to make a pair, so I should assume there’ll only be one or two mature Mandrakes left after that.’","That was the safest assumption.","Humans might have a higher potential ceiling, but it was difficult to surpass a dwarf craftsman.","Arnold sincerely hoped Count Gorgon would return with good results.","If he did, both their lives would become much easier from then on.","[Posting one fucking idiot for everyone to see.]","Arnold happened to be browsing the Gallery when a title suddenly caught his eye.","The title itself was striking enough, but the author was Grylls.","Since he was publicly exposing someone, apparently somebody had tried to scam him.","Curious about what kind of fool had managed to earn Grylls’s distrust, Arnold opened the post.","Title) Posting one fucking idiot for everyone to see.","Wild Grylls","[Wild Grylls: If you beat me at word-chain, I’ll give you two. I’ll start. Sewing machine.]","[xxx: Machine teeth.]","[Wild Grylls: Teeth your mom.]","What kind of bastard is this? I’m just exposing him.","[Wild Grylls: Have you already prepared the shoes?]","[xxx: Yes. But you’ll have to give me two mature Mandrakes.]","[Wild Grylls: ? What kind of bullshit is that?]","[xxx: There are two shoes, aren’t there? You give me one Mandrake, and I’ll give you one shoe. Keep that in mind.]","└ Is this guy mentally disabled? kekekekekeke","└ Look at Grylls setting up \"sewing machine\" just to bait him into answering \"machine teeth\" kekekekeke","└ This bastard seriously has no conscience kekekekeke","└ xxx: Delete this post. If you don’t, I’ll retaliate.","└ Wild Grylls: Retaliate how? You gonna come to the Forest of Four Seasons? I’d appreciate that. You can dig up your own mature Mandrake.","└ Kekekekeke, he really was an idiot.","└ Threatening Grylls doesn’t work, bro kekeke","└ Looking at stuff like this, his situation almost seems convenient kekeke","\"Heh. Hehehe.\"","Arnold chuckled.","The world truly was vast, and there was no shortage of idiots.","That was one of the things he’d learned from using the Gallery.","’I should browse just a little longer before getting back to work.’","Arnold slowly continued lurking through the Gallery.","And then—","\"Aaaaaaaaaagh!\"","Just like Grylls before him, he peered into an abyss that should never have been seen."]},{"title":"Chapter 51","paragraphs":["Shoes (3)","Shoes are extremely important, as they make up one of the key parts of clothing among the three basic necessities of life: food, clothing, and shelter.","Humans, in particular, are bipedal creatures, making shoes essential.","Walking around barefoot could result in stepping on something sharp or slipping and falling.","Since it could put someone in dangerous situations, the importance of shoes could hardly be overstated.","That was why early footwear had to be sturdy and safe above all else.","Otherwise, there would have been no point in wearing it.","Since humans walked on two legs and shoes were subjected to some of the roughest treatment, the requirements for them to properly fulfill their purpose were demanding.","Title) Bought soccer cleats lol","(Photo of soccer cleats with two stripes)","Saved up my allowance and bought some soccer cleats hehe. How are they?","└ Those are knockoffs, aren’t they? Why are there only two stripes?","└ Yeah. There should be three stripes.","└ Ah, shit. I just noticed. Why are there only two stripes?","└ Dude proudly showed off his fakes lolololol","└ How much did you pay for them?","└ 300,000 yura...;;","└ Damn lol","Driven by such public demand, clothing-related industries centered around sports also developed.","Title) Do beastkin wear shoes?","Do they walk around barefoot or something?","└ Suspiciously) We wear shoes too. What, do you think beastkin are savages? ;;","└ You aren’t savages?","└ Suspiciously) Sounds like you’re the savage, judging by how rude you are. Want me to crack your skull open?","└ Scary bastard ;;;","However, as time passed and technology advanced, shoes also began functioning as a type of fashion item.","Not only did people sometimes sacrifice performance in pursuit of design, they also began wearing footwear originally made for performance simply because it looked cool.","The emergence of sports was the starting point.","Ordinary people valued convenience more than performance, so they did not pay much attention to the actual capabilities of athletic shoes.","At most, perhaps they cared about slip resistance?","└ lololol","└ Of course beastkin wear shoes. It’s not like they don’t have houses just because they’re beastkin.","└ Then how do they get shoes that fit? Their feet seem to vary like crazy in size.","└ Custom-made, obviously. Just look at rabbit beastkin. Their feet alone are freaking long.","The existence of beastkin, in particular, had a major influence on the development of footwear.","There were combat boots worn by soldiers, and then there were safety boots worn by adventurers who traveled through harsh terrain all across the world.","The varieties of shoes were practically endless depending on who wore them and what profession they belonged to.","\"So you’re telling me to make this?\"","\"Don’t if you don’t want to.\"","\"Hey, now. Look at this dwarf. Who said I didn’t want to?\"","Short stature.","Two muscular arms that looked disproportionately powerful for his size.","Broad shoulders.","And a thick brown beard that could practically be called his trademark.","The brown-bearded dwarf grabbed the shoulder of the dwarf who had turned away.","The dwarf whose shoulder had been caught turned back around.","His eyes were slightly glazed with alcohol, and his nose was as red as a strawberry.","Anyone could tell at a glance that he was drunk.","His red beard went particularly well with his alcohol-flushed face.","This dwarf’s name was Gareth.","He was the sort of drunken dwarf commonly found in Mountain, the land of the dwarves.","\"You got any ideas?\"","\"Of course I do. But what do I get out of making this?\"","Gareth’s friend, Wagner, raised a perfectly reasonable question.","The two had been through thick and thin together for many years, so they usually granted each other’s requests without much fuss.","However, the item Gareth had asked Wagner to make was enough to make him question the request before even agreeing to it.","\"I don’t care that you suddenly showed up asking me to make a pair of high-performance shoes. But anyone can see these are shoes for a human, aren’t they?\"","Wagner asked as he waved the sheet of paper in his hand.","It was the paper Gareth had handed him containing the requirements for this particular order.","Gareth glanced at the paper and nodded.","\"That’s right.\"","\"Where the hell did you get a request like this?\"","\"From the Gallery.\"","\"That damn Gallery.\"","Wagner frowned at Gareth’s answer.","Wagner knew about the Gallery as well, but he had never logged into it even once in his entire life.","He simply saw no reason to.","People overwhelmed by their lives in the real world had no spare time to log into the Gallery.","And entertainment wasn’t an issue either, because to dwarves, invention itself was entertainment.","In that sense, Gareth was more than eccentric enough to deserve the label.","A dwarf who had become completely obsessed with the Gallery instead of inventing things.","Even so, his natural talent ensured that he never had trouble making a living.","\"What the hell did they offer you to make you accept an order like this?\"","\"Ah. I probably shouldn’t tell you.\"","\"Why not?\"","\"Because it has something to do with booze. Hic.\"","\"Booze?\"","The moment Wagner heard that it involved alcohol, his eyes widened with interest.","Dwarves and alcohol.","The two were inseparable.","It went beyond mere personal preference and was considered a racial characteristic. Dwarves were famous for having dedicated alcohol refrigerators or even breweries in their homes.","They had gone so far as to invent not only locomotives but even airships to ensure the smooth transportation of alcohol.","That alone said everything there was to say.","Mountain, the land of the dwarves, was a place where mechanical civilization had developed all because of alcohol.","\"Yeah. Booze. You remember that infused liquor I gave you last time, right?\"","\"Of course I do. That bright red stuff. It was damn good. Slurp.\"","As soon as Gareth brought up the infused liquor, Wagner unconsciously swallowed his saliva.","He still remembered it vividly.","Gareth had somehow obtained a red herb and brought over a batch of liquor he’d made by infusing it.","Normally, drinking alcohol made intoxication set in and brought on drowsiness, but that infused liquor had done the exact opposite.","The moment he drank it, not only had his entire body filled with strength, but even his mind had felt clearer.","How incredible had the taste been, too? The herb’s bittersweet flavor blended perfectly with the alcohol, giving it an exceptionally clean finish.","He could confidently say it was so good that merely imagining it made his mouth water.","\"Apparently that human needs shoes this time. He’s already stranded somewhere dangerous, so he needs a pair with really good performance.\"","\"Did he say he’d give you booze if you made them?\"","\"Not booze. He said he’d give me an herb. I’ll give it to you if you want.\"","\"Ooh! I’ll make them right away!\"","The dwarves were actually thinking of a fully matured mandrake as nothing more than an ingredient for infused liquor.","If Grylls had heard this conversation, he would have been appalled, but ultimately would have let it slide as long as they made the shoes properly.","But if anyone else had witnessed this scene?","They would have been foaming at the mouth at the thought of someone treating a fully matured mandrake as a mere ingredient for infused liquor.","But the most important thing in a dwarf’s life was alcohol.","It might look like a humble pleasure to others, but to them, that was happiness.","\"By the way, what’s that herb called? It was bright red and definitely looked medicinal.\"","\"They said it’s a fully matured mandrake, but I don’t really know. Just think of it as a mandrake.\"","\"Hmm. Mandrake-infused liquor is already delicious, so I guess this one’s even better?\"","\"Probably? I heard you could make a single top-grade elixir with one of those.\"","\"Really? Then isn’t it insanely expensive?\"","Wagner was puzzled.","Elixirs were extremely expensive items.","To dwarves, alcohol itself might as well be an elixir, but an elixir was still an elixir.","He wasn’t particularly interested in such things, so the value didn’t fully register with him, but he couldn’t help wondering about it.","\"Hic! It’s really expensive. But think about it.\"","\"Think about what?\"","\"It’s infused liquor made from an ingredient for a top-grade elixir. How could you possibly resist that? It’s way more worthwhile than selling it and using the money to drink ordinary beer.\"","\"Oh. I wasn’t thinking far enough ahead. You’re a genius, as expected.\"","\"You’re too kind. Hic!\"","One might say the two were perfectly happy encouraging each other’s nonsense, but that was simply how dwarves were.","A race that loved alcohol so much it was practically part of their bodies.","A race with a longer natural life expectancy than humans, yet a similar average lifespan because of liver disease.","A race for whom it was virtually impossible to find a single example of someone who didn’t drink.","Those were dwarves.","Ordering them to give up alcohol was practically the same as sentencing them to death.","\"But this... is trickier than I thought.\"","Wagner studied the paper Gareth had given him.","Gareth apparently agreed, because he nodded.","\"That’s why I came to you. I know metal, but I’m hopeless with leather.\"","\"True, but... shoes that are sturdy as a baseline and waterproof on top of that? Slip resistance too? You’ve basically crammed every performance feature imaginable into these.\"","Being dwarves didn’t mean they were masters of every craft.","Each dwarf had their own specialty.","Gareth’s specialty was metallurgy, while Wagner’s was leatherworking.","\"We’ll have to start with high-quality materials. You said this human is stranded somewhere, right?\"","\"Yeah.\"","\"Then durability has to be high too. If I do it like this...\"","Wagner picked up a pen and began sketching out a rough design.","As expected of a dwarven master leatherworker, even his rough concept looked sophisticated.","\"There’s no avoiding the extra weight if we make them this way. Tell him he’ll have to accept that.\"","\"Got it. I’m sure he’ll understand that much.\"","\"But where the hell did this stranded human end up that he’s willing to give you a fully matured mandrake?\"","\"He said he got stranded in the Forest of Four Seasons. I don’t really know much about it either.\"","\"Tsk, tsk. Of all places, he had to end up there.\"","Wagner had heard of the Forest of Four Seasons before.","A forest that was a labyrinth in and of itself, one from which no one could ever escape once they entered.","Having custom-made shoes probably wouldn’t increase the man’s chances of survival by much.","But even increasing those odds a little would be enough.","\"Finished estimating everything yet? Hic! So how long will it take?\"","\"I’ve already got suitable materials, so about a week should—\"","\"Hey. Look at this.\"","Gareth cut Wagner off and headed somewhere.","Wagner watched him curiously, but when Gareth soon returned carrying something, his eyes widened.","\"Th-That’s...!\"","It was a uniquely shaped glass bottle of the sort one might see in the Central Plains.","Its middle was narrow while its upper portion widened outward.","Inside it was a plant with something resembling a human face, its mouth stretched wide open.","And as if that weren’t enough, the container was filled to the brim with red liquid.","It was the infused liquor Gareth had made using the fully matured mandrake.","\"Hic! If you shorten the deadline, you can drink all of this.\"","\"A-Ahem. Then three days...\"","\"Plus the crab he’ll be sending tomorrow as a drinking snack. He said he’d give me some.\"","At those words, Wagner’s expression turned serious as he raised one index finger.","\"One day.\"","What dwarves needed wasn’t more money.","Liquor made from rare ingredients.","That was all they needed.","\"Good. Then we’ll drink this after you’re completely finished. If you half-ass the shoes, the deal’s off. Keep that in mind.\"","\"Who do you take me for? Just wait. I’ll make you a damn spectacular pair of shoes.\"","\"Good. I’m counting on you.\"","Wagner disappeared into his workshop for a while to begin making the shoes.","Gareth didn’t return home.","He didn’t mind staying behind as both a supervisor and drinking companion.","’He said it’s the Forest of Four Seasons, so there must be herbs even better than a fully matured mandrake there, right?’","He stared at the fully matured mandrake liquor.","Just one glass was enough to make strength surge throughout his entire body.","Perhaps there were even better ingredients out there.","And if he made liquor with one of those?","His mouth watered just imagining it.","’It doesn’t even have to be booze. A good drinking snack would be enough.’","The fully matured mandrake was one thing, but he was looking forward to the snacks too.","Hadn’t Grylls caught a huge fish yesterday and then a crab today?","Mountain was a country surrounded by mountains, so its people had little opportunity to come into contact with the sea.","Naturally, seafood was expensive, and the best option was usually to obtain it through the Gallery auction house.","But even that wasn’t particularly appealing because of the notoriously brutal transaction fees.","’Should I see what he’s doing right now?’","Recently, Gareth had started enjoying his interactions with Grylls.","Hadn’t the small favor he’d done for him unexpectedly been repaid with a fully matured mandrake?","Even without the mandrake, though, it was entertaining.","[Honestly, demons make better booze these days. Agree?]","\"This bastard?\"","But there was one thing Gareth could never ignore: bait.","He immediately opened the post.","By the time he entered, countless users had already gathered and were fiercely arguing back and forth.","A particularly large number of users were throwing fits, and it wasn’t difficult to guess that most of them were dwarves.","Dwarves could tolerate people making fun of them for being short or whatever else.","That was simply a racial characteristic, so there was nothing they could do about it.","But anything involving alcohol—especially brewed alcohol—was absolutely intolerable.","It was basically their berserk button.","The topic resurfaced on the Gallery whenever people got bored.","└ Let’s be real, demons do make tastier booze. Demons were the first ones to invent refrigeration and freezing magic too~","└ Passing Dwarf) Dwarves were the ones who integrated that magic into machinery. Get your facts straight.","└ Yeah, sure~ But without demons, you couldn’t even make refrigerators~","└ Dwarven booze is honestly just bitter. Demon booze is sweet and actually tastes good lol","└ Don’t you guys miss out on the fun of having a beer while watching sports? lololol","Eventually, Gareth could no longer contain his anger and slammed his fist hard against the table.","Just another peaceful day on the Gallery.","***","\"Why is this guy throwing another fit?\"","Grylls had polished off three crabs in no time with his animal companions.","Now he was resting while browsing the Gallery.","As he browsed, he noticed a post with an unusually large number of comments. When he opened it, he found a full-blown shitshow underway.","The argument was about how alcohol made by demons tasted better than alcohol made by dwarves.","’Is it like saying Chinese-made kimchi tastes better than the kimchi we make at home?’","If that was the case, he could understand why they were so angry."]}]);
